a, or for one who indulges in sex with the wife of his guru or another superior. It is also the best method of atonement for on
e who murders women, the king or his father, for one who slaughters cows, and for all other sinful men. Simply by chanting the holy name of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, such sinful persons may attract the attention of the Supreme Lord, who therefore considers, "Because this man has chanted My holy name, My duty is to give him protection."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.11 - By following the Vedic ritualistic ceremonies or undergoing atonement, sinful men do not become as purified as by chanting once the holy name of Lord Hari. Although ritualisti
c atonement may free one from sinful reactions, it does not awaken devotional service, unlike the chanting of the Lord's names, which reminds one of the Lord's fame, qualities, attributes, pastimes and paraphernalia.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.12 - The ritualistic ceremonies
 of atonement recommended in the religious scriptures are insufficient to cleanse the heart absolutely because after atonement one's mind again runs toward material activities. Consequently, for one who wants liberation from the fruitive reactions of mate
rial activities, the chanting of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba mantra, or glorification of the name, fame and pastimes of the Lord, is recommended as the most perfect process of atonement because such chanting eradicates the dirt from one's heart completely.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.13 - At the time of death, this Aj\'e4mila helplessly and very loudly chanted the holy name of the Lord, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a. That chanting alone has already freed him from the reactions of all sinful life. Therefore, O servants of Yamar\'e4ja, do not try to take him to your master for punishment in hellish conditions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.14 - One who chants the holy name of the Lord is immediately freed from the reactions of unlimited sins, even if he chants indirectly [to indicate something else], jokingly, for musical entertainment, or e
ven neglectfully. This is accepted by all the learned scholars of the scriptures.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.15 - If one chants the holy name of Hari and then dies because of an accidental misfortune, such as falling from the top of a house, slipping and suffering broken bon
es while traveling on the road, being bitten by a serpent, being afflicted with pain and high fever, or being injured by a weapon, one is immediately absolved from having to enter hellish life, even though he is sinful.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.16 - Authorities who are lea
rned scholars and sages have carefully ascertained that one should atone for the heaviest sins by undergoing a heavy process of atonement and one should atone for lighter sins by undergoing lighter atonement. Chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a mantra, however, vanquishes all the effects of sinful activities, regardless of whether heavy or light.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.17 - Although one may neutralize the reactions of sinful life through austerity, charity, vows and other such methods, these pious activities cannot uproot the materia
l desires in one's heart. However, if one serves the lotus feet of the Personality of Godhead, he is immediately freed from all such contaminations.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.18 - As a fire burns dry grass to ashes, so the holy name of the Lord, whether chanted knowingly or unknowingly, burns to ashes, without fail, all the reactions of one's sinful activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.19 - If a person unaware of the effective potency of a certain medicine takes that medicine or is forced to take it, it will act even without his knowledge be
cause its potency does not depend on the patient's understanding. Similarly, even though one does not know the value of chanting the holy name of the Lord, if one chants knowingly or unknowingly, the chanting will be very effective.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.20 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear King, having thus perfectly judged the principles of devotional service with reasoning and arguments, the order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu released the br\'e4hma
\'eba Aj\'e4mila from the bondage of the Yamad\'fctas and saved him from imminent death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.21 - My dear Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, O subduer of all enemies, after the servants of Yamar\'e4ja had been answered by the order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, they went to Yamar\'e4
ja and explained to him everything that had happened.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.22 - Having been released from the nooses of Yamar\'e4ja's servants, the br\'e4hma\'eba Aj\'e4mila, now free from fear, came to his senses and immediately offered obeisances to the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fc
tas by bowing his head at their lotus feet. He was extremely pleased by their presence, for he had seen them save his life from the hands of the servants of Yamar\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.23 - O sinless Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, the order carriers of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, saw that Aj\'e4mila was attempting to say something, and thus they sudd
enly disappeared from his presence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.24-25 - After hearing the discourses between the Yamad\'fctas and the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, Aj\'e4
mila could understand the religious principles that act under the three modes of material nature. These principles are mentioned i
n the three Vedas. He could also understand the transcendental religious principles, which are above the modes of material nature and which concern the relationship between the living being and the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Furthermore, Aj\'e4
mila heard glorification of the name, fame, qualities and pastimes of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He thus became a perfectly pure devotee. He could then remember his past sinful activities, which he greatly regretted having performed.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.26 - Aj\'e4mila said: Alas, being a servant of my senses, how degraded I became! I fell down from my position as a duly qualified br\'e4hma\'eba and begot children in the womb of a prostitute.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.27 - Alas, all condemnation upon me! I acted so sinfully that I degraded my fam
ily tradition. Indeed, I gave up my chaste and beautiful young wife to have sexual intercourse with a fallen prostitute accustomed to drinking wine. All condemnation upon me!
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.28 - My father and mother were old and had no other son or friend to look
 after them. Because I did not take care of them, they lived with great difficulty. Alas, like an abominable lower-class man, I ungratefully left them in that condition.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.29 - It is now clear that as a consequence of such activities, a sinful person like me must be thrown into hellish conditions meant for those who have broken religious principles and must there suffer extreme miseries.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.30 - Was this a dream I saw, or was it reality? I saw fearsome men with ropes in their hands coming to arrest me and drag me away. Where have they gone?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.31 - And where have those four liberated and very beautiful persons gone who released me from arrest and saved me from being dragged down to the hellish regions?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.32 - I am certainly most abomina
ble and unfortunate to have merged in an ocean of sinful activities, but nevertheless, because of my previous spiritual activities, I could see those four exalted personalities who came to rescue me. Now I feel exceedingly happy because of their visit.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.33 - Were it not for my past devotional service, how could I, a most unclean keeper of a prostitute, have gotten an opportunity to chant the holy name of Vaiku\'eb\'f6
hapati when I was just ready to die? Certainly it could not have been possible.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.34 - Aj\'e4mila continued: I am a shameless cheater who has killed his brahminical culture. Indeed, I am sin personified. Where am I in comparison to the all-auspicious chanting of the holy name of Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba?

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.35 - I am such a sinful person, but sinc
e I have now gotten this opportunity, I must completely control my mind, life and senses and always engage in devotional service so that I may not fall again into the deep darkness and ignorance of material life.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.36-37 - Because of identifying ones
elf with the body, one is subjected to desires for sense gratification, and thus one engages in many different types of pious and impious action. This is what constitutes material bondage. Now I shall disentangle myself from my material bondage, which has
 
been caused by the Supreme Personality of Godhead's illusory energy in the form of a woman. Being a most fallen soul, I was victimized by the illusory energy and have become like a dancing dog led around by a woman's hand. Now I shall give up all lusty de
sires and free myself from this illusion. I shall become a merciful, well-wishing friend to all living entities and always absorb myself in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.38 - Simply because I chanted the holy name of the Lord in the association of devotees, 
my heart is now becoming purified. Therefore I shall not fall victim again to the false lures of material sense gratification. Now that I have become fixed in the Absolute Truth, henceforward I shall not identify myself with the body. I shall give up fals
e conceptions of "I" and "mine" and fix my mind on the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.39 - Because of a moment's association with devotees [the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas], Aj\'e4mila detached himself from the material conception of life with determination. Thus freed from all 
material attraction, he immediately started for Hardwar.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.40 - In Hardwar, Aj\'e4mila took shelter at a Vi\'f1\'ebu temple, where he executed the process of bhakti-yoga. He controlled his senses and fully applied his mind in the service of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.41 - Aj\'e4mila fully engaged in devotional service. Thus he detached his mind from the process of sense gratification and became fully absorbed in thinking of the form of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.42 - When his intelligence and mind were fixed upon the form of the Lord, the br\'e4hma\'eba Aj\'e4
mila once again saw before him four celestial persons. He could understand that they were those he had seen previously, and thus he offered them his obeisances by bowing down before them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.43 - Upon seeing the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, Aj\'e4mila gave up his material body at Hardwar on the bank of the Ganges. He regained his original spiritual body, which was a body appropriate for an associate of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.44 - Accompanied by the order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, Aj\'e4mila boarded an airplane made of gold. Passing through the airways, he went directly to the abode of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, the husband of the goddess of fortune.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.45 - Aj\'e4mila was a br\'e4hma\'eba who because of bad association had given up all brahminical culture and religious principles.
 Becoming most fallen, he stole, drank and performed other abominable acts. He even kept a prostitute. Thus he was destined to be carried away to hell by the order carriers of Yamar\'e4
ja, but he was immediately rescued simply by a glimpse of the chanting of the holy name N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.46 - Therefore one who desires freedom from material bondage should adopt the process of chanting and glorifying the name, fame, form and pastimes of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, at whose feet all the holy places stan
d. One cannot derive the proper benefit from other methods, such as pious atonement, speculative knowledge and meditation in mystic yoga, because even after following such methods one takes to fruitive activities again, unable to control his mind, which i
s contaminated by the base qualities of nature, namely passion and ignorance.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.47-48 - Because this very confidential historical narration has the potency to vanquish all sinful reactions, one who hears or describes it with faith and devotion is no l
onger doomed to hellish life, regardless of his having a material body and regardless of how sinful he may have been. Indeed, the Yamad\'fctas, who carry out the orders of Yamar\'e4
ja, do not approach him even to see him. After giving up his body, he returns home, back to Godhead, where he is very respectfully received and worshiped.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.49 - While suffering at the time of death, Aj\'e4mila chanted the holy name of the Lord, and although the chanting was directed toward his son, he nevertheless returned home, ba
ck to Godhead. Therefore if one faithfully and inoffensively chants the holy name of the Lord, where is the doubt that he will return to Godhead?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\f35\fs28\cf2\insrsid10252087 Aj\'e4mila Delivered by the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas
