\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: My dear King, the servants of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu are always very expert in logic 
and arguments. After hearing the statements of the Yamad\'fctas, they replied as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.2 - The Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas said: Alas, how painful it is that irreligion is being introduced into an assembly where religion should be maintained. Indeed, those in charg
e of maintaining the religious principles are needlessly punishing a sinless, unpunishable person.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.3 - A king or governmental official should be so well qualified that he acts as a father, maintainer and protector of the citizens because of affecti
on and love. He should give the citizens good advice and instructions according to the standard scriptures and should be equal to everyone. Yamar\'e4
ja does this, for he is the supreme master of justice, and so do those who follow in his footsteps. However, i
f such persons become polluted and exhibit partiality by punishing an innocent, blameless person, where will the citizens go to take shelter for their maintenance and security?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.4 - The mass of people follow the example of a leader in society and imitate his behavior. They accept as evidence whatever the leader accepts.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.5-6 - People in general are not very advanced in knowledge by which to discriminate between religion and irreligion. The innocent, unenlightened citizen is like an ignorant an
imal sleeping in peace with its head on the lap of its master, faithfully believing in the master's protection. If a leader is actually kindhearted and deserves to be the object of a living entity's faith, how can he punish or kill a foolish person who ha
s fully surrendered in good faith and friendship?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.7 - Aj\'e4mila has already atoned for all his sinful actions. Indeed, he has atoned not only for sins performed in one life but for those performed in millions of lives, for in a helpless condition he c
hanted the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Even though he did not chant purely, he chanted without offense, and therefore he is now pure and eligible for liberation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.8 - The Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas continued: Even previously, while eating and at other times, this Aj\'e4mila would call his son, saying, "My dear N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, please come here." Although calling the name of his son, he nevertheless uttered the four syllables n\'e4-r\'e4-ya-\'eba. Simply by chanting the name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba in this way, he sufficiently atoned for the sinful rea
ctions of millions of lives.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.9-10 - The chanting of the holy name of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu is the best process of atonement for a thief of gold or other valuables, for a drunkard, for one who betrays a friend or relative, for one who kills a br\'e4hma\'eb
a, or for 
one who indulges in sex with the wife of his guru or another superior. It is also the best method of atonement for one who murders women, the king or his father, for one who slaughters cows, and for all other sinful men. Simply by chanting the holy name o
f Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, such sinful persons may attract the attention of the Supreme Lord, who therefore considers, "Because this man has chanted My holy name, My duty is to give him protection."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.11 - By following the Vedic ritualistic ceremonies or undergoin
g atonement, sinful men do not become as purified as by chanting once the holy name of Lord Hari. Although ritualistic atonement may free one from sinful reactions, it does not awaken devotional service, unlike the chanting of the Lord's names, which remi
nds one of the Lord's fame, qualities, attributes, pastimes and paraphernalia.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.12 - The ritualistic ceremonies of atonement recommended in the religious scriptures are insufficient to cleanse the heart absolutely because after atonement one's mind a
gain runs toward material activities. Consequently, for one who wants liberation from the fruitive reactions of material activities, the chanting of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a mantra, or glorification of the name, fame and pastimes of the Lord, is recommended as the most perfect process of atonement because such chanting eradicates the dirt from one's heart completely.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.13 - At the time of death, this Aj\'e4mila helplessly and very loudly chanted the holy name of the Lord, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. That chanting alone has already 
freed him from the reactions of all sinful life. Therefore, O servants of Yamar\'e4ja, do not try to take him to your master for punishment in hellish conditions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.14 - One who chants the holy name of the Lord is immediately freed from the reactions of
 unlimited sins, even if he chants indirectly [to indicate something else], jokingly, for musical entertainment, or even neglectfully. This is accepted by all the learned scholars of the scriptures.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.15 - If one chants the holy name of Hari and then
 dies because of an accidental misfortune, such as falling from the top of a house, slipping and suffering broken bones while traveling on the road, being bitten by a serpent, being afflicted with pain and high fever, or being injured by a weapon, one is 
immediately absolved from having to enter hellish life, even though he is sinful.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.16 - Authorities who are learned scholars and sages have carefully ascertained that one should atone for the heaviest sins by undergoing a heavy process of atonement a
nd one should atone for lighter sins by undergoing lighter atonement. Chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba mantra, however, vanquishes all the effects of sinful activities, regardless of whether heavy or light.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.17 - Although one may neutralize the reactions of 
sinful life through austerity, charity, vows and other such methods, these pious activities cannot uproot the material desires in one's heart. However, if one serves the lotus feet of the Personality of Godhead, he is immediately freed from all such conta
minations.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.18 - As a fire burns dry grass to ashes, so the holy name of the Lord, whether chanted knowingly or unknowingly, burns to ashes, without fail, all the reactions of one's sinful activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.19 - If a person unaware of the effective
 potency of a certain medicine takes that medicine or is forced to take it, it will act even without his knowledge because its potency does not depend on the patient's understanding. Similarly, even though one does not know the value of chanting the holy 
name of the Lord, if one chants knowingly or unknowingly, the chanting will be very effective.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.20 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear King, having thus perfectly judged the principles of devotional service with reasoning and arguments, the order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu released the br\'e4hma
\'eba Aj\'e4mila from the bondage of the Yamad\'fctas and saved him from imminent death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.21 - My dear Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, O subduer of all enemies, after the servants of Yamar\'e4ja had been answered by the order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, they went to Yamar\'e4
ja and explained to him everything that had happened.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.22 - Having been released from the nooses of Yamar\'e4ja's servants, the br\'e4hma\'eba Aj\'e4mila, now free from fear, came to his senses and immediately offered obeisances to the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fc
tas by bowing his head at their lotus feet. He was extremely pleased by their presence, for he had seen them save his life from the hands of the servants of Yamar\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.23 - O sinless Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, the order carriers of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, saw that Aj\'e4
mila was attempting to say something, and thus they suddenly disappeared from his presence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.24-25 - After hearing the discourses between the Yamad\'fctas and the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, Aj\'e4mila could un
derstand the religious principles that act under the three modes of material nature. These principles are mentioned in the three Vedas. He could also understand the transcendental religious principles, which are above the modes of material nature and whic
h concern the relationship between the living being and the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Furthermore, Aj\'e4
mila heard glorification of the name, fame, qualities and pastimes of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He thus became a perfectly pure devotee. He could then remember his past sinful activities, which he greatly regretted having performed.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.26 - Aj\'e4mila said: Alas, being a servant of my senses, how degraded I became! I fell down from my position as a duly qualified br\'e4hma\'eba and begot children in the womb of a prostitute.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.27 - Alas, all condemnation upon me! I acted so sinfully that I degraded my family tradition. Indeed, I gave up my chaste and beautiful young wife to have sexual intercourse with a fallen prostitute accustomed to drink
ing wine. All condemnation upon me!
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.28 - My father and mother were old and had no other son or friend to look after them. Because I did not take care of them, they lived with great difficulty. Alas, like an abominable lower-class man, I ungratefull
y left them in that condition.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.29 - It is now clear that as a consequence of such activities, a sinful person like me must be thrown into hellish conditions meant for those who have broken religious principles and must there suffer extreme miseries.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.30 - Was this a dream I saw, or was it reality? I saw fearsome men with ropes in their hands coming to arrest me and drag me away. Where have they gone?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.31 - And where have those four liberated and very beautiful persons gone who released me from arrest and saved me from being dragged down to the hellish regions?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.32 - I am certainly most abominable and unfortunate to have merged in an ocean of sinful activities, but nevertheless, because of my previous spiritual activities, I could
 see those four exalted personalities who came to rescue me. Now I feel exceedingly happy because of their visit.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.33 - Were it not for my past devotional service, how could I, a most unclean keeper of a prostitute, have gotten an opportunity to chant the holy name of Vaiku\'eb\'f6
hapati when I was just ready to die? Certainly it could not have been possible.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.34 - Aj\'e4mila continued: I am a shameless cheater who has killed his brahminical culture. Indeed, I am sin personified. Where am I in comparison to the all-auspicious chanting of the holy name of Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba?

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.35 - I am such a sinful person, but since I have now gotten this opportunity, I must completely control my mind, life and senses and always engage in devotional service so that I 
may not fall again into the deep darkness and ignorance of material life.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.36-37 - Because of identifying oneself with the body, one is subjected to desires for sense gratification, and thus one engages in many different types of pious and impious a
ction. This is what constitutes material bondage. Now I shall disentangle myself from my material bondage, which has been caused by the Supreme Personality of Godhead's illusory energy in the form of a woman. Being a most fallen soul, I was victimized by 
t
he illusory energy and have become like a dancing dog led around by a woman's hand. Now I shall give up all lusty desires and free myself from this illusion. I shall become a merciful, well-wishing friend to all living entities and always absorb myself in
 K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.2.38 - Simply because I chanted the holy name of the Lord in the association of devotees, my heart is now becoming purified. Therefore I shall not fall victim again to the false lures of material sense gratification. Now that I h
ave become fixed in the Absolute Truth, henceforward I shall not identify myself with the body. I shall give up false conceptions of "I" and "mine" and fix my mind on the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.39 - Because of a moment's association with devotees [the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas], Aj\'e4
mila detached himself from the material conception of life with determination. Thus freed from all material attraction, he immediately started for Hardwar.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.40 - In Hardwar, Aj\'e4mila took shelter at a Vi\'f1\'ebu temple, where he executed the process of bhakti-yoga. He controlled his senses and fully applied his mind in the service of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.41 - Aj\'e4mila fully engaged in devotional service. Thus he detached his mind from the process of sense gratification and became fully absorbed in thinking of the form of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.42 - When his intelligence and mind were fixed upon the form of the Lord, the br\'e4hma\'eba Aj\'e4mila once again saw before him four celestial persons. He could understand that they were those he had seen previously
, and thus he offered them his obeisances by bowing down before them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.43 - Upon seeing the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, Aj\'e4mila gave up his material body at Hardwar on the bank of the Ganges. He regained his original spiritual body, which was a body appropriate for an associate of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.44 - Accompanied by the order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, Aj\'e4mila boarded an airplane made of gold. Passing through the airways, he went directly to the abode of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, the husband of the goddess of fortune.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.45 - Aj\'e4mila was a br\'e4hma\'eb
a who because of bad association had given up all brahminical culture and religious principles. Becoming most fallen, he stole, drank and performed other abominable acts. He even kept a prostitute. Thus he was destined to be carried a
way to hell by the order carriers of Yamar\'e4ja, but he was immediately rescued simply by a glimpse of the chanting of the holy name N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.46 - Therefore one who desires freedom from material bondage should adopt the process of chanting and glori
fying the name, fame, form and pastimes of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, at whose feet all the holy places stand. One cannot derive the proper benefit from other methods, such as pious atonement, speculative knowledge and meditation in mystic yoga, 
because even after following such methods one takes to fruitive activities again, unable to control his mind, which is contaminated by the base qualities of nature, namely passion and ignorance.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.47-48 - Because this very confidential historical narr
ation has the potency to vanquish all sinful reactions, one who hears or describes it with faith and devotion is no longer doomed to hellish life, regardless of his having a material body and regardless of how sinful he may have been. Indeed, the Yamad
\'fctas, who carry out the orders of Yamar\'e4ja, do not approach him even to see him. After giving up his body, he returns home, back to Godhead, where he is very respectfully received and worshiped.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.2.49 - While suffering at the time of death, Aj\'e4mila chante
d the holy name of the Lord, and although the chanting was directed toward his son, he nevertheless returned home, back to Godhead. Therefore if one faithfully and inoffensively chants the holy name of the Lord, where is the doubt that he will return to G
odhead?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Translations 1-49
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0\pararsid10252087 \shading10000\cfpat16 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.1 - King Par\'e9k\'f1it said: O my lord, O \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, Yamar\'e4
ja is the controller of all living entities in terms of their religious and irreligious activities, but his order had been foiled. When his servants, the Yamad\'fctas, informed him of their defeat by the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fc
tas, who had stopped them from arresting Aj\'e4mila, what did he reply?
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.2 - O great sage, never before has it been heard anywhere that an order from Yamar\'e4ja has been baffled. Therefore I think that people will have doubt
s about this that no one but you can eradicate. Since that is my firm conviction, kindly explain the reasons for these events.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.3 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 replied: My dear King, when the order carriers of Yamar\'e4ja were baffled and defeated by the order carriers of Vi\'f1\'ebu, they approached their master, the controller of Sa\'e0yaman
\'e9-pur\'e9 and master of sinful persons, to tell him of this incident.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.4 - The Yamad\'fctas said: Our dear lord, how many controllers or rulers are there in this material world? 
How many causes are responsible for manifesting the various results of activities performed under the three modes of material nature [sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba and tamo-gu\'eba]?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.5 - If in this universe there are many rulers and justices who disagree abo
ut punishment and reward, their contradictory actions will neutralize each other, and no one will be punished or rewarded. Otherwise, if their contradictory acts fail to neutralize each other, everyone will have to be both punished and rewarded.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.6 - The Yamad\'fctas continued: Since there are many different karm\'e9
s, or workers, there may be different judges or rulers to give them justice, but just as one central emperor controls different departmental rulers, there must be one supreme controller to guide all the judges.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.3.7 - The supreme judge must be one, not many. It was our understanding that you are that supreme judge and that you have jurisdiction even over the demigods. Our impression was that you are the master of all living entities, the su
preme authority who discriminates between the pious and impious activities of all human beings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.8 - But now we see that the punishment ordained under your authority is no longer effective, since your order has been transgressed by four wonderful and perfect persons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.9 - We were bringing the most sinful Aj\'e4mila toward the hellish planets, following your order, when those beautiful persons from Siddhaloka forcibly cut the knots of the ropes with which we were arresting him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.10 - As soon as the sinful Aj\'e4mila uttered the name N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, these four beautiful men immediately arrived and reassured him, saying, "Do not fear. Do not fear." We wish to know about them from Your Lordship. If you think we are able to understand them, kindly describe who they are.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.11 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Thus having been questioned, Lord Yamar\'e4
ja, the supreme controller of the living entities, was very pleased with his order carriers because of hearing from them the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. He remembered the lotus feet of the Lord and began to reply.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.12 - Yamar\'e4ja said: My dear servants, you have accepted me as the Supreme, but factually I am not. Above me, and above all the other demigods, including Indra and Candra, is the one supreme master a
nd controller. The partial manifestations of His personality are Brahm\'e4, Vi\'f1\'ebu and \'c7
iva, who are in charge of the creation, maintenance and annihilation of this universe. He is like the two threads that form the length and breadth of a woven cloth. The entire world is controlled by Him just as a bull is controlled by a rope in its nose.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.13 - Just as the driver of a bullock cart ties ropes through the nostrils of his bulls to control them, the Supreme Personality of Godhead binds all men through the 
ropes of His words in the Vedas, which set forth the names and activities of the distinct orders of human society [br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya and \'e7\'fc
dra]. In fear, the members of these orders all worship the Supreme Lord by offering Him presentations according to their respective activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.14-15 - I, Yamar\'e4ja; Indra, the King of heaven; Nir\'e5ti; Varu\'eba; Candra, the moon-god; Agni; Lord \'c7iva; Pavana; Lord Brahm\'e4; S\'fcrya, the sun-god; Vi\'e7v\'e4su; the eight Vasus; the S\'e4
dhyas; the Maruts; the Rudras; the Siddhas; and Mar\'e9ci and the other great \'e5\'f1is engaged in maintaining the departmental affairs of the universe, as well as the best of the demigods headed by B\'e5haspati, and the great sages headed by Bh\'e5
gu are all certainly freed from the influence of the two 
base material modes of nature, namely passion and ignorance. Nevertheless, although we are in the mode of goodness, we cannot understand the activities of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. What, then, is to be said of others, who, under illusion, merely
 speculate to know God?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.16 - As the different limbs of the body cannot see the eyes, the living entities cannot see the Supreme Lord, who is situated as the Supersoul in everyone's heart. Not by the senses, by the mind, by the life air, by thoughts 
within the heart, or by the vibration of words can the living entities ascertain the real situation of the Supreme Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.17 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is self-sufficient and fully independent. He is the master of everyone and everything, 
including the illusory energy. He has His form, qualities and features; and similarly His order carriers, the Vai\'f1\'eb
avas, who are very beautiful, possess bodily features, transcendental qualities and a transcendental nature almost like His. They always wander within this world with full independence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.18 - The order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who are worshiped even by the demigods, possess wonderful bodily features exactly like those of Vi\'f1\'ebu and are very rarely seen. The Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas protect the devotees 
of the Lord from the hands of enemies, from envious persons and even from my jurisdiction, as well as from natural disturbances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.19 - Real religious principles are enacted by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Although fully situated in the mode of goodness, even the great \'e5\'f1
is who occupy the topmost planets cannot ascertain the real religious principles, nor can the demigods or the leaders of Siddhaloka, to say nothing of the asuras, ordinary human beings, Vidy\'e4dharas and C\'e4ra\'ebas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.20-21 - Lord Brahm\'e4, Bhagav\'e4n N\'e4rada, Lord \'c7iva, the four Kum\'e4ras, Lord Kapila [the son of Devah\'fcti], Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Janaka Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Grandfather Bh\'e9\'f1
ma, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 and I myself know the real religious principle. My dear servants, this transcendental religious principle, which is known as bh\'e4
gavata-dharma, or surrender unto the Supreme Lord and love for Him, is uncontaminated by the material modes of nature. It is very confidential and difficult for ordinary human beings t
o understand, but if by chance one fortunately understands it, he is immediately liberated, and thus he returns home, back to Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.22 - Devotional service, beginning with the chanting of the holy name of the Lord, is the ultimate religious principle for the living entity in human society.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.23 - My dear servants, who are as good as my sons, just see how glorious is the chanting of the holy name of the Lord. The greatly sinful Aj\'e4mila chanted only to call his son, not knowing that he was ch
anting the Lord's holy name. Nevertheless, by chanting the holy name of the Lord, he remembered N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, and thus he was immediately saved from the ropes of death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.24 - Therefore it should be understood that one is easily relieved from all sinful 
reactions by chanting the holy name of the Lord and chanting of His qualities and activities. This is the only process recommended for relief from sinful reactions. Even if one chants the holy name of the Lord with improper pronunciation, he will achieve 
relief from material bondage if he chants without offenses. Aj\'e4mila, for example, was extremely sinful, but while dying he merely chanted the holy name, and although calling his son, he achieved complete liberation because he remembered the name of N
\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.25 - Because they are bewildered by the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Y\'e4j\'ef
avalkya and Jaimini and other compilers of the religious scriptures cannot know the secret, confidential religious system of the twelve mah\'e4janas. They cannot understand the transcendental value of performing devotional service or chanting the Hare K
\'e5\'f1\'eba mantra. Because their minds are attracted to the ritualistic ceremonies mentioned in the Vedas-especially the Yajur Veda, S\'e4ma Veda and \'c5g Veda-thei
r intelligence has become dull. Thus they are busy collecting the ingredients for ritualistic ceremonies that yield only temporary benefits, such as elevation to Svargaloka for material happiness. They are not attracted to the sa\'eck\'e9
rtana movement; instead, they are interested in dharma, artha, k\'e4ma and mok\'f1a.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.26 - Considering all these points, therefore, intelligent men decide to solve all problems by adopting the devotional service of chanting the holy name of the Lord, who is situated in everyone'
s heart and who is a mine of all auspicious qualities. Such persons are not within my jurisdiction for punishment. Generally they never commit sinful activities, but even if by mistake or because of bewilderment or illusion they sometimes commit sinful ac
ts, they are protected from sinful reactions because they always chant the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba mantra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.27 - My dear servants, please do not approach such devotees, for they have fully surrendered to the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. They 
are equal to everyone, and their narrations are sung by the demigods and the inhabitants of Siddhaloka. Please do not even go near them. They are always protected by the club of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and therefore Lord Brahm\'e4
 and I and even the time factor are not competent to chastise them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.28 - Paramaha\'e0sas are exalted persons who have no taste for material enjoyment and who drink the honey of the Lord's lotus feet. My dear servants, bring to me for punishment only persons who are av
erse to the taste of that honey, who do not associate with paramaha\'e0sas and who are attached to family life and worldly enjoyment, which form the path to hell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.29 - My dear servants, please bring to me only those sinful persons who do not use their tongues to chant the holy name and qualities of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, whose hearts do not remember the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a even once, and whose heads do not bow down even once before Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Send me those who do not perform their duties toward Vi\'f1\'ebu, which are the only duties in human life. Please bring me all such fools and rascals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.30 - [Then Yamar\'e4ja, considering himself and his servants to be offenders, spoke as follows, begging pardon from the Lord.] O my Lord, my servants have surely committed a great offense by arresting a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava such as Aj\'e4mila. O N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, O supreme and oldest person, please forgive us. Because of our ignorance, we failed to recognize Aj\'e4mila as a servant of Your Lordship, and thus we have certainly committed a great offense. Theref
ore with folded hands we beg Your pardon. My Lord, since You are supremely merciful and are always full of good qualities, please pardon us. We offer our respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.31 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear King, the chanting of the holy name of the Lord is able to uproot even the reactions of the greatest sins. Therefore the chanting of the sa\'eck\'e9
rtana movement is the most auspicious activity in the entire universe. Please try to understand this so that others will take it seriously.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.3.32 - One who constantly hears and chants the holy name of the Lord and hears and chants about His activities can very easily attain the platform of pure devotional service, which can cleanse the dirt from one's heart. One cannot achieve such p
urification merely by observing vows and performing Vedic ritualistic ceremonies.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.33 - Devotees who always lick the honey from the lotus feet of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba do not care at all for material activities, which are performed under the three modes of mat
erial nature and which bring only misery. Indeed, devotees never give up the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a to return to material activities. Others, however, who are addicted to Vedic rituals because they have neglected the service of the Lord's lotus feet and are e
nchanted by lusty desires, sometimes perform acts of atonement. Nevertheless, being incompletely purified, they return to sinful activities again and again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.34 - After hearing from the mouth of their master about the extraordinary glories of the Lord and His name, fame and attributes, the Yamad\'fc
tas were struck with wonder. Since then, as soon as they see a devotee, they fear him and dare not look at him again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.35 - When the great sage Agastya, the son of Kumbha, was residing in the Malaya Hills and worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, I approached him, and he explained to me this confidential history.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  3. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
