\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.9 - We were bringing the most sinful Aj\'e4mila toward the hellish planets, following your order, when those beautiful persons from Siddhaloka forcibly cut the knots of the ropes with which we were arresting him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.10 - As soon as the sinful Aj\'e4mila uttered the name N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, these four beautiful men immediately arrived and reassured him, saying, "Do not fear. Do 
not fear." We wish to know about them from Your Lordship. If you think we are able to understand them, kindly describe who they are.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.11 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Thus having been questioned, Lord Yamar\'e4ja, the supreme controller of the living en
tities, was very pleased with his order carriers because of hearing from them the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. He remembered the lotus feet of the Lord and began to reply.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.12 - Yamar\'e4ja said: My dear servants, you have accepted me as the Supreme, but fac
tually I am not. Above me, and above all the other demigods, including Indra and Candra, is the one supreme master and controller. The partial manifestations of His personality are Brahm\'e4, Vi\'f1\'ebu and \'c7
iva, who are in charge of the creation, maintenance and annihilation of this universe. He is like the two threads that form the length and breadth of a woven cloth. The entire world is controlled by Him just as a bull is controlled by a rope in its nose.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.13 - Just as the driver of a bullock cart ties ro
pes through the nostrils of his bulls to control them, the Supreme Personality of Godhead binds all men through the ropes of His words in the Vedas, which set forth the names and activities of the distinct orders of human society [br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1
atriya, vai\'e7ya and \'e7\'fcdra]. In fear, the members of these orders all worship the Supreme Lord by offering Him presentations according to their respective activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.14-15 - I, Yamar\'e4ja; Indra, the King of heaven; Nir\'e5ti; Varu\'eba; Candra, the moon-god; Agni; Lord \'c7iva; Pavana; Lord Brahm\'e4; S\'fcrya, the sun-god; Vi\'e7v\'e4su; the eight Vasus; the S\'e4
dhyas; the Maruts; the Rudras; the Siddhas; and Mar\'e9ci and the other great \'e5\'f1is engaged in maintaining the departmental affairs of the universe, as well as the best of the demigods headed by B\'e5haspati, and the great sages headed by Bh\'e5
gu are all certainly freed from the influence of the two base material modes of nature, namely passion and ignorance. Nevertheless, although we are in the mode of goodness, we cannot understand the
