\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.16 - As the different limbs of the body cannot see the eyes, the living entities cannot see the Supreme Lord,
 who is situated as the Supersoul in everyone's heart. Not by the senses, by the mind, by the life air, by thoughts within the heart, or by the vibration of words can the living entities ascertain the real situation of the Supreme Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.17 - The Su
preme Personality of Godhead is self-sufficient and fully independent. He is the master of everyone and everything, including the illusory energy. He has His form, qualities and features; and similarly His order carriers, the Vai\'f1\'eb
avas, who are very beautiful, possess bodily features, transcendental qualities and a transcendental nature almost like His. They always wander within this world with full independence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.18 - The order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who are worshiped even by the demigods, possess wonderful bodily features exactly like those of Vi\'f1\'ebu and are very rarely seen. The Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fc
tas protect the devotees of the Lord from the hands of enemies, from envious persons and even from my jurisdiction, as well as from natural disturbances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.19 - Real religious principles are enacted by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Although fully situated in the mode of goodness, even the great \'e5\'f1
is who occupy the topmost planets cannot ascertain the real religious principles, nor can the demigods or the leaders of Siddhaloka, to say nothing of the asuras, ordinary human beings, Vidy\'e4dharas and C\'e4ra\'ebas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.20-21 - Lord Brahm\'e4, Bhagav\'e4n N\'e4rada, Lord \'c7iva, the four Kum\'e4ras, Lord Kapila [the son of Devah\'fcti], Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Janaka Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Grandfather Bh\'e9\'f1
ma, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 and I myself know the real religious principle. My dear servants, this transcendental religious principle, which is known as bh\'e4gavata-dharma, or surrender unto the Supreme Lord and love for Him, 
is uncontaminated by the material modes of nature. It is very confidential and difficult for ordinary human beings to understand, but if by chance one fortunately understands it, he is immediately liberated, and thus he returns home, back to Godhead.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.22 - Devotional service, beginning with the chanting of the holy name of the Lord, is the ultimate religious principle for the living entity in human society.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.23 - My dear servants, who are as good as my sons, just see how glorious is the chanting of the holy name of the Lord. The greatly sinful Aj\'e4
mila chanted only to call his son, not knowing that he was chanting the Lord's holy name. Nevertheless, by chanting the holy name of the Lord, he remembered N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, and thus he was immediately saved from the ropes of death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.24 - Therefore it should be understood that one is easily relieved from all sinful reactions by chanting the holy name of the Lord and chanting of His qualities and activities. This is the only process recommended for relie
f from sinful reactions. Even if one chants the holy name of the Lord with improper pronunciation, he will achieve relief from material bondage if he chants without offenses. Aj\'e4
mila, for example, was extremely sinful, but while dying he merely chanted the holy name, and although calling his son, he achieved complete liberation because he remembered the name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.25 - Because they are bewildered by the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Y\'e4j\'efavalkya and Jaimini and other c
ompilers of the religious scriptures cannot know the secret, confidential religious system of the twelve mah\'e4janas. They cannot understand the transcendental value of performing devotional service or chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a mantra. Because their minds are attracted to the ritualistic ceremonies mentioned in the Vedas-especially the Yajur Veda, S\'e4ma Veda and \'c5
g Veda-their intelligence has become dull. Thus they are busy collecting the ingredients for ritualistic ceremonies that yield only temporary benefits, such as elevation to Svargaloka for material happiness. They are not attracted to the sa\'eck\'e9
rtana movement; instead, they are interested in dharma, artha, k\'e4ma and mok\'f1a.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.26 - Considering all these points, therefore, intelligent men decide to solve
 all problems by adopting the devotional service of chanting the holy name of the Lord, who is situated in everyone's heart and who is a mine of all auspicious qualities. Such persons are not within my jurisdiction for punishment. Generally they never com
mit sinful activities, but even if by mistake or because of bewilderment or illusion they sometimes commit sinful acts, they are protected from sinful reactions because they always chant the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba mantra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.27 - My dear servants, please do not ap
proach such devotees, for they have fully surrendered to the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. They are equal to everyone, and their narrations are sung by the demigods and the inhabitants of Siddhaloka. Please do not even go near them. Th
ey are always protected by the club of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and therefore Lord Brahm\'e4 and I and even the time factor are not competent to chastise them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.28 - Paramaha\'e0sas are exalted persons who have no taste for material enjoyment an
d who drink the honey of the Lord's lotus feet. My dear servants, bring to me for punishment only persons who are averse to the taste of that honey, who do not associate with paramaha\'e0
sas and who are attached to family life and worldly enjoyment, which form the path to hell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.29 - My dear servants, please bring to me only those sinful persons who do not use their tongues to chant the holy name and qualities of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, whose hearts do not remember the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a even once, and whose heads do not bow down even once before Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Send me those who do not perform their duties toward Vi\'f1\'ebu, which are the only duties in human life. Please bring me all such fools and rascals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.30 - [Then Yamar\'e4ja, considering himself and his servants to be offenders, spoke as follows, begging pardon from the Lord.] O my Lord, my servants have surely committed a great offense by arresting a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava such as Aj\'e4mila. O N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, O supreme and oldest person, please forgive us. Because of our ignorance, we failed to recognize Aj\'e4
mila as a servant of Your Lordship, and thus we have certainly committed a great offense. Therefore with folded hands we beg Your pardon. My Lord, since You are supremely merciful and are always full of good qualities, please pardon us.
 We offer our respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.31 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear King, the chanting of the holy name of the Lord is able to uproot even the reactions of the greatest sins. Therefore the chanting of the sa\'eck\'e9rtana movement is t
he most auspicious activity in the entire universe. Please try to understand this so that others will take it seriously.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.32 - One who constantly hears and chants the holy name of the Lord and hears and chants about His activities can very easily at
tain the platform of pure devotional service, which can cleanse the dirt from one's heart. One cannot achieve such purification merely by observing vows and performing Vedic ritualistic ceremonies.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.33 - Devotees who always lick the honey from the lotus feet of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a do not care at all for material activities, which are performed under the three modes of material nature and which bring only misery. Indeed, devotees never give up the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eba to return to material activities. Others, h
owever, who are addicted to Vedic rituals because they have neglected the service of the Lord's lotus feet and are enchanted by lusty desires, sometimes perform acts of atonement. Nevertheless, being incompletely purified, they return to sinful activities
 again and again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.34 - After hearing from the mouth of their master about the extraordinary glories of the Lord and His name, fame and attributes, the Yamad\'fc
tas were struck with wonder. Since then, as soon as they see a devotee, they fear him and dare not look at him again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.35 - When the great sage Agastya, the son of Kumbha, was residing in the Malaya Hills and worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, I approached him, and he explained to me this confidential history.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Yamar\'e4ja Instructs His Messengers
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat8 {\fs28\cf2\insrsid10252087   \bullet   }{
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.1 - King Par\'e9k\'f1it said: O my lord, O \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, Yamar\'e4
ja is the controller of all living entities in terms of their religious and irreligious activities, but his order had been foiled. When his servants, the Yamad\'fctas, informed him of their defeat by the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fc
tas, who had stopped them from arresting Aj\'e4mila, what did he reply?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.2 - O great sage, never before has it been heard anywhere that an order from Yamar\'e4ja has been baffled. Therefore I think that people will have doubts about this that no one
 but you can eradicate. Since that is my firm conviction, kindly explain the reasons for these events.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.3 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 replied: My dear King, when the order carriers of Yamar\'e4ja were baffled and defeated by the order carriers of Vi\'f1\'ebu, they approached their master, the controller of Sa\'e0yaman
\'e9-pur\'e9 and master of sinful persons, to tell him of this incident.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.4 - The Yamad\'fctas said: Our dear lord, how many controllers or rulers are there in this material world? How many causes are resp
onsible for manifesting the various results of activities performed under the three modes of material nature [sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba and tamo-gu\'eba]?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.5 - If in this universe there are many rulers and justices who disagree about punishment and reward
, their contradictory actions will neutralize each other, and no one will be punished or rewarded. Otherwise, if their contradictory acts fail to neutralize each other, everyone will have to be both punished and rewarded.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.6 - The Yamad\'fctas continued: Since there are many different karm\'e9
s, or workers, there may be different judges or rulers to give them justice, but just as one central emperor controls different departmental rulers, there must be one supreme controller to guide all the judges.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.
3.7 - The supreme judge must be one, not many. It was our understanding that you are that supreme judge and that you have jurisdiction even over the demigods. Our impression was that you are the master of all living entities, the supreme authority who dis
criminates between the pious and impious activities of all human beings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.8 - But now we see that the punishment ordained under your authority is no longer effective, since your order has been transgressed by four wonderful and perfect persons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.9 - We were bringing the most sinful Aj\'e4mila toward the hellish planets, following your order, when those beautiful persons from Siddhaloka forcibly cut the knots of the ropes with which we were arresting him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.10 - As soon as the sinful Aj\'e4mila uttered the name N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, these four beautiful men immediately arrived and reassured him, saying, "Do not fear. Do not fear." We wish to know about them from Your Lordship. If you think we are able to understand them, kindly describe who they are.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.11 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Thus having been questioned, Lord Yamar\'e4
ja, the supreme controller of the living entities, was very pleased with his order carriers because of hearing from them the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. He remembered the lotus feet of the Lord and began to reply.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.12 - Yamar\'e4ja said: My dear servants, you have accepted me as the Supreme, but factually I am not. Above me, and above all the other demigods, including Indra and Candra, is the one supreme master and controller. The parti
al manifestations of His personality are Brahm\'e4, Vi\'f1\'ebu and \'c7
iva, who are in charge of the creation, maintenance and annihilation of this universe. He is like the two threads that form the length and breadth of a woven cloth. The entire world is controlled by Him just as a bull is controlled by a rope in its nose.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.13 - Just as the driver of a bullock cart ties ropes through the nostrils of his bulls to control them, the Supreme Personality of Godhead binds all men through the ropes of His words in th
e Vedas, which set forth the names and activities of the distinct orders of human society [br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya and \'e7\'fc
dra]. In fear, the members of these orders all worship the Supreme Lord by offering Him presentations according to their respective activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.14-15 - I, Yamar\'e4ja; Indra, the King of heaven; Nir\'e5ti; Varu\'eba; Candra, the moon-god; Agni; Lord \'c7iva; Pavana; Lord Brahm\'e4; S\'fcrya, the sun-god; Vi\'e7v\'e4su; the eight Vasus; the S\'e4
dhyas; the Maruts; the Rudras; the Siddhas; and Mar\'e9ci and the other great \'e5\'f1is engaged in maintaining the departmental affairs of the universe, as well as the best of the demigods headed by B\'e5haspati, and the great sages headed by Bh\'e5
gu are all certainly freed from the influence of the two base material modes of n
ature, namely passion and ignorance. Nevertheless, although we are in the mode of goodness, we cannot understand the activities of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. What, then, is to be said of others, who, under illusion, merely speculate to know God?

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.3.16 - As the different limbs of the body cannot see the eyes, the living entities cannot see the Supreme Lord, who is situated as the Supersoul in everyone's heart. Not by the senses, by the mind, by the life air, by thoughts within the heart, or by
 the vibration of words can the living entities ascertain the real situation of the Supreme Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.17 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is self-sufficient and fully independent. He is the master of everyone and everything, including the illusory e
nergy. He has His form, qualities and features; and similarly His order carriers, the Vai\'f1\'eb
avas, who are very beautiful, possess bodily features, transcendental qualities and a transcendental nature almost like His. They always wander within this world with full independence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.18 - The order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who are worshiped even by the demigods, possess wonderful bodily features exactly like those of Vi\'f1\'ebu and are very rarely seen. The Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fc
tas protect the devotees of the Lord from the hands of enemies, from envious persons and even from my jurisdiction, as well as from natural disturbances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.19 - Real religious principles are enacted by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Although fully situated in the mode of goodness, even the great \'e5\'f1
is who occupy the topmost planets cannot ascertain the real religious principles, nor can the demigods or the leaders of Siddhaloka, to say nothing of the asuras, ordinary human beings, Vidy\'e4dharas and C\'e4ra\'ebas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.20-21 - Lord Brahm\'e4, Bhagav\'e4n N\'e4rada, Lord \'c7iva, the four Kum\'e4ras, Lord Kapila [the son of Devah\'fcti], Sv\'e4yambhuva Manu, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Janaka Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, Grandfather Bh\'e9\'f1
ma, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 and I myself know the real religious principle. My dear servants, this transcendental religious principle, which is known as bh\'e4
gavata-dharma, or surrender unto the Supreme Lord and love for Him, is uncontaminated by the material modes of nature. It is very confidential and difficult for ordinary human beings to understand, but if by 
chance one fortunately understands it, he is immediately liberated, and thus he returns home, back to Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.22 - Devotional service, beginning with the chanting of the holy name of the Lord, is the ultimate religious principle for the living entity in human society.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.23 - My dear servants, who are as good as my sons, just see how glorious is the chanting of the holy name of the Lord. The greatly sinful Aj\'e4
mila chanted only to call his son, not knowing that he was chanting the Lord's holy name. Nevertheless, by chanting the holy name of the Lord, he remembered N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, and thus he was immediately saved from the ropes of death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.24 - Therefore it should be understood that one is easily relieved from all sinful reactions by chanting th
e holy name of the Lord and chanting of His qualities and activities. This is the only process recommended for relief from sinful reactions. Even if one chants the holy name of the Lord with improper pronunciation, he will achieve relief from material bon
dage if he chants without offenses. Aj\'e4mila, for example, was extremely sinful, but while dying he merely chanted the holy name, and although calling his son, he achieved complete liberation because he remembered the name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.25 - Because they are bewildered by the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Y\'e4j\'ef
avalkya and Jaimini and other compilers of the religious scriptures cannot know the secret, confidential religious system of the twelve mah\'e4janas. They cannot understand the transcendental value of performing devotional service or chanting the Hare K
\'e5\'f1\'eba mantra. Because their minds are attracted to the ritualistic ceremonies mentioned in the Vedas-especially the Yajur Veda, S\'e4ma Veda and \'c5g Veda-their intelligence has becom
e dull. Thus they are busy collecting the ingredients for ritualistic ceremonies that yield only temporary benefits, such as elevation to Svargaloka for material happiness. They are not attracted to the sa\'eck\'e9
rtana movement; instead, they are interested in dharma, artha, k\'e4ma and mok\'f1a.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.26 - Considering all these points, therefore, intelligent men decide to solve all problems by adopting the devotional service of chanting the holy name of the Lord, who is situated in everyone's heart and who is a min
e of all auspicious qualities. Such persons are not within my jurisdiction for punishment. Generally they never commit sinful activities, but even if by mistake or because of bewilderment or illusion they sometimes commit sinful acts, they are protected f
rom sinful reactions because they always chant the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba mantra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.27 - My dear servants, please do not approach such devotees, for they have fully surrendered to the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. They are equal to everyone, a
nd their narrations are sung by the demigods and the inhabitants of Siddhaloka. Please do not even go near them. They are always protected by the club of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and therefore Lord Brahm\'e4
 and I and even the time factor are not competent to chastise them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.28 - Paramaha\'e0sas are exalted persons who have no taste for material enjoyment and who drink the honey of the Lord's lotus feet. My dear servants, bring to me for punishment only persons who are averse to the taste of tha
t honey, who do not associate with paramaha\'e0sas and who are attached to family life and worldly enjoyment, which form the path to hell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.29 - My dear servants, please bring to me only those sinful persons who do not use their tongues to chant the holy name and qualities of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, whose hearts do not remember the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a even once, and whose heads do not bow down even once before Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Send me those who do not perform their duties toward Vi\'f1\'ebu, which are the only duties in human life. Please bring me all such fools and rascals.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.30 - [Then Yamar\'e4ja, considering himself and his servants to be offenders, spoke as follows, begging pardon from the Lord.] O my Lord, my servants have surely committed a great offense by arresting a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava such as Aj\'e4mila. O N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, O supreme and oldest person, please forgive us. Because of our ignorance, we failed to recognize Aj\'e4
mila as a servant of Your Lordship, and thus we have certainly committed a great offense. Therefore with folded hands we
 beg Your pardon. My Lord, since You are supremely merciful and are always full of good qualities, please pardon us. We offer our respectful obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.31 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear King, the chanting of the holy name of the Lord is able to uproot even the reactions of the greatest sins. Therefore the chanting of the sa\'eck\'e9
rtana movement is the most auspicious activity in the entire universe. Please try to understand this so that others will take it seriously.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.32 - One wh
o constantly hears and chants the holy name of the Lord and hears and chants about His activities can very easily attain the platform of pure devotional service, which can cleanse the dirt from one's heart. One cannot achieve such purification merely by o
bserving vows and performing Vedic ritualistic ceremonies.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.33 - Devotees who always lick the honey from the lotus feet of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba do not care at all for material activities, which are performed under the three modes of material nature and which b
ring only misery. Indeed, devotees never give up the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a to return to material activities. Others, however, who are addicted to Vedic rituals because they have neglected the service of the Lord's lotus feet and are enchanted by lusty desire
s, sometimes perform acts of atonement. Nevertheless, being incompletely purified, they return to sinful activities again and again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.34 - After hearing from the mouth of their master about the extraordinary glories of the Lord and His name, fame and attributes, the Yamad\'fc
tas were struck with wonder. Since then, as soon as they see a devotee, they fear him and dare not look at him again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.3.35 - When the great sage Agastya, the son of Kumbha, was residing in the Malaya Hills and worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, I approached him, and he explained to me this confidential history.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
