{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.1-2 - The blessed King said to \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9: My dear lord, the demigods, demons, human beings, N\'e4gas, beasts and birds were created during the reign of Sv\'e4
yambhuva Manu. You have spoken about this creation briefly [in the Third Canto]. Now I wish to know about it elaborately. I also wish to know about the potency of the Supreme Personality of Godhead by which He brought about the secondary creation.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.3 - S\'fcta Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O great sages [assembled at Naimi\'f1\'e4ra\'ebya], after the great yogi \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 heard King Par\'e9k\'f1it's inquiry, he praised it and thus replied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.4 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: When the ten sons of Pr\'e4c\'e9nabarhi emerged from the waters, in which they were performing austerities, they saw that the entire surface of the world was covered by trees.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.5 - Because of having undergone long austerities in the water, the Pracet\'e4s were very angry at the trees. Desiring to burn them to ashes, they generated wind and fire from their mouths.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.6 - My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, when Soma, the king of the trees and predominating deity of the moon, saw the fire and wind burning all the trees to ashes, he felt great sympathy because 
he is the maintainer of all herbs and trees. To appease the anger of the Pracet\'e4s, Soma spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.7 - O greatly fortunate ones, you should not kill these poor trees by burning them to ashes. Your duty is to wish the citizens [praj\'e4s] all prosperity and to act as their protectors.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.8 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, \'c7r\'e9 Hari, is the master of all living entities, including all the praj\'e4patis, such as Lord Brahm\'e4. Because He is the all-pervading and indestructible master, He has cr
eated all these trees and vegetables as eatables for other living entities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.9 - By nature's arrangement, fruits and flowers are considered the food of insects and birds; grass and other legless living entities are meant to be the food of four-legge
d animals like cows and buffalo; animals that cannot use their front legs as hands are meant to be the food of animals like tigers, which have claws; and four-legged animals like deer and goats, as well as food grains, are meant to be the food of human be
ings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.10 - O pure-hearted ones, your father, Pr\'e4c\'e9
nabarhi, and the Supreme Personality of Godhead have ordered you to generate population. Therefore how can you burn to ashes these trees and herbs, which are needed for the maintenance of your subjects and descendants?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.11 - The path of goodness traversed by your father, grandfather and great-grandfathers is that of maintaining the subjects [praj\'e4
s], including the men, animals and trees. That is the path you should follow. Unnecessary anger is contrary to your duty. Therefore I request you to control your anger.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.12 - As the father and mother are the friends and maintainers of their children, as the eyelid is the protector of the eye, as the husband is the maintainer and protector of a wo
man, as the householder is the maintainer and protector of beggars, and as the learned is the friend of the ignorant, so the king is the protector and giver of life to all his subjects. The trees are also subjects of the king. Therefore they should be giv
en protection.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.4.13 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is situated as the Supersoul within the cores of the hearts of all living entities, whether moving or nonmoving, including men, birds, animals, trees and, indeed, all living entities. Therefore 
you should consider every body a residence or temple of the Lord. By such vision you will satisfy the Lord. You should not angrily kill these living entities in the forms of trees.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.14 - One who inquires into self-realization and thus subdues his powerful anger-which awakens suddenly in the body as if falling from the sky-transcends the influence of the modes of material nature.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.15 - There is no need to burn these poor trees any longer. Let whatever trees still remain be happy. Indeed, you should also be happy. Now, here is a beautiful, well-qualified girl named M\'e4ri\'f1\'e4
, who was raised by the trees as their daughter. You may accept this beautiful girl as your wife.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.16 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear King, after thus pacifying the Pracet\'e4s, Soma, the king of the moon, gave them the beautiful girl born of Pramloc\'e4 Apsar\'e4. The Pracet\'e4s all received Pramloc\'e4
's daughter, who had high, very beautiful hips, and married her according to the religious system.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.17 - In the womb of that girl the Pracet\'e4s all begot a son named Dak\'f1a, who filled the three worlds with living entities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.18 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Please hear from me with great attention how Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a, who was very affectionate to his daughters, created di
fferent types of living entities through his semen and through his mind.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.19 - With his mind, Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a first created all kinds of demigods, demons, human beings, birds, beasts, aquatics and so on.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.20 - But when Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a saw that he was not properly generating all kinds of living entities, he approached a mountain near the Vindhya mountain range, and there he executed very difficult austerities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.21 - Near that mountain was a very holy place named Aghamar\'f1a\'eba. There Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1
a executed ritualistic ceremonies and satisfied the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, by engaging in great austerities to please Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.22 - My dear King, I shall fully explain to you the Ha\'e0sa-guhya prayers, which were offered to the Supreme Personality of Godhead by Dak\'f1a, and I shall explain how the Lord was pleased with him for those prayers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.23 - Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a said: The Supreme Personality of Godhead is transcendental to the illusory energy and the physical categories it pro
duces. He possesses the potency for unfailing knowledge and supreme willpower, and He is the controller of the living entities and the illusory energy. The conditioned souls who have accepted this material manifestation as everything cannot see Him, for H
e is above the evidence of experimental knowledge. Self-evident and self-sufficient, He is not caused by any superior cause. Let me offer my respectful obeisances unto Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.24 - As the sense objects [form, taste, touch, smell and sound] cannot under
stand how the senses perceive them, so the conditioned soul, although residing in his body along with the Supersoul, cannot understand how the supreme spiritual person, the master of the material creation, directs his senses. Let me offer my respectful ob
eisances unto that Supreme Person, who is the supreme controller.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.25 - Because they are only matter, the body, the life airs, the external and internal senses, the five gross elements and the subtle sense objects [form, taste, smell, sound and touch
] cannot know their own nature, the nature of the other senses or the nature of their controllers. But the living being, because of his spiritual nature, can know his body, the life airs, the senses, the elements and the sense objects, and he can also kno
w the three qualities that form their roots. Nevertheless, although the living being is completely aware of them, he is unable to see the Supreme Being, who is omniscient and unlimited. I therefore offer my respectful obeisances unto Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.26 - When one's consciousness is completely purified of the contamination of material existence, gross and subtle, without being agitated as in the working and dreaming states, and when the mind is not dissolved as in su\'f1
upti, deep sleep, one comes to the platform o
f trance. Then one's material vision and the memories of the mind, which manifests names and forms, are vanquished. Only in such a trance is the Supreme Personality of Godhead revealed. Thus let us offer our respectful obeisances unto the Supreme Personal
ity of Godhead, who is seen in that uncontaminated, transcendental state.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.27-28 - Just as great learned br\'e4hma\'ebas who are expert in performing ritualistic ceremonies and sacrifices can extract the fire dormant within wooden fuel by chanting the fifteen S\'e4midhen\'e9
 mantras, thus proving the efficacy of the Vedic mantras, so those who are actually advanced in consciousness-in other words, those who are K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious-can find the Supersoul, who by His own spiritual potency is situated within the heart. 
The heart is covered by the three modes of material nature and the nine material elements [material nature, the total material energy, the ego, the mind and the five objects of sense gratification], and also by the five material elements and the ten sense
s. These twenty-seven elements constitute the external energy of the Lord. Great yog\'e9s meditate upon the Lord, who is situated as the Supersoul, Param\'e4tm\'e4
, within the core of the heart. May that Supersoul be pleased with me. The Supersoul is realized when o
ne is eager for liberation from the unlimited varieties of material life. One actually attains such liberation when he engages in the transcendental loving service of the Lord and realizes the Lord because of his attitude of service. The Lord may be addre
ssed by various spiritual names, which are inconceivable to the material senses. When will that Supreme Personality of Godhead be pleased with me?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.29 - Anything expressed by material vibrations, anything ascertained by material intelligence and anyt
hing experienced by the material senses or concocted within the material mind is but an effect of the modes of material nature and therefore has nothing to do with the real nature of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The Supreme Lord is beyond the creat
ion of this material world, for He is the source of the material qualities and creation. As the cause of all causes, He exists before the creation and after the creation. I wish to offer my respectful obeisances unto Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.30 - The Supreme Brahman, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, is the ultimate resting place and source of everything. Everything is done by Him, everything belongs to Him, and everything is offered to Him. He is the ultimate objective, and whether acting or causing others to act, He is the ultimate doer. There 
are many causes, high and low, but since He is the cause of all causes, He is well known as the Supreme Brahman who existed before all activities. He is one without a second and has no other cause. I therefore offer my respects unto Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.31 - Let m
e offer my respectful obeisances unto the all-pervading Supreme Personality of Godhead, who possesses unlimited transcendental qualities. Acting from within the cores of the hearts of all philosophers, who propagate various views, He causes them to forget
 their own souls while sometimes agreeing and sometimes disagreeing among themselves. Thus He creates within this material world a situation in which they are unable to come to a conclusion. I offer my obeisances unto Him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.32 - There are two parties-namely, the theists and the atheists. The theist, who accepts the Supersoul, finds the spiritual cause through mystic yoga. The S\'e4\'ec
khyite, however, who merely analyzes the material elements, comes to a conclusion of impersonalism and does not accept a supreme cause-whether Bhagav\'e4n, Param\'e4tm\'e4
 or even Brahman. Instead, he is preoccupied with the superfluous, external activities of material nature. Ultimately, however, both parties demonstrate the Absolute Truth because although they offer opposing statement
s, their object is the same ultimate cause. They are both approaching the same Supreme Brahman, to whom I offer my respectful obeisances.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.33 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is inconceivably opulent, who is devoid of all material names, fo
rms and pastimes, and who is all-pervading, is especially merciful to the devotees who worship His lotus feet. Thus He exhibits transcendental forms and names with His different pastimes. May that Supreme Personality of Godhead, whose form is eternal and 
full of knowledge and bliss, be merciful to me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.34 - As the air carries various characteristics of the physical elements, like the aroma of a flower or colors resulting from a mixture of dust in the air, the Lord appears through lower systems of wor
ship according to one's desires, although He appears as the demigods and not in His original form. What is the use of these other forms? May the original Supreme Personality of Godhead please fulfill my desires.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.35-39 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, who is extremely affectionate to His devotees, was very pleased by the prayers offered by Dak\'f1
a, and thus He appeared at that holy place known as Aghamar\'f1a\'eba. O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, best of the Kuru dynasty, the Lord's lotus feet rested on the shoulders of His carrier, Garu\'f2
a, and He appeared with eight long, mighty, very beautiful arms. In His hands He held a disc, conchshell, sword, shield, arrow, bow, rope and club-in each hand a different weapon, all brilliantly sh
ining. His garments were yellow and His bodily hue deep bluish. His eyes and face were very cheerful, and from His neck to His feet hung a long garland of flowers. His chest was decorated with the Kaustubha jewel and the mark of \'c7r\'e9
vatsa. On His head was a
 gorgeous round helmet, and His ears were decorated with earrings resembling sharks. All these ornaments were uncommonly beautiful. The Lord wore a golden belt on His waist, bracelets on His arms, rings on His fingers, and ankle bells on His feet. Thus de
corated by various ornaments, Lord Hari, who is attractive to all the living entities of the three worlds, is known as Puru\'f1ottama, the best personality. He was accompanied by great devotees like N\'e4
rada, Nanda and all the principal demigods, led by the heavenly king, Indra, and the residents of various upper planetary systems such as Siddhaloka, Gandharvaloka and C\'e4ra\'eb
aloka. Situated on both sides of the Lord and behind Him as well, these devotees offered Him prayers continuously.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.40 - Seeing that wonderful and effulgent form of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a was first somewhat afraid, but then he was very pleased to see the Lord, and he fell to the ground like a stick [da
\'eb\'f2avat] to offer his respects to the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.41 - As rivers are filled by water flowing from a mountain, all of Dak\'f1a's senses were filled with pleasure. Because of his highly elevated happiness, Dak\'f1
a could not say anything, but simply remained flat on the ground.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.42 - Although Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a could not say anything, when the Lord, who knows everyone's heart, saw His devotee prostrate in that manner and desiring to increase the population, He addressed him as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.43 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: O most fortunate Pr\'e4cetasa, b
ecause of your great faith in Me, you have attained the supreme devotional ecstasy. Indeed, because of your austerities, combined with exalted devotion, your life is now successful. You have achieved complete perfection.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.44 - My dear Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1
a, you have performed extreme austerities for the welfare and growth of the world. My desire also is that everyone within this world be happy. I am therefore very pleased with you because you are endeavoring to fulfill My desire for the welfare of the ent
ire world.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.45 - Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva, the Manus, all the other demigods in the higher planetary systems, and you praj\'e4
patis, who are increasing the population, are working for the benefit of all living entities. Thus you expansions of My marginal energy are incarnations of My various qualities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.46 - My dear br\'e4hma\'eba, austerity in the form of meditation is My heart, Vedic knowledge in the form of hymns and mantras constitutes My body, and spiritual activities and ecstatic emotions are My act
ual form. The ritualistic ceremonies and sacrifices, when properly conducted, are the various limbs of My body, the unseen good fortune proceeding from pious or spiritual activities constitutes My mind, and the demigods who execute My orders in various de
partments are My life and soul.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.47 - Before the creation of this cosmic manifestation, I alone existed with My specific spiritual potencies. Consciousness was then unmanifested, just as one's consciousness is unmanifested during the time of sleep.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.4.48 - I am the reservoir of unlimited potency, and therefore I am known as unlimited or all-pervading. From My material energy the cosmic manifestation appeared within Me, and in this universal manifestation appeared the chief being, Lord Brahm\'e4
, who is your source and is not born of a material mother.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.49-50 - When the chief lord of the universe, Lord Brahm\'e4 [Svayambh\'fc], having been inspired by My energy, was attempting to create, he thought himself incapable. Therefore I gave him advice, and 
in accordance with My instructions he underwent extremely difficult austerities. Because of these austerities, the great Lord Brahm\'e4 was able to create nine personalities, including you, to help him in the functions of creation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.51 - O My dear son Dak\'f1a, Praj\'e4pati Pa\'efcajana has a daughter named Asikn\'e9, whom I offer to you so that you may accept her as your wife.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.52 - Now unite in sexual life as man and woman, and in this way, by sexual intercourse, you will be able to beget hundreds of children in the womb of this girl to increase the population.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.53 - After you give birth to many hundreds and thousands of children, they will also be captivated by My illusory energy and will engage, like You, in sexual intercourse. But because of My me
rcy to you and them, they will also be able to give Me presentations in devotion.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.4.54 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After the creator of the entire universe, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, had spoken in this way in the presence of Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1
a, He immediately disappeared as if He were an object experienced in a dream.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  4. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
