\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.7.37 - All of you are my superiors
. Therefore although accepting priesthood is sometimes reproachable, I cannot refuse even a small request from you. I agree to be your priest. I shall fulfill your request by dedicating my life and possessions.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.7.38 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: O King, after making this promise to the demigods, the exalted Vi\'e7var\'fc
pa, surrounded by the demigods, performed the necessary priestly activities with great enthusiasm and attention.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.7.39 - The opulence of the demons, who are generally known as the enemies of the demigods, was protected by the talents and tactics of \'c7ukr\'e4c\'e4rya, but Vi\'e7var\'fc
pa, who was most powerful, composed a protective prayer known as the N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-kavaca. By this intelligent mantra, he took away the opulence of the demons and gave it to Mahendra, the King of heaven.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.7.40 - Vi\'e7var\'fcpa, who was most liberal, spoke to King Indra [Sahasr\'e4k\'f1a] the secret hymn that protected Indra and conquered the military power of the demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Translations 1-40
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.1-2 - King Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired from \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9: My lord, kindly explain the Vi\'f1\'eb
u mantra armor that protected King Indra and enabled him to conquer his enemies, along with their carriers, and enjoy the opulence of the three worlds. Please explain to me that N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba armor, by which King Indra achiev
ed success in battle, conquering the enemies who were endeavoring to kill him.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.3 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: King Indra, the leader of the demigods, inquired about the armor known as N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-kavaca from Vi\'e7var\'fcpa, who was engaged by the demigods 
as their priest. Please hear Vi\'e7var\'fcpa's reply with great attention.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.4-6 - Vi\'e7var\'fcpa said: If some form of fear arrives, one should first wash his hands and legs clean and then perform \'e4camana by chanting this mantra: o\'e0 apavitra\'f9 pavitro v\'e4 sarv\'e4vasth\'e4\'e0 gato 'pi v
\'e4/ ya\'f9 smaret pu\'eb\'f2ar\'e9k\'e4k\'f1a\'e0 sa bahy\'e4bhyantara\'f9 \'e7uci\'f9/ \'e7r\'e9-vi\'f1\'ebu \'e7r\'e9-vi\'f1\'ebu \'e7r\'e9-vi\'f1\'ebu. Then one should touch ku\'e7
a grass and sit gravely and silently, facing north. When completely purified, one should touch the mantra composed of eight sylla
bles to the eight parts of his body and touch the mantra composed of twelve syllables to his hands. Thus, in the following manner, he should bind himself with the N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a coat of armor. First, while chanting the mantra composed of eight syllables [o\'e0 namo n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb\'e4ya], beginning with the pra\'ebava, the syllable o\'e0
, one should touch his hands to eight parts of his body, starting with the two feet and progressing systematically to the knees, thighs, abdomen, heart, chest, mouth and head. Then one should chant t
he mantra in reverse, beginning from the last syllable [ya], while touching the parts of his body in the reverse order. These two processes are known as utpatti-ny\'e4sa and sa\'e0h\'e4ra-ny\'e4sa respectively.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.7 - Then one should chant the mantra composed of twelve syllables [o\'e0 namo bhagavate v\'e4sudev\'e4ya]. Preceding each syllable by the o\'e0k\'e4
ra, one should place the syllables of the mantra on the tips of his fingers, beginning with the index finger of the right hand and concluding with the index finger of the left. The four remaining syllables should be placed on the joints of the thumbs.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.8-10 - One must then chant the mantra of six syllables [o\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebave nama\'f9]. One should place the syllable "o\'e0" on his heart, the syllable "vi" on the top of his head, the syllable "\'f1
a" between his eyebrows, the syllable "\'eba" on his tuft of hair [\'e7ikh\'e4], and the syllable "ve" between his eyes. The chanter of the mantra should then place the syllable "na" on all the joints of his body and meditate on the syllable "ma" as be
ing a weapon. He should thus become the perfect personification of the mantra. Thereafter, adding visarga to the final syllable "ma," he should chant the mantra "ma\'f9 astr\'e4ya pha\'f6
" in all directions, beginning from the east. In this way, all directions will be bound by the protective armor of the mantra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.11 - After finishing this chanting, one should think himself qualitatively one with the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is full in six opulences and is worthy to be meditated upon. Then one shoul
d chant the following protective prayer to Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, the N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-kavaca.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.12 - The Supreme Lord, who sits on the back of the bird Garu\'f2a, touching him with His lotus feet, holds eight weapons-the conchshell, disc, shield, sword, club, arrows, 
bow and ropes. May that Supreme Personality of Godhead protect me at all times with His eight arms. He is all-powerful because He fully possesses the eight mystic powers [a\'ebim\'e4, laghim\'e4, etc.].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.13 - May the Lord, who assumes the body of a great fish, protect me in the water from the fierce animals that are associates of the demigod Varu\'eba. By expanding His illusory energy, the Lord assumed the form of the dwarf V
\'e4mana. May V\'e4mana protect me on the land. Since the gigantic form of the Lord, Vi\'e7var\'fcpa, conquers the three worlds, may He protect me in the sky.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.14 - May Lord N\'e5si\'e0hadeva, who appeared as the enemy of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu, protect me in all directions. His loud laughing vibrated in all directions and caused the pregnant wives of the asuras
 to have miscarriages. May that Lord be kind enough to protect me in difficult places like the forest and battlefront.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.15 - The Supreme indestructible Lord is ascertained through the performance of ritualistic sacrifices and is therefore known as Yaj\'efe\'e7
vara. In His incarnation as Lord Boar, He raised the planet earth from the water at the bottom of the universe and kept it on His pointed tusks. May that Lord protect me from rogues on the street. May Para\'e7ur\'e4
ma protect me on the tops of mountains, and may the elder brother of Bharata, Lord R\'e4macandra, along with His brother Lak\'f1ma\'eba, protect me in foreign countries.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.16 - May Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba protect me from unnecessarily following false religious systems and falling from my duties due to madness.
 May the Lord in His appearance as Nara protect me from unnecessary pride. May Lord Datt\'e4
treya, the master of all mystic power, protect me from falling while performing bhakti-yoga, and may Lord Kapila, the master of all good qualities, protect me from the material bondage of fruitive activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.17 - May Sanat-kum\'e4ra protect me from lusty desires. As I begin some auspicious activity, may Lord Hayagr\'e9va protect me from being an offender by neglecting to offer respectful obeisances to the Supreme Lord. May Devar
\'f1i N\'e4rada protect me from committing offenses in worshiping the Deity, and may Lord K\'fcrma, the tortoise, protect me from falling to the unlimited hellish planets.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.18 - May the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His incarnation as Dhanvantari relieve me from undesirable eatables and protect me from physical illness. May Lord \'c5\'f1
abhadeva, who conquered His inner and outer senses, protect me from fear produced by the duality of heat and cold. May Yaj\'efa protect me from defamation and harm from the populace, and may Lord Balar\'e4ma as \'c7e\'f1a protect me from envious serpents.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.19 - May the Personality of Godhead in His incarnation as Vy\'e4sadeva protect me from all kinds of ignorance resulting from the absence of Vedic knowledge. May Lord Buddha
deva protect me from activities opposed to Vedic principles and from laziness that causes one to madly forget the Vedic principles of knowledge and ritualistic action. May Kalkideva, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who appeared as an incarnation to pr
otect religious principles, protect me from the dirt of the age of Kali.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.20 - May Lord Ke\'e7ava protect me with His club in the first portion of the day, and may Govinda, who is always engaged in playing His flute, protect me in the second portion of the day. May Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, who is equipped with all potencies, protect me in the third part of the day, and may Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who carries a disc to kill His enemies, protect me in the fourth part of the day.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.21 - May Lord Madhus\'fcdana, who carries a bow very fearful for the demons, protect me during the fifth part of the day. In the evening, may Lord M\'e4dhava, appearing as Brahm\'e4, Vi\'f1\'ebu and Mahe\'e7
vara, protect me, and in the beginning of night may Lord H\'e5\'f1\'e9ke\'e7a protect me. At the dead of night [in the second and third parts of night] may Lord Padman\'e4bha alone protect me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.22 - May the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who bears the \'c7r\'e9vatsa on His chest, protect me after midnight until the sky becomes pinkish. May Lord Jan\'e4rdana, who carries a sword
 in His hand, protect me at the end of night [during the last four gha\'f6ik\'e4s of night]. May Lord D\'e4modara protect me in the early morning, and may Lord Vi\'e7ve\'e7vara protect me during the junctions of day and night.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.23 - Set into motion by the Supreme 
Personality of Godhead and wandering in all the four directions, the disc of the Supreme Lord has sharp edges as destructive as the fire of devastation at the end of the millennium. As a blazing fire burns dry grass to ashes with the assistance of the bre
eze, may that Sudar\'e7ana cakra burn our enemies to ashes.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.24 - O club in the hand of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, you produce sparks of fire as powerful as thunderbolts, and you are extremely dear to the Lord. I am also His servant. Therefore 
kindly help me pound to pieces the evil living beings known as Ku\'f1m\'e4\'eb\'f2as, Vain\'e4yakas, Yak\'f1as, R\'e4k\'f1asas, Bh\'fctas and Grahas. Please pulverize them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.25 - O best of conchshells, O P\'e4\'efcajanya in the hands of the Lord, you are always filled with the breath of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. Therefore you create a fearful sound vibration that causes trembling in the hearts of enemies like the R\'e4k\'f1asas, pramatha ghosts, Pretas, M\'e4t\'e4s, Pi\'e7\'e4cas and br\'e4hma\'eba ghosts with fearful eyes.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.26 - O king of sharp-edged swords, you
 are engaged by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Please cut the soldiers of my enemies to pieces. Please cut them to pieces! O shield marked with a hundred brilliant moonlike circles, please cover the eyes of the sinful enemies. Pluck out their sinful 
eyes.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.8.27-28 - May the glorification of the transcendental name, form, qualities and paraphernalia of the Supreme Personality of Godhead protect us from the influence of bad planets, meteors, envious human beings, serpents, scorpions, and animals lik
e tigers and wolves. May it protect us from ghosts and the material elements like earth, water, fire and air, and may it also protect us from lightning and our past sins. We are always afraid of these hindrances to our auspicious life. Therefore, may they
 all be completely destroyed by the chanting of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba mah\'e4-mantra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.29 - Lord Garu\'f2a, the carrier of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, is the most worshipable lord, for he is as powerful as the Supreme Lord Himself. He is the personified Vedas and is worshiped by
 selected verses. May he protect us from all dangerous conditions, and may Lord Vi\'f1vaksena, the Personality of Godhead, also protect us from all dangers by His holy names.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.30 - May the Supreme Personality of Godhead's holy names, His transcendental forms, His carriers and all the weapons decorating Him as personal associates protect our intelligence, senses, mind and life air from all dangers.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.31 - The subtle and gross cosmic manifestation is material, but nevertheless it is nondifferent fro
m the Supreme Personality of Godhead because He is ultimately the cause of all causes. Cause and effect are factually one because the cause is present in the effect. Therefore the Absolute Truth, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, can destroy all our dan
gers by any of His potent parts.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.32-33 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead, the living entities, the material energy, the spiritual energy and the entire creation are all individual substances. In the ultimate analysis, however, together they const
itute the supreme one, the Personality of Godhead. Therefore those who are advanced in spiritual knowledge see unity in diversity. For such advanced persons, the Lord's bodily decorations, His name, His fame, His attributes and forms and the weapons in Hi
s hand are manifestations of the strength of His potency. According to their elevated spiritual understanding, the omniscient Lord, who manifests various forms, is present everywhere. May He always protect us everywhere from all calamities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.34 - Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja loudly chanted the holy name of Lord N\'e5si\'e0hadeva. May Lord N\'e5si\'e0hadeva, roaring for His devotee Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, protect us from all fear of dangers created by stalwart leaders in all directions through poison, weapons, water, fire, air and so on. May the Lord cover their influence by His own transcendental influence. May N\'e5si\'e0
hadeva protect us in all directions and in all corners, above, below, within and without.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.35 - Vi\'e7var\'fcpa continued: O Indra, this mystic armor related to Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a has been described by me to you. By putting on this protective covering, you will certainly be able to conquer the leaders of the demons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.36 - If one employs this armor, whomever he sees with his eyes or touches with his feet is immediately freed from all the above-mentioned dangers.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.37 - This prayer, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-kavaca, constitutes subtle knowledge transcendentally connected with N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. One who employs this prayer is never disturbed or put in danger by the government, by plunderer
s, by evil demons or by any type of disease.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.38 - O King of heaven, a br\'e4hma\'eba named Kau\'e7ika formerly used this armor when he purposely gave up his body in the desert by mystic power.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.39 - Surrounded by many beautiful women, Citraratha, the King of Gandharvaloka, was once passing in his airplane over the br\'e4hma\'eba's body at the spot where the br\'e4hma\'eba had died.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.40 - Suddenly Citraratha was forced to fall from the sky headfirst with his airplane. Struck with wonder, he was ordered by the great sages named the V\'e4likhilyas to throw the br\'e4hma\'eb
a's bones in the nearby River Sarasvat\'e9. He had to do this and bathe in the river before returning to his own abode.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.41 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: My dear Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, one who employs
 this armor or hears about it with faith and veneration when afraid because of any conditions in the material world is immediately freed from all dangers and is worshiped by all living entities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.8.42 - King Indra, who performed one hundred sacrifices, received this prayer of protection from Vi\'e7var\'fcpa. After conquering the demons, he enjoyed all the opulences of the three worlds.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  8. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
