\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\cf2\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.24 - O my L
ord, O Supreme Personality of Godhead, will I again be; able to be a servant of Your eternal servants who find shelter only at Your lotus feet? O Lord of my life, may I again become their servant so that my mind may always think of Your transcendental att
ributes, my words always glorify those attributes, and my body always engage in the loving service of Your Lordship?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\cf2\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.25 - O my Lord, source of all opportunities, I do not desire to enjoy in Dhruvaloka, the heavenly planets or the planet where Lord Brahm\'e4
 resides, nor do I want to be the supreme ruler of all the earthly planets or the lower planetary systems. I do not desire to be master of the powers of mystic yoga, nor do I want liberation if I have to give up Your lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\cf2\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.26 - O lotus
-eyed Lord, as baby birds that have not yet developed their wings always look for their mother to return and feed them, as small calves tied with ropes await anxiously the time of milking, when they will be allowed to drink the milk of their mothers, or a
s a morose wife whose husband is away from home always longs for him to return and satisfy her in all respects, I always yearn for the opportunity to render direct service unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\cf2\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.27 - O my Lord, my master, I am wandering throughout this material
 world as a result of my fruitive activities. Therefore I simply seek friendship in the association of Your pious and enlightened devotees. My attachment to my body, wife, children and home is continuing by the spell of Your external energy, but I wish to
 be attached to them no longer. Let my mind, my consciousness and everything I have be attached only to You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf2\insrsid10252087  }{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The Transcendental Qualities of V\'e5tr\'e4sura
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0\pararsid10252087 \shading10000\cfpat8 {\fs28\cf2\insrsid10252087   \bullet 
  }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.1 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, V\'e5tr\'e4sura, the commander in chief of the demons, advised his lieutenants in the principles of reli
gion, but the cowardly demoniac commanders, intent upon fleeing the battlefield, were so disturbed by fear that they could not accept his words.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.2-3 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, the demigods, taking advantage of a favorable opportunity presented by time, at
tacked the army of the demons from the rear and began driving away the demoniac soldiers, scattering them here and there as if their army had no leader. Seeing the pitiable condition of his soldiers, V\'e5tr\'e4
sura, the best of the asuras, who was called Indra\'e7atru, the enemy of Indra, was very much aggrieved. Unable to tolerate such reverses, he stopped and forcefully rebuked the demigods, speaking the following words in an angry mood.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.4 - O demigods, these demoniac soldiers have taken birth uselessly.
 Indeed, they have come from the bodies of their mothers exactly like stool. What is the benefit of killing such enemies from behind while they are running in fear? One who considers himself a hero should not kill an enemy who is afraid of losing his life
. Such killing is never glorious, nor can it promote one to the heavenly planets.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.5 - O insignificant demigods, if you truly have faith in your heroism, if you have patience in the cores of your hearts and if you are not ambitious for sense gratification, please stand before me for a moment.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.6 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: V\'e5tr\'e4sura, the angry and most powerful hero, terrified the demigods with his stout and strongly built body. When he roared with a resounding voice, nearly all living entities 
fainted.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.7 - When all the demigods heard V\'e5tr\'e4sura's tumultuous roar, which resembled that of a lion, they fainted and fell to the ground as if struck by thunderbolts.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.8 - As the demigods closed their eyes in fear, V\'e5tr\'e4sura, taking up hi
s trident and making the earth tremble with his great strength, trampled the demigods beneath his feet on the battlefield the way a mad elephant tramples hollow bamboos in the forest.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.9 - Seeing V\'e5tr\'e4sura's disposition, Indra, the King of heaven, became intolerant and threw at him one of his great clubs, which are extremely difficult to counteract. However, as the club flew toward him, V\'e5tr\'e4
sura easily caught it with his left hand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.10 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, the powerful V\'e5tr\'e4sura, the enemy of
 King Indra, angrily struck the head of Indra's elephant with that club, making a tumultuous sound on the battlefield. For this heroic deed, the soldiers on both sides glorified him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.11 - Struck with the club by V\'e5tr\'e4sura like a mountain struck by a thunderbolt, the elephant Air\'e4
vata, feeling great pain and spitting blood from its broken mouth, was pushed back fourteen yards. In great distress, the elephant fell, with Indra on its back.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.12 - When he saw Indra's carrier elephant thus fatigued and injured and when he saw Indra morose because his carrier had been harmed in that way, the great soul V\'e5tr\'e4
sura, following religious principles, refrained from again striking Indra with the club. Taking this opportunity, Indra touched the elephant wi
th his nectar-producing hand, thus relieving the animal's pain and curing its injuries. Then the elephant and Indra both stood silently.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.13 - O King, when the great hero V\'e5tr\'e4sura saw Indra, his enemy, the killer of his brother, standing before him with a thunderbolt in his hand, desiring to fight, V\'e5tr\'e4
sura remembered how Indra had cruelly killed his brother. Thinking of Indra's sinful activities, he became mad with lamentation and forgetfulness. Laughing sarcastically, he spoke as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.14 - \'c7r\'e9 V\'e5tr\'e4sura said: He who has killed a br\'e4hma\'eb
a, he who has killed his spiritual master-indeed, he who has killed my brother-is now, by good fortune, standing before me face to face as my enemy. O most abominable one, when I pierce your stonelike 
heart with my trident, I shall be freed from my debt to my brother.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.15 - Only for the sake of living in the heavenly planets, you killed my elder brother-a self-realized, sinless, qualified br\'e4hma\'eba who had been appointed your chief priest. He was
 your spiritual master, but although you entrusted him with the performance of your sacrifice, you later mercilessly severed his heads from his body the way one butchers an animal.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.16 - Indra, you are bereft of all shame, mercy, glory and good fortune. Deprived of these good qualities by the reactions of your fruitive activities, you are to be condemned even by the man-eaters [R\'e4k\'f1
asas]. Now I shall pierce your body with my trident, and after you die with great pain, even fire will not touch you; only the vultures will eat your body.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.17 - You are naturally cruel. If the other demigods, unaware of my prowess, follow you by attacking me with raised weapons, I shall sever their heads with this sharp trident. With those heads I shall perform a 
sacrifice to Bhairava and the other leaders of the ghosts, along with their hordes.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.18 - But if in this battle you cut off my head with your thunderbolt and kill my soldiers, O Indra, O great hero, I shall take great pleasure in offering my body t
o other living entities [such as jackals and vultures]. I shall thus be relieved of my obligations to the reactions of my karma, and my fortune will be to receive the dust from the lotus feet of great devotees like N\'e4rada Muni.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.19 - O King of the 
demigods, since I, your enemy, am standing before you, why don't you hurl your thunderbolt at me? Although your attack upon me with your club was certainly useless, like a request of money from a miser, the thunderbolt you carry will not be useless. You n
eed have no doubts about this.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.20 - O Indra, King of heaven, the thunderbolt you carry to kill me has been empowered by the prowess of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and the strength of Dadh\'e9
ci's austerities. Since you have come here to kill me in accordance with Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's order, there is no doubt that I shall be killed by the release of your thunderbolt. Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u has sided with you. Therefore your victory, opulence and all good qualities are assured.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.21 - By the force of your thunderbolt, I shall be freed of material bondage and shall give up this body and this world of material desires. Fixing my mind upon the lotus feet of Lord Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eb
a, I shall attain the destination of such great sages as N\'e4rada Muni, just as Lord Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eba has said.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.22 - 
Persons who fully surrender at the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and always think of His lotus feet are accepted and recognized by the Lord as His own personal assistants or servants. The Lord never bestows upon such servants the brilli
a
nt opulences of the upper, lower and middle planetary systems of this material world. When one possesses material opulence in any of these three divisions of the universe, his possessions naturally increase his enmity, anxiety, mental agitation, pride and
 belligerence. Thus one goes through much endeavor to increase and maintain his possessions, and he suffers great unhappiness when he loses them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.23 - Our Lord, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, forbids His devotees to endeavor uselessly for reli
gion, economic development and sense gratification. O Indra, one can thus infer how kind the Lord is. Such mercy is obtainable only by unalloyed devotees, not by persons who aspire for material gains.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.24 - O my Lord, O Supreme Personality of Godhe
ad, will I again be; able to be a servant of Your eternal servants who find shelter only at Your lotus feet? O Lord of my life, may I again become their servant so that my mind may always think of Your transcendental attributes, my words always glorify th
ose attributes, and my body always engage in the loving service of Your Lordship?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.25 - O my Lord, source of all opportunities, I do not desire to enjoy in Dhruvaloka, the heavenly planets or the planet where Lord Brahm\'e4 resides, nor do I want to be
 the supreme ruler of all the earthly planets or the lower planetary systems. I do not desire to be master of the powers of mystic yoga, nor do I want liberation if I have to give up Your lotus feet.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.26 - O lotus-eyed Lord, as baby birds that have
 not yet developed their wings always look for their mother to return and feed them, as small calves tied with ropes await anxiously the time of milking, when they will be allowed to drink the milk of their mothers, or as a morose wife whose husband is aw
ay from home always longs for him to return and satisfy her in all respects, I always yearn for the opportunity to render direct service unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.11.27 - O my Lord, my master, I am wandering throughout this material world as a result of my fruitive a
ctivities. Therefore I simply seek friendship in the association of Your pious and enlightened devotees. My attachment to my body, wife, children and home is continuing by the spell of Your external energy, but I wish to be attached to them no longer. Let
 my mind, my consciousness and everything I have be attached only to You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Translations 1-27
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.1 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Desiring to give up his body, V\'e5tr\'e4sura considered death in the battle preferable to victory. O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, he vigorously took up his trident 
and with great force attacked Lord Indra, the King of heaven, just as Kai\'f6abha had forcefully attacked the Supreme Personality of Godhead when the universe was inundated.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.2 - Then V\'e5tr\'e4sura, the great hero of the demons, whirled his trident, which
 had points like the flames of the blazing fire at the end of the millennium. With great force and anger he threw it at Indra, roaring and exclaiming loudly, "O sinful one, thus shall I kill you!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.3 - Flying in the sky, V\'e5tr\'e4sura's trident resembl
ed a brilliant meteor. Although the blazing weapon was difficult to look upon, King Indra, unafraid, cut it to pieces with his thunderbolt. Simultaneously, he cut off one of V\'e5tr\'e4sura's arms, which was as thick as the body of V\'e4
suki, the King of the serpents.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.4 - Although one of his arms was severed from his body, V\'e5tr\'e4
sura angrily approached King Indra and struck him on the jaw with an iron mace. He also struck the elephant that carried Indra. Thus Indra dropped the thunderbolt from his hand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.5 - The denizens of various planets, like the demigods, demons, C\'e4ra\'ebas and Siddhas, praised V\'e5tr\'e4sura's deed, but when they observed that Indra was in great danger, they lamented, "Alas! Alas!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.6 - Having dropped the thunderbolt from his hand in the presence of his enemy, Indra was practically defeated and was very much ashamed. He dared not pick up his weapon again. V\'e5tr\'e4
sura, however, encouraged him, saying, "Take up your thunderbolt and kill your enemy. This is not the time to lament your fate."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.7 - V\'e5tr\'e4sura continued: O Indra, no one is guaranteed of being always victorious but the original enjoyer, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Bhagav\'e4
n. He is the cause of creation, maintenance and annihilation, and He knows everything. Being dependent and being obliged to accept material bodies, belligerent subordinates are sometimes victorious and sometimes defeated.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.8 - All living beings in all the planets of this universe, including the presiding deities of all the planets, are fully under the control of the Lord. They work like birds caught in a net, who cannot move independently.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.9 - Our sensory prowess, mental power, bodily strength, living force, immortality and mortality are all subject to the superintendence of th
e Supreme Personality of Godhead. Not knowing this, foolish people think the dull material body to be the cause of their activities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.10 - O King Indra, as a wooden doll that looks like a woman or as an animal made of grass and leaves cannot move o
r dance independently, but depends fully on the person who handles it, all of us dance according to the desire of the supreme controller, the Personality of Godhead. No one is independent.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.11 - The three puru\'f1as-K\'e4ra\'ebodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu, Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu and K\'f1\'e9rodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9-Vi\'f1\'eb
u-the material nature, the total material energy, the false ego, the five material elements, the material senses, the mind, the intelligence and consciousness cannot create the material manifestation without the direction of t
he Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.12 - A foolish, senseless person cannot understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Although always dependent, he falsely thinks himself the Supreme. If one thinks, "According to one's previous fruitive action
s, one's material body is created by the father and mother, and the same body is annihilated by another agent, as another animal is devoured by a tiger," this is not proper understanding. The Supreme Personality of Godhead Himself creates and devours the 
living beings through other living beings.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.13 - Just as a person not inclined to die must nonetheless give up his longevity, opulence, fame and everything else at the time of death, so, at the appointed time of victory, one can gain all these when 
the Supreme Lord awards them by His mercy.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.14 - Since everything is dependent on the supreme will of the Personality of Godhead, one should be equipoised in fame and defamation, victory and defeat, life and death. In their effects, represented as 
happiness and distress, one should maintain oneself in equilibrium, without anxiety.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.15 - One who knows that the three qualities-goodness, passion and ignorance-are not qualities of the soul but qualities of material nature, and who knows that the
 pure soul is simply an observer of the actions and reactions of these qualities, should be understood to be a liberated person. He is not bound by these qualities.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.16 - O my enemy, just look at me. I have already been defeated, for my weapon and 
arm have been cut to pieces. You have already overwhelmed me, but nonetheless, with a desire to kill you, I am trying my best to fight. I am not at all morose, even under such adverse conditions. Therefore you should give up your moroseness and continue f
ighting.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.12.17 - O my enemy, consider this battle a gambling match in which our lives are the stakes, the arrows are the dice, and the animals acting as carriers are the game board. No one can understand who will be defeated and who will be victorious
. It all depends on providence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.18 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Hearing the straightforward, instructive words of V\'e5tr\'e4
sura, King Indra praised him and again took the thunderbolt in his hand. Without bewilderment or duplicity, he then smiled and spoke to V\'e5tr\'e4sura as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.19 - Indra said: O great demon, I see by your discrimination and endurance in devotional service, despite your dangerous position, that you are a perfect devotee of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the Supersoul and fr
iend of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.20 - You have surmounted the illusory energy of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, and because of this liberation, you have given up the demoniac mentality and have attained the position of an exalted devotee.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.21 - O V\'e5tr\'e4sura, demons are gene
rally conducted by the mode of passion. Therefore, what a great wonder it is that although you are a demon, you have adopted the mentality of a devotee and have fixed your mind on the Supreme Personality of Godhead, V\'e4
sudeva, who is always situated in pure goodness.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.22 - A person fixed in the devotional service of the Supreme Lord, Hari, the Lord of the highest auspiciousness, swims in the ocean of nectar. For him what is the use of the water in small ditches?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.23 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: V\'e5tr\'e4
sura and King Indra spoke about devotional service even on the battlefield, and then as a matter of duty they again began fighting. My dear King, both of them were great fighters and were equally powerful.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.24 - O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, V\'e5tr\'e4sura, who was completely able to subdue his enemy, took his iron club, whirled it around, aimed it at Indra and then threw it at him with his left hand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.25 - With his thunderbolt named \'c7ataparvan, Indra simultaneously cut to pieces V\'e5tr\'e4sura's club and his remaining hand.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.26 - V\'e5tr\'e4sura, bleeding profusely, his two arms cut off at their roots, looked very beautiful, like a flying mountain whose wings have been cut to pieces by Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.27-29 - V\'e5tr\'e4sura was very powerful in physical s
trength and influence. He placed his lower jaw on the ground and his upper jaw in the sky. His mouth became very deep, like the sky itself, and his tongue resembled a large serpent. With his fearful, deathlike teeth, he seemed to be trying to devour the e
ntire universe. Thus assuming a gigantic body, the great demon V\'e5tr\'e4sura shook even the mountains and began crushing the surface of the earth with his legs, as if he were the Himalayas walking about. He came before Indra and swallowed him and Air
\'e4vata, his carrier, just as a big python might swallow an elephant.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.30 - When the demigods, along with Brahm\'e4, other praj\'e4patis and other great saintly persons, saw that Indra had been swallowed by the demon, they became very morose. "Alas," they lamented. "
What a calamity ! What a calamity !"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.31 - The protective armor of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, which Indra possessed, was identical with N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a Himself, the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Protected by that armor and by his own mystic power, King Indra, although swallowed by V\'e5tr\'e4sura, did not die within the demon's belly.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.32 - With his thunderbolt, King Indra, who was also extremely powerful, pierced through V\'e5tr\'e4sura's abdomen and came out. Indra, the killer of the demon Bala, then immediately cut off V\'e5tr\'e4
sura's head, which was as high as the peak of a mountain.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.33 - Although the thunderbolt revolved around V\'e5tr\'e4sura's neck with great speed, separating his head from his body took one complete year-360 days, the time in which the sun, moon and ot
her luminaries complete a northern and southern journey. Then, at the suitable time for V\'e5tr\'e4sura to be killed, his head fell to the ground.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.12.34 - When V\'e5tr\'e4sura was killed, the Gandharvas and Siddhas in the heavenly planets beat kettledrums in jubilation. With Vedic hymns they celebrated the prowess of Indra, the killer of V\'e5tr\'e4
sura, praising Indra and showering flowers upon him with great pleasure.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
