{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.1 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, who are so charitably disposed, when V\'e5tr\'e4sura was killed, all the presiding deities and everyone else in the three planetary systems 
was immediately pleased and free from trouble-everyone, that is, except Indra.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.2 - Thereafter, the demigods, the great saintly persons, the inhabitants of Pit\'e5loka and Bh\'fctaloka, the demons, the followers of the demigods, and also Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7
iva and the demigods subordinate to Indra all returned to their respective homes. While departing, however, no one spoke to Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.3 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired from \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9: O great sage, what was the reason for Indra's unhappiness? I wish to hear about this. When he killed V\'e5tr\'e4
sura, all the demigods were extremely happy. Why, then, was Indra himself unhappy?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.4 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 answered: When all the great sages and demigods were disturbed by the extraordinary power of V\'e5tr\'e4
sura, they had assembled to ask Indra to kill him. Indra, however, being afraid of killing a br\'e4hma\'eba, declined their request.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.5 - King Indra replied: When I killed Vi\'e7var\'fcpa, I received extensive sinful reactions, but I was favored by the women, land, trees and water, and therefore I was able to divide the sin among them. But now if I kill V
\'e5tr\'e4sura, another br\'e4hma\'eba, how shall I free myself from the sinful reactions?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.6 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Hearing this, the great sages replied to King Indra, "O King of heaven, all good fortune unto you. Do not fear. We shall perform an a\'e7
vamedha sacrifice to release you from any sin you may accrue by killing the br\'e4hma\'eba."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.7 - The \'e5\'f1is continued: O King Indra, by performing an a\'e7vamedha sacrifice and thereby pleasing the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is the Supersoul, Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, the supreme controller, one can be relieved even of the sinful reactions for killing the entire world, not to speak of killing a demon like V\'e5tr\'e4sura.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.8-9 - One who has killed a br\'e4hma\'eba, one who has killed a cow or one who has killed his father, mother or spiritual master can be immediately freed from all sinful reactions simply by chanting the holy name of Lord N
\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Other sinful persons, such as dog-eaters and ca\'eb\'f2\'e4las, who are less than \'e7\'fcdras, can also be freed in this way. But you are a devotee, and we shall help you by performing the great horse sacrifice. If you please Lord N\'e4
r\'e4ya\'eba in that way, why should you be afraid? You will be freed even if you kill the entire universe, including the br\'e4hma\'ebas, not to speak of killing a disturbing demon like V\'e5tr\'e4sura.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.10 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Encouraged by the words of the sages, Indra killed V\'e5tr\'e4sura, and when he was killed the sinful reaction for killing a br\'e4hma\'eba [brahma-haty\'e4
] certainly took shelter of Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.11 - Following the advice of the demigods, Indra killed V\'e5tr\'e4sura, and he suffered because of this sinful killing. Although the other demigods were happy, he could not derive happiness from the killing of V\'e5tr\'e4
sura. Indra's other good qualities, such as tolerance and opulence, could not help him in his grief.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.12-13 - Indra saw personified sinful reaction chasing him, appearing like a ca\'eb\'f2\'e4la woman, 
a woman of the lowest class. She seemed very old, and all the limbs of her body trembled. Because she was afflicted with tuberculosis, her body and garments were covered with blood. Breathing an unbearable fishy odor that polluted the entire street, she c
alled to Indra, "Wait! Wait!"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.14 - O King, Indra first fled to the sky, but there also he saw the woman of personified sin chasing him. This witch followed him wherever he went. At last he very quickly went to the northeast and entered the M\'e4nasa-s
arovara Lake.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.15 - Always thinking of how he could be relieved from the sinful reaction for killing a br\'e4hma\'eb
a, King Indra, invisible to everyone, lived in the lake for one thousand years in the subtle fibers of the stem of a lotus. The fire-god used to bring him his share of all yaj\'ef
as, but because the fire-god was afraid to enter the water, Indra was practically starving.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.16 - As long as King Indra lived in the water, wrapped in the stem of the lotus, Nahu\'f1a was equipped with the ability to rule the heavenly kingdom, due to his knowledge, austerity and mystic power. Nahu\'f1
a, however, blinded and maddened by power and opulence, made undesirable proposals to Indra's wife with a desire to enjoy her. Thus Nahu\'f1a was cursed by a br\'e4hma\'eba and later became a snake.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.17 - Indra's sins were diminished by the influence of Rudra, the demigod of all directions. Because Indra was protected by the goddess of fortune, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's wife, who resides in the lotus clusters of M\'e4
nasa-sarovara Lake, Indra's sins could not affect him. Indra was ultimately relieved of all the reactions of his sinful deeds by strictly worshiping Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu. Then he was called back to the heavenly planets by the br\'e4hma\'eb
as and reinstated in his position.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.18 - O King, when Lord Indra reached the heavenly planets, the saintly br\'e4hma\'ebas approached him and properly initiated him into a horse sacrifice [a\'e7vamedha-yaj\'efa] meant to please the Supreme Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.19-20 - The horse sacrifice performed by the saintly br\'e4hma\'eb
as relieved Indra of the reactions to all his sins because he worshiped the Supreme Personality of Godhead in that sacrifice. O King, although he had committed a gravely sinful act, it was nullified at once by that sacrifice, just as fog is vanquished by 
the brilliant sunrise.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.21 - King Indra was favored by Mar\'e9
ci and the other great sages. They performed the sacrifice just according to the rules and regulations, worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the Supersoul, the original person. Thu
s Indra regained his exalted position and was again honored by everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.13.22-23 - In this very great narrative there is glorification of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, there are statements about the exaltedness of devotional service,
 there are descriptions of devotees like Indra and V\'e5tr\'e4
sura, and there are statements about King Indra's release from sinful life and about his victory in fighting the demons. By understanding this incident, one is relieved of all sinful reactions. Theref
ore the learned are always advised to read this narration. If one does so, one will become expert in the activities of the senses, his opulence will increase, and his reputation will become widespread. One will also be relieved of all sinful reactions, he
 will conquer all his enemies, and the duration of his life will increase. Because this narration is auspicious in all respects, learned scholars regularly hear and repeat it on every festival day.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
