\b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.1 - \'c7r\'e9la \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 said: After offering obeisances to the direction from which Ananta, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, had disappeared, Citraketu began traveling in outer space as the head of the Vidy\'e4dharas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.2-3 - Being praised by great sages and saints and by the inhabitants of Siddhaloka and C\'e4ra\'ebaloka, Citraketu, the most powerful mystic yog\'e9
, wandered about enjoying life for millions of years. With bodily strength and senses free from deterioration, he traveled within the valleys of Sumeru Mountain, which 
is the place of perfection for various kinds of mystic power. In those valleys he enjoyed life with the women of Vidy\'e4dhara-loka by chanting the glories of the Supreme Lord, Hari.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.4-5 - One time while King Citraketu was traveling in outer space on a brilliantly effulgent airplane given to him by Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, he saw Lord \'c7iva, surrounded by Siddhas and C\'e4ra\'ebas. Lord \'c7
iva was sitting in an assembly of great saintly persons and embracing P\'e4rvat\'e9 on his lap with his arm. Citraketu laughed loudly and spoke, within the hearing of P\'e4rvat\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.6 - Citraketu said: Lord \'c7iva, the spiritual master of the general populace, is the best of all living entities who have accepted material bodies. He enunciates the system of religion. Yet how wonderful it is tha
t he is embracing his wife, P\'e4rvat\'e9, in the midst of an assembly of great saintly persons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.7 - Lord \'c7iva, whose hair is matted on his head, has certainly undergone great austerities and penances. Indeed, he is the president in the assembly of stri
ct followers of Vedic principles. Nonetheless, he is seated with his wife on his lap in the midst of saintly persons and is embracing her as if he were a shameless, ordinary human being.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.8 - Ordinary conditioned persons generally embrace their wives and enjoy their company in solitary places. How wonderful it is that Lord Mah\'e4
deva, although a great master of austerity, is embracing his wife openly in the midst of an assembly of great saints.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.9 - \'c7r\'e9la \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear King, after hearing Citraketu's statement, Lord \'c7
iva, the most powerful personality, whose knowledge is fathomless, simply smiled and remained silent, and all the members of the assembly followed the lord by not saying anything.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.10 - Not knowing the prowess of Lord \'c7iva and P\'e4rvat\'e9, Citraketu strongly criticized them. His statements were not at all pleasing, and therefore the goddess P\'e4rvat\'e9
, being very angry, spoke as follows to Citraketu, who thought himself better than Lord \'c7iva in controlling the senses.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.11 - The goddess P\'e4rvat\'e9
 said: Alas, has this upstart now received a post from which to punish shameless persons like us? Has he been appointed ruler, carrier of the rod of punishment? Is he now the only master of everything?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.12 - Alas, Lord Brahm\'e4, who has taken his birth from the lotus flower, does not know the principles of religion, nor do the great saints like Bh\'e5gu and N\'e4rada, nor the four Kum\'e4ras, headed by Sanat-kum\'e4
ra. Manu and Kapila have also forgotten the religious principles. I suppose it to be because of this that they have not tried to stop Lord \'c7iva from behaving improperly.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.13 - This Citraketu is the lowest of k\'f1atriyas, for he has impudently overridden Brahm\'e4 and the other demigods by insulting Lord \'c7iva, upon whose lotus feet they always meditate. Lord \'c7
iva is personified religion and the spiritual master of the entire world, and therefore Citraketu must be punished.
