 said: After offering obeisances to the direction from which Ananta, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, had disappeared, Citraketu began traveling in outer space as the head of the Vidy\'e4dharas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.2-3 - Being praised by great sages and saints and by the inhabitants of Siddhaloka and C\'e4ra\'ebaloka, Citraketu, the most powerful mystic yog\'e9, wandered about enjoying life for millions of years. With bodily strength
 and senses free from deterioration, he traveled within the valleys of Sumeru Mountain, which is the place of perfection for various kinds of mystic power. In those valleys he enjoyed life with the women of Vidy\'e4
dhara-loka by chanting the glories of the Supreme Lord, Hari.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.4-5 - One time while King Citraketu was traveling in outer space on a brilliantly effulgent airplane given to him by Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, he saw Lord \'c7iva, surrounded by Siddhas and C\'e4ra\'ebas. Lord \'c7
iva was sitting in an assembly of great saintly persons and embracing P\'e4rvat\'e9 on his lap with his arm. Citraketu laughed loudly and spoke, within the hearing of P\'e4rvat\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.6 - Citraketu said: Lord \'c7iva, the spiritual master of the general populace, is the best of all living entities who ha
ve accepted material bodies. He enunciates the system of religion. Yet how wonderful it is that he is embracing his wife, P\'e4rvat\'e9, in the midst of an assembly of great saintly persons.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.7 - Lord \'c7iva, whose hair is matted on his head, has certainly
 undergone great austerities and penances. Indeed, he is the president in the assembly of strict followers of Vedic principles. Nonetheless, he is seated with his wife on his lap in the midst of saintly persons and is embracing her as if he were a shamele
ss, ordinary human being.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.8 - Ordinary conditioned persons generally embrace their wives and enjoy their company in solitary places. How wonderful it is that Lord Mah\'e4
deva, although a great master of austerity, is embracing his wife openly in the midst of an assembly of great saints.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.9 - \'c7r\'e9la \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear King, after hearing Citraketu's statement, Lord \'c7
iva, the most powerful personality, whose knowledge is fathomless, simply smiled and remained silent, and all the members of the assembly followed the lord by not saying anything.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.10 - Not knowing the prowess of Lord \'c7iva and P\'e4rvat\'e9, Citraketu strongly criticized them. His statements were not at all pleasing, and therefore the goddess P\'e4rvat\'e9, being very angr
y, spoke as follows to Citraketu, who thought himself better than Lord \'c7iva in controlling the senses.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.11 - The goddess P\'e4rvat\'e9 said: Alas, has this upstart now received a post from which to punish shameless persons like us? Has he been appointed 
ruler, carrier of the rod of punishment? Is he now the only master of everything?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.12 - Alas, Lord Brahm\'e4, who has taken his birth from the lotus flower, does not know the principles of religion, nor do the great saints like Bh\'e5gu and N\'e4rada, nor the four Kum\'e4ras, headed by Sanat-kum\'e4
ra. Manu and Kapila have also forgotten the religious principles. I suppose it to be because of this that they have not tried to stop Lord \'c7iva from behaving improperly.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.13 - This Citraketu is the lowest of k\'f1atriyas, for he has impudently overridden Brahm\'e4 and the other demigods by insulting Lord \'c7iva, upon whose lotus feet they always meditate. Lord \'c7
iva is personified religion and the spiritual master of the entire world, and therefore Citraketu must be punished.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.14 - This person is puffed up because of his achievements, thinking, "I am the best." He does not deserve to approach the shelter of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u's lotus feet, which are worshiped by all saintly persons, for he is impudent, thinking himself greatly important.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.15 - O impudent one, my dear son, now take birth in a low, sinful family of demons so that you will not commit such an offense again toward exalted, saintly persons in this world.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.16 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, when Citraketu was cursed by P\'e4rvat\'e9, he descended from his airplane, bowed before her with great humility and pleased her completely.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.17 - Citraketu said: My dear mother, with my own hands folded together I accept the curse upon me. I do not mind the curse, for happiness and distress are given by the demigods as a result of one's past deeds.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.18 - Deluded by ignorance, the living entity wanders in the forest of this material world, enjoying the happiness and distress resu
lting from his past deeds, everywhere and at all times. [Therefore, my dear mother, neither you nor I am to be blamed for this incident.]
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.19 - In this material world, neither the living entity himself nor others [friends and enemies] are the cause
 of material happiness and distress. But because of gross ignorance, the living entity thinks that he and others are the cause.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.20 - This material world resembles the waves of a constantly flowing river. Therefore, what is a curse and what is a fa
vor? What are the heavenly planets, and what are the hellish planets? What is actually happiness, and what is actually distress? Because the waves flow constantly, none of them has an eternal effect.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.21 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is one.
 Unaffected by the conditions of the material world, He creates all the conditioned souls by His own personal potency. Because of being contaminated by the material energy, the living entity is put into ignorance and thus into different conditions of bond
age. Sometimes, by knowledge, the living entity is given liberation. In sattva-gu\'eba and rajo-gu\'eba, he is subjected to happiness and distress.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.22 - The Supreme Personality of Godhead is equally disposed toward all living entities. Therefore no one i
s very dear to Him, and no one is a great enemy for Him; no one is His friend, and no one is His relative. Being unattached to the material world, He has no affection for so-called happiness or hatred for so-called distress. The two terms happiness and di
stress are relative. Since the Lord is always happy, for Him there is no question of distress.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.23 - Although the Supreme Lord is unattached to our happiness and distress according to karma, and although no one is His enemy or favorite, He creates p
ious and impious activities through the agency of His material potency. Thus for the continuation of the materialistic way of life He creates happiness and distress, good fortune and bad, bondage and liberation, birth and death.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.24 - O mother, you
 are now unnecessarily angry, but since all my happiness and distress are destined by my past activities, I do not plead to be excused or relieved from your curse. Although what I have said is not wrong, please let whatever you think is wrong be pardoned.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.25 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, subduer of the enemy, after Citraketu satisfied Lord \'c7iva and his wife, P\'e4rvat\'e9
, he boarded his airplane and left as they looked on. When Lord \'c7iva and P\'e4rvat\'e9 saw that Citraketu, although informed of the curse, was unafraid, they smiled, being fully astonished by his behavior.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.26 - Thereafter, in the presence of the great sage N\'e4rada, the demons, the inhabitants of Siddhaloka, and his personal associates, Lord \'c7iva, who is most powerful, spoke to his wife, P\'e4rvat\'e9
, while they all listened.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.27 - Lord \'c7iva said: My dear beautiful P\'e4rvat\'e9, have you seen the greatness of the Vai\'f1\'ebavas? Being servants of the servants of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Hari, they are great souls 
and are not interested in any kind of material happiness.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.28 - Devotees solely engaged in the devotional service of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, never fear any condition of life. For them the heavenly planets, liberation and the h
ellish planets are all the same, for such devotees are interested only in the service of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.29 - Because of the actions of the Supreme Lord's external energy, the living entities are conditioned in contact with material bodies. The dualitie
s of happiness and distress, birth and death, curses and favors, are natural by-products of this contact in the material world.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.30 - As one mistakenly considers a flower garland to be a snake or experiences happiness and distress in a dream, so, i
n the material world, by a lack of careful consideration, we differentiate between happiness and distress, considering one good and the other bad.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.31 - Persons engaged in devotional service to Lord V\'e4sudeva, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, have naturally perfect knowledge
 and detachment from this material world. Therefore such devotees are not interested in the so-called happiness or so-called distress of this world.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.32 - Neither I [Lord \'c7iva], nor Brahm\'e4, nor the A\'e7vin\'e9-kum\'e4ras, nor N\'e4rada or the other great sages who are Brahm\'e4
's sons, nor even the demigods can understand the pastimes and personality of the Supreme Lord. Although we are part of the Supreme Lord, we consider ourselves independent, separate controllers, and thus we cannot understand His identity.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.17.33 - He holds no one as very dear and no one as inimical. He has no one for His own relative, and no one is alien to Him. He is actually the soul of the soul of all living entities. Thus He is the auspicious friend of all living beings and is very
 near and dear to all of them.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.34-35 - This magnanimous Citraketu is a dear devotee of the Lord. He is equal to all living entities and is free from attachment and hatred. Similarly, I am also very dear to Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a. Therefore, no one should be astonished to see the activities of the most exalted devotees of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, for they are free from attachment and envy. They are always peaceful, and they are equal to everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.36 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O King, after hearing this speech by her husband, the demigoddess [Um\'e4, the wife of Lord \'c7
iva] gave up her astonishment at the behavior of King Citraketu and became steady in intelligence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.37 - The great devotee Citraketu was so powerful that he was quite competent to curse mother P\'e4rvat\'e9 in retaliation, but instead of doing so he very humbly accepted the curse and bowed his head before Lord \'c7
iva and his wife. This is very much to be appreciated as the standard behavior of a Vai\'f1\'ebava.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.38 - Being cursed by mother Durg\'e4 [Bhav\'e4n\'e9, the wife of Lord \'c7
iva], that same Citraketu accepted birth in a demoniac species of life. Although still fully equipped with transcendental knowledge and practical application of that knowledge in life, he appeared as a demon at the fire sacrifice performed by Tva\'f1\'f6
\'e4, and thus he became famous as V\'e5tr\'e4sura.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.39 - My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, you inquired from me how V\'e5tr\'e4sura, a great devotee, took birth in a demoniac family. Thus I have tried to explain to you everything about this.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.40 - Citraketu was a great devotee [mah\'e4tm\'e4]. If one hears this history of Citraketu from a pure devotee, the listener also is freed from the conditional life of material existence.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.17.41 - One who rises from bed early in the morning and recites this history 
of Citraketu, controlling his words and mind and remembering the Supreme Personality of Godhead, will return home, back to Godhead, without difficulty.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Translations 1-41
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.1 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: P\'e5\'e7ni, who was the wife of Savit\'e4, the fifth of the twelve sons of Aditi, gave birth to three daughters-S\'e4vitr\'e9, Vy\'e4h\'e5ti and Tray\'e9
-and the sons named Agnihotra, Pa\'e7u, Soma, C\'e4turm\'e4sya and the five Mah\'e4yaj\'efas.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.2 - O King, Siddhi, who was the wife of Bhaga, the sixth son of Aditi, bore three sons, named Mahim\'e4, Vibhu and Prabhu, and one extremely beautiful daughter, whose name was \'c4\'e7\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.3-4 - Dh\'e4t\'e4, the seventh son of Aditi, had four wives, named Kuh\'fc, Sin\'e9v\'e4l\'e9, R\'e4k\'e4 and Anumati. These wives begot four sons, named S\'e4yam, Dar\'e7a, Pr\'e4ta\'f9 and P\'fcr\'ebam\'e4sa resp
ectively. The wife of Vidh\'e4t\'e4, the eighth son of Aditi, was named Kriy\'e4. In her Vidh\'e4t\'e4 begot the five fire-gods named the Pur\'e9\'f1yas. The wife of Varu\'eba, the ninth son of Aditi, was named Car\'f1a\'eb\'e9. Bh\'e5gu, the son of Brahm
\'e4, took birth again in her womb.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.5 - By the semen of Varu\'eba, the great mystic V\'e4lm\'e9ki took birth from an anthill. Bh\'e5gu and V\'e4lm\'e9ki were specific sons of Varu\'eba, whereas Agastya and Vasi\'f1\'f6ha \'c5\'f1is were the common sons of Varu
\'eba and Mitra, the tenth son of Aditi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.6 - Upon seeing Urva\'e7\'e9, the celestial society girl, both Mitra and Varu\'eba discharged semen, which they preserved in an earthen pot. The two sons Agastya and Vasi\'f1\'f6
ha later appeared from that pot, and they are therefore the common sons of Mitra and Varu\'eba. Mitra begot three sons in the womb of his wife, whose name was Revat\'e9. Their names were Utsarga, Ari\'f1\'f6a and Pippala.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.7 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, Indra, the King of the heavenly planets and eleventh son of Aditi, begot three sons, named Jayanta, \'c5\'f1abha and M\'e9\'f2hu\'f1a, in the womb of his wife, Paulom\'e9. Thus we have heard.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.8 - By His own potency, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who has multifarious potencies, appeared in the form of a dwarf as Urukrama, the twelfth son of Aditi. In the womb of His wife, whose name was K\'e9
rti, He begot one son, named B\'e5hat\'e7loka, who had many sons, headed by Saubhaga.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.9 - Later [in the Eighth Canto of \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam] I shall describe how Urukrama, Lord V\'e4manadeva, appeared as the son of the great sage Ka\'e7yapa and how He
 covered the three worlds with three steps. I shall describe the uncommon activities He performed, His qualities, His power and how He took birth from the womb of Aditi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.10 - Now let me describe the sons of Diti, who were begotten by Ka\'e7yapa but who became demons. In this demoniac family the great devotee Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja appeared, and Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja also appeared in that family. The demons are technically known as Daityas because they proceeded from the womb of Diti.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.11 - First the two sons named Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu and Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a took birth from Diti's womb. Both of them were very powerful and were worshiped by the Daityas and D\'e4navas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.12-13 - The wife of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was known as Kay\'e4dhu. She was the daughter of Jambha and a descendant of Danu. She gave birth to four consecutive sons, known as Sa\'e0hl\'e4da, Anuhl\'e4da, Hl\'e4da and Prahl\'e4
da. The sister of these four sons was known as Si\'e0hik\'e4. She married the demon named Vipracit and gave birth to another demon, named R\'e4hu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.14 - While R\'e4hu, in disguise, was drinking nectar among the demigods, the Supreme Personality of Godhead severed his head. The wife of Sa\'e0hl\'e4da was named K\'e5ti. By union with Sa\'e0hl\'e4da, K\'e5
ti gave birth to a son named Pa\'efcajana.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.15 - The wife of Hl\'e4da was named Dhamani. She gave birth to two sons, named V\'e4t\'e4pi and Ilvala. When Agastya Muni became Ilvala's guest, Ilvala served him a feast by cooking V\'e4t\'e4
pi, who was in the shape of a ram.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.16 - The wife of Anuhl\'e4da was named S\'fcry\'e4. She gave birth to two sons, named B\'e4\'f1kala and Mahi\'f1a. Prahl\'e4da had one son, Virocana, whose wife gave birth to Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.17 - Thereafter, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja begot one hundred sons in the womb of A\'e7an\'e4. Of these one hundred sons, King B\'e4\'eba was the eldest. The activities of Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, which are very laudable, will be described later [in the Eighth Canto].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.18 - Since King B\'e4\'eba was a great worshiper of Lord \'c7iva, he became one of Lord \'c7iva's most celebrated associates. Even now, Lord \'c7iva protects King B\'e4\'eba's capital and always stands beside him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.19 - The forty-nine Marut demigods were also born from the womb of Diti. None of them had sons. Although they were born of Diti, King Indra gave them a position as demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.20 - King Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired: 
My dear lord, due to their birth, the forty-nine Maruts must have been obsessed with a demoniac mentality. Why did Indra, the King of heaven, convert them into demigods? Did they perform any rituals or pious activities?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.21 - My dear br\'e4hma\'eba, I and all the sages present with me are eager to know about this. Therefore, O great soul, kindly explain to us the reason.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.22 - \'c7r\'e9 S\'fcta Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O great sage \'c7aunaka, after hearing Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it speak respectfully and briefly on topics essential to hear, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, who was well aware of everything, praised his endeavor with great pleasure and replied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.23 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Just to help Indra, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu killed the two brothers Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu. Because o
f their being killed, their mother, Diti, overwhelmed with lamentation and anger, contemplated as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.24 - Lord Indra, who is very much fond of sense gratification, has killed the two brothers Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu by means of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Therefore Indra is cruel, hardhearted and sinful. When will I, having killed him, rest with a pacified mind?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.25 - When dead, the bodies of all the rulers known as kings and great leaders will be transformed into worms, stool or ashes. If one e
nviously kills others for the protection of such a body, does he actually know the true interest of life? Certainly he does not, for if one is envious of other entities, he surely goes to hell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.26 - Diti thought: Indra considers his body eternal, and thus he has become unrestrained. I therefore wish to have a son who can remove Indra's madness. Let me adopt some means to help me in this.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.27-28 - Thinking in this way [with a desire for a son to kill Indra], Diti began constantly acting to satisfy Ka\'e7yapa by her pleasing behavior. O King, Diti always carried out Ka\'e7
yapa's orders very faithfully, as he desired. With service, love, humility and control, with words spoken very sweetly to satisfy her husband, and with smiles and glances at him, Diti attracted his mind and brought it under her control.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.29 - Although Ka\'e7yapa Muni was a learned scholar, he was captivated by Diti's artificial behavior, which brought him under her control. Therefore he assured his wife that he would fulfill he
r desires. Such a promise by a husband is not at all astonishing.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.30 - In the beginning of creation, Lord Brahm\'e4, the father of the living entities of the universe, saw that all the living entities were unattached. To increase population, he then 
created woman from the better half of man's body, for woman's behavior carries away a man's mind.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.31 - O my dear one, the most powerful sage Ka\'e7yapa, being extremely pleased by the mild behavior of his wife Diti, smiled and spoke to her as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.32 - Ka\'e7
yapa Muni said: O beautiful woman, O irreproachable lady, since I am very much pleased by your behavior, you may ask me for any benediction you want. If a husband is pleased, what desires are difficult for his wife to obtain, either in t
his world or in the next?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.33-34 - A husband is the supreme demigod for a woman. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord V\'e4sudeva, the husband of the goddess of fortune, is situated in everyone's heart and is worshiped through the various names an
d forms of the demigods by fruitive workers. Similarly, a husband represents the Lord as the object of worship for a woman.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.35 - My dear wife, whose body is so beautiful, your waist being thin, a conscientious wife should be chaste and should abide by the orders of her husband. She should very devoutly worship her husband as a representative of V
\'e4sudeva.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.36 - My dear gentle wife, because you have worshiped me with great devotion, considering me a representative of the Supreme Personality o
f Godhead, I shall reward you by fulfilling your desires, which are unobtainable for an unchaste wife.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.37 - Diti replied: O my husband, O great soul, I have now lost my sons. If you want to give me a benediction, I ask you for an immortal son who can kill Indra. I pray for this because Indra, with the help of Vi\'f1\'eb
u, has killed my two sons Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.38 - Upon hearing Diti's request, Ka\'e7yapa Muni was very much aggrieved. "Alas," he lamented, "now I face the danger of the impious act of killing Indra."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.39 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni thought: Alas, I have now become too attached to material enjoyment. Taking advantage of this, my mind has been attracted by the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the form of 
a woman [my wife]. Therefore I am surely a wretched person who will glide down toward hell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.40 - This woman, my wife, has adopted a means that follows her nature, and therefore she is not to be blamed. But I am a man. Therefore, all condemnation u
pon me! I am not at all conversant with what is good for me, since I could not control my senses.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.41 - A woman's face is as attractive and beautiful as a blossoming lotus flower during autumn. Her words are very sweet, and they give pleasure to th
e ear, but if we study a woman's heart, we can understand it to be extremely sharp, like the blade of a razor. In these circumstances, who could understand the dealings of a woman?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.42 - To satisfy their own interests, women deal with men as if the
 men were most dear to them, but no one is actually dear to them. Women are supposed to be very saintly, but for their own interests they can kill even their husbands, sons or brothers, or cause them to be killed by others.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.43 - I promised to give her a benediction, and this promise cannot be violated, but Indra does not deserve to be killed. In these circumstances, the solution I have is quite suitable.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.44 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Ka\'e7yapa Muni, thinking in this way, became somewhat angry. Condemning himself, O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, descendant of Kuru, he spoke to Diti as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.45 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni said: My dear gentle wife, if you follow my instructions regarding this vow for at least one year, you will surely get a son who will 
be able to kill Indra. However, if you deviate from this vow of following the Vai\'f1\'ebava principles, you will get a son who will be favorable to Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.46 - Diti replied: My dear br\'e4hma\'eba, I must accept your advice and follow the vow. Now let me understand what I have to do, what is forbidden and what will not break the vow. Please clearly state all this to me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.47 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni said: My dear wife, to follow this vow, do not be violent or cause harm to anyone. Do not curse anyone, and do not
 speak lies. Do not cut your nails and hair, and do not touch impure things like skulls and bones.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.48 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: My dear gentle wife, never enter the water while bathing, never be angry, and do not even speak or associate with wicke
d people. Never wear clothes that have not been properly washed, and do not put on a garland that has already been worn.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.49 - Never eat leftover food, never eat pras\'e4da offered to the goddess K\'e4l\'e9 [Durg\'e4], and do not eat anything contaminated by flesh or fish. Do not eat anything brought or touched by a \'e7\'fc
dra nor anything seen by a woman in her menstrual period. Do not drink water by joining your palms.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.50 - After eating, you should not go out to the street without having washed your mouth
, hands and feet. You should not go out in the evening or with your hair loose, nor should you go out unless you are properly decorated with ornaments. You should not leave the house unless you are very grave and are sufficiently covered.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.51 - You
 should not lie down without having washed both of your feet or without being purified, nor with wet feet or with your head pointed west or north. You should not lie naked, or with other women, or during the sunrise or sunset.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.52 - Putting on washed clothing, being always pure and being adorned with turmeric, sandalwood pulp and other auspicious items, before breakfast one should worship the cows, the br\'e4hma\'eb
as, the goddess of fortune and the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.53 - With flowe
r garlands, sandalwood pulp, ornaments and other paraphernalia, a woman following this vow should worship women who have sons and whose husbands are living. The pregnant wife should worship her husband and offer him prayers. She should meditate upon him, 
thinking that he is situated in her womb.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.54 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: If you perform this ceremony called pu\'e0savana, adhering to the vow with faith for at least one year, you will give birth to a son destined to kill Indra. But if there is any dis
crepancy in the discharge of this vow, the son will be a friend to Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.55 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, Diti, the wife of Ka\'e7yapa, agreed to undergo the purificatory process known as pu\'e0savana. "Yes," she said, "I shall do everything according to your ins
tructions." With great jubilation she became pregnant, having taken semen from Ka\'e7yapa, and faithfully began discharging the vow.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.56 - O King, who are respectful to everyone, Indra understood Diti's purpose, and thus he contrived to fulfill his ow
n interests. Following the logic that self-preservation is the first law of nature, he wanted to break Diti's promise. Thus he engaged himself in the service of Diti, his aunt, who was residing in an \'e4\'e7rama.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.57 - Indra served his aunt daily by bringing flowers, fruits, roots and wood for yaj\'efas from the forest. He also brought ku\'e7a grass, leaves, sprouts, earth and water exactly at the proper time.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.58 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, as the hunter of a deer becomes like a deer by covering his body with 
deerskin and serving the deer, so Indra, although at heart the enemy of the sons of Diti, became outwardly friendly and served Diti in a faithful way. Indra's purpose was to cheat Diti as soon as he could find some fault in the way she discharged the vows
 of the ritualistic ceremony. However, he wanted to be undetected, and therefore he served her very carefully.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.59 - O master of the entire world, when Indra could find no faults, he thought, "How will there be good fortune for me?" Thus he was full of deep anxiety.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.60 - Having grown weak and thin because of strictly following the principles of the vow, Diti once unfortunately neglected to wash her mouth, hands and feet after eating and went to sleep during the evening twilight.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.61 - Finding this fault, Indra, who has all the mystic powers [the yoga-siddhis such as a\'ebim\'e4 and laghim\'e4], entered Diti's womb while she was unconscious, being fast asleep.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.62 - After entering Diti's womb, Indra, with the help of his thunderbolt, cu
t into seven pieces her embryo, which appeared like glowing gold. In seven places, seven different living beings began crying. Indra told them, "Do not cry," and then he cut each of them into seven pieces again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.63 - O King, being very much aggrieved, they pleaded to Indra with folded hands, saying, "Dear Indra, we are the Maruts, your brothers. Why are you trying to kill us?"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.64 - When Indra saw that actually they were his devoted followers, he said to them: If you are all my brothers, you have nothing more to fear from me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.65 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, you were burned by the brahm\'e4stra of A\'e7vatth\'e4m\'e4, but when Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a entered the womb of your mother, you were saved. Similarly, although the one embryo was cut into forty-nine pieces by the thunderbolt of Indra, they were all saved by the mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.66-67 - If one worships the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the original person, even once, he receives the benefit of being promoted to the spiritual world and possessing the same bodily features as Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Diti worshiped Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu for almost one year, adhering to a great vow. Because of such strength in spiritual life, the forty-nine Maruts were born. How, then, is it wond
erful that the Maruts, although born from the womb of Diti, became equal to the demigods by the mercy of the Supreme Lord ?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.68 - Because of worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Diti was completely purified. When she got up from bed, she 
saw her forty-nine sons along with Indra. These forty-nine sons were all as brilliant as fire and were in friendship with Indra, and therefore she was very pleased.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.69 - Thereafter, Diti said to Indra: My dear son, I adhered to this difficult vow just to get a son to kill you twelve \'c4dityas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.70 - I prayed for only one son, but now I see that there are forty-nine. How has this happened? My dear son Indra, if you know, please tell me the truth. Do not try to speak lies.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.71 - Indra r
eplied: My dear mother, because I was grossly blinded by selfish interests, I lost sight of religion. When I understood that you were observing a great vow in spiritual life, I wanted to find some fault in you. When I found such a fault, I entered your wo
mb and cut the embryo to pieces.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.72 - First I cut the child in the womb into seven pieces, which became seven children. Then I cut each of the children into seven pieces again. By the grace of the Supreme Lord, however, none of them died.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.73 - My dear mother, when I saw that all forty-nine sons were alive, I was certainly struck with wonder. I decided that this was a secondary result of your having regularly executed devotional service in worship of Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.74 - Although those who are interested only in worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead do not desire anything material from the Lord and do not even want liberation, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba fulfills all their desires.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.75 - The ultimate goal of all ambitions is to become a s
ervant of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. If an intelligent man serves the most dear Lord, who gives Himself to His devotees, how can he desire material happiness, which is available even in hell?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.76 - O my mother, O best of all women, I am a 
fool. Kindly excuse me for whatever offenses I have committed. Your forty-nine sons have been born unhurt because of your devotional service. As an enemy, I cut them to pieces, but because of your great devotional service they did not die.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.77 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 continued: Diti was extremely satisfied by Indra's good behavior. Then Indra offered his respects to his aunt with profuse obeisances, and with her permission he went away to the heavenly planets with his brothers the Maruts.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.78 - My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1
it, I have replied as far as possible to the questions you have asked me, especially in regard to this pure, auspicious narration about the Maruts. Now you may inquire further, and I shall explain more.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  18. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
\b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.1 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: P\'e5\'e7ni, who was the wife of Savit\'e4
, the fifth of the twelve sons of Aditi, gave birth to three daughters-S\'e4vitr\'e9, Vy\'e4h\'e5ti and Tray\'e9-and the sons named Agnihotra, Pa\'e7u, Soma, C\'e4turm\'e4sya and the five Mah\'e4yaj\'efas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.2 - O King, Siddhi, who was the wife of Bhaga, the sixth son of Aditi, bore three sons, named Mahim\'e4, Vibhu and Prabhu, and one extremely beautiful daughter, whose name was \'c4\'e7\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.3-4 - Dh\'e4t\'e4, the seventh son of Aditi, had four wives, named Kuh\'fc, Sin\'e9v\'e4l\'e9, R\'e4k\'e4 and Anumati. These wives begot four sons, named S\'e4yam, Dar\'e7a, Pr\'e4ta\'f9 and P\'fcr\'ebam\'e4
sa respectively. The wife of Vidh\'e4t\'e4, the eighth son of Aditi, was named Kriy\'e4. In her Vidh\'e4t\'e4 begot the five fire-gods named the Pur\'e9\'f1yas. The wife of Varu\'eba, the ninth son of Aditi, was named Car\'f1a\'eb\'e9. Bh\'e5
gu, the son of Brahm\'e4, took birth again in her womb.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.5 - By the semen of Varu\'eba, the great mystic V\'e4lm\'e9ki took birth from an anthill. Bh\'e5gu and V\'e4lm\'e9ki were specific sons of Varu\'eba, whereas Agastya and Vasi\'f1\'f6ha \'c5\'f1is were the common sons of Varu
\'eba and Mitra, the tenth son of Aditi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.6 - Upon seeing Urva\'e7\'e9, the celestial society girl, both Mitra and Varu\'eba discharged semen, which they preserved in an earthen pot. The two sons Agastya and Vasi\'f1\'f6ha later appeared from that pot, 
and they are therefore the common sons of Mitra and Varu\'eba. Mitra begot three sons in the womb of his wife, whose name was Revat\'e9. Their names were Utsarga, Ari\'f1\'f6a and Pippala.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.7 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, Indra, the King of the heavenly planets and eleventh son of Aditi, begot three sons, named Jayanta, \'c5\'f1abha and M\'e9\'f2hu\'f1a, in the womb of his wife, Paulom\'e9. Thus we have heard.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.8 - By His own potency, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who has multifarious potencies, appeared in the form of a dwarf as Urukrama, the twelfth son of Aditi. In the womb of His wife, whose name was K\'e9
rti, He begot one son, named B\'e5hat\'e7loka, who had many sons, headed by Saubhaga.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.9 - Later [in the Eighth Canto of \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam] I shall describe how Urukrama, Lord V\'e4manadeva, appeared as the son of the great sage Ka\'e7
yapa and how He covered the three worlds with three steps. I shall describe the uncommon activities He performed, His qualities, His power and how He took birth from the womb of Aditi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.10 - Now let me describe the sons of Diti, who were begotten by Ka\'e7yapa but who became demons. In this demoniac family the great devotee Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja appeared, and Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja also appeared in that family. The demons are technically known as Daityas because they proceeded from the womb of Diti.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.11 - First the two sons named Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu and Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a took birth from Diti's womb. Both of them were very powerful and were worshiped by the Daityas and D\'e4navas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.12-13 - The wife of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was known as Kay\'e4dhu. She was the daughter of Jambha and a descendant of Danu. She gave birth to four consecutive sons, known as Sa\'e0hl\'e4da, Anuhl\'e4da, Hl\'e4da and Prahl\'e4
da. The sister of these four sons was known as Si\'e0hik\'e4. She married the demon named Vipracit and gave birth to another demon, named R\'e4hu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.14 - While R\'e4hu, in disguise, was drinking nectar among the demigods, the Supreme Personality of Godhead severed his head. The wife of Sa\'e0hl\'e4da was named K\'e5ti. By union with Sa\'e0hl\'e4da, K\'e5ti gave 
birth to a son named Pa\'efcajana.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.15 - The wife of Hl\'e4da was named Dhamani. She gave birth to two sons, named V\'e4t\'e4pi and Ilvala. When Agastya Muni became Ilvala's guest, Ilvala served him a feast by cooking V\'e4t\'e4
pi, who was in the shape of a ram.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.16 - The wife of Anuhl\'e4da was named S\'fcry\'e4. She gave birth to two sons, named B\'e4\'f1kala and Mahi\'f1a. Prahl\'e4da had one son, Virocana, whose wife gave birth to Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.17 - Thereafter, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja begot one hundred sons in the womb of A\'e7an\'e4. Of these one hundred sons, King B\'e4\'eba was the eldest. The activities of Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, which are very laudable, will be described later [in the Eighth Canto].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.18 - Since King B\'e4\'eba was a great worshiper of Lord \'c7iva, he became one of Lord \'c7iva's most celebrated associates. Even now, Lord \'c7iva protects King B\'e4\'eba's capital and always stands beside him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.19 - The forty-nine Marut demigods were also born from the womb of Diti. None of them had sons. Although they were born of Diti, King Indra gave them a position as demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.20 - King Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired: My dear lord, due to their birth, the forty-nine Maruts must have been obsessed with a demoniac mentality. Why did Indra, the King of heaven, convert them into demigods? Did they perf
orm any rituals or pious activities?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.21 - My dear br\'e4hma\'eba, I and all the sages present with me are eager to know about this. Therefore, O great soul, kindly explain to us the reason.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.22 - \'c7r\'e9 S\'fcta Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O great sage \'c7aunaka, after hearing Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it speak respectfully and briefly on topics essential to hear, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, who was well aware of everything, praised his endeavor with great pleasure and replied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.23 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Just to help Indra, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu killed the two brothers Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu. Because of their being killed, their mother, Diti, overwhelmed with lamentation and anger, contemplated as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.24 - Lord Indra, who is very much fond of sense gratification, has killed the two brothers Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu by means of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Therefore Indra is cruel, hardhearted and sinful. When will I, having killed him, rest with a pacified mind?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.25 - When dead, the bodies of all the rulers known as kings a
nd great leaders will be transformed into worms, stool or ashes. If one enviously kills others for the protection of such a body, does he actually know the true interest of life? Certainly he does not, for if one is envious of other entities, he surely go
es to hell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.26 - Diti thought: Indra considers his body eternal, and thus he has become unrestrained. I therefore wish to have a son who can remove Indra's madness. Let me adopt some means to help me in this.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.27-28 - Thinking in this way [with a desire for a son to kill Indra], Diti began constantly acting to satisfy Ka\'e7yapa by her pleasing behavior. O King, Diti always carried out Ka\'e7
yapa's orders very faithfully, as he desired. With service, love, humility and control, with words spoken very sweetly to satisfy her husband, and with smiles and glances at him, Diti attracted his mind and brought it under her control.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.29 - Although Ka\'e7yapa Muni was a learned scholar, he was captivated by Diti's artificial behavior, which brought him 
under her control. Therefore he assured his wife that he would fulfill her desires. Such a promise by a husband is not at all astonishing.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.30 - In the beginning of creation, Lord Brahm\'e4, the father of the living entities of the universe, saw that 
all the living entities were unattached. To increase population, he then created woman from the better half of man's body, for woman's behavior carries away a man's mind.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.31 - O my dear one, the most powerful sage Ka\'e7yapa, being extremely pleased by the mild behavior of his wife Diti, smiled and spoke to her as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.32 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni said: O beautiful woman, O irreproachable lady, since I am very much pleased by your behavior, you may ask me for any benediction you want. If a husband i
s pleased, what desires are difficult for his wife to obtain, either in this world or in the next?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.33-34 - A husband is the supreme demigod for a woman. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord V\'e4sudeva, the husband of the goddess of fortune, is s
ituated in everyone's heart and is worshiped through the various names and forms of the demigods by fruitive workers. Similarly, a husband represents the Lord as the object of worship for a woman.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.35 - My dear wife, whose body is so beautiful, your waist being thin, a conscientious wife should be chaste and should abide by the orders of her husband. She should very devoutly worship her husband as a representative of V
\'e4sudeva.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.36 - My dear gentle wife, because you have worshiped me with gre
at devotion, considering me a representative of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, I shall reward you by fulfilling your desires, which are unobtainable for an unchaste wife.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.37 - Diti replied: O my husband, O great soul, I have now lost my sons. If you want to give me a benediction, I ask you for an immortal son who can kill Indra. I pray for this because Indra, with the help of Vi\'f1\'eb
u, has killed my two sons Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.38 - Upon hearing Diti's request, Ka\'e7yapa Muni was very much aggrieved. "Alas," he lamented, "now I face the danger of the impious act of killing Indra."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.39 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni thought: Alas, I have now become too attached to material enjoyment. Taking advantage of this, my mind has been attracted by 
the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the form of a woman [my wife]. Therefore I am surely a wretched person who will glide down toward hell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.40 - This woman, my wife, has adopted a means that follows her nature, and therefo
re she is not to be blamed. But I am a man. Therefore, all condemnation upon me! I am not at all conversant with what is good for me, since I could not control my senses.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.41 - A woman's face is as attractive and beautiful as a blossoming lotus flo
wer during autumn. Her words are very sweet, and they give pleasure to the ear, but if we study a woman's heart, we can understand it to be extremely sharp, like the blade of a razor. In these circumstances, who could understand the dealings of a woman?

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 S
B 6.18.42 - To satisfy their own interests, women deal with men as if the men were most dear to them, but no one is actually dear to them. Women are supposed to be very saintly, but for their own interests they can kill even their husbands, sons or brothe
rs, or cause them to be killed by others.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.43 - I promised to give her a benediction, and this promise cannot be violated, but Indra does not deserve to be killed. In these circumstances, the solution I have is quite suitable.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.44 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Ka\'e7yapa Muni, thinking in this way, became somewhat angry. Condemning himself, O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, descendant of Kuru, he spoke to Diti as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.45 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni said: My dear gentle wife, if you follow my instructions rega
rding this vow for at least one year, you will surely get a son who will be able to kill Indra. However, if you deviate from this vow of following the Vai\'f1\'ebava principles, you will get a son who will be favorable to Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.46 - Diti replied: My dear br\'e4hma\'eba, I must accept your advice and follow the vow. Now let me understand what I have to do, what is forbidden and what will not break the vow. Please clearly state all this to me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.47 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni said: My dear wife, to follow this vow, d
o not be violent or cause harm to anyone. Do not curse anyone, and do not speak lies. Do not cut your nails and hair, and do not touch impure things like skulls and bones.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.48 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: My dear gentle wife, never enter the water whi
le bathing, never be angry, and do not even speak or associate with wicked people. Never wear clothes that have not been properly washed, and do not put on a garland that has already been worn.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.49 - Never eat leftover food, never eat pras\'e4da offered to the goddess K\'e4l\'e9 [Durg\'e4], and do not eat anything contaminated by flesh or fish. Do not eat anything brought or touched by a \'e7\'fc
dra nor anything seen by a woman in her menstrual period. Do not drink water by joining your palms.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.50 - After eat
ing, you should not go out to the street without having washed your mouth, hands and feet. You should not go out in the evening or with your hair loose, nor should you go out unless you are properly decorated with ornaments. You should not leave the house
 unless you are very grave and are sufficiently covered.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.51 - You should not lie down without having washed both of your feet or without being purified, nor with wet feet or with your head pointed west or north. You should not lie naked, or with ot
her women, or during the sunrise or sunset.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.52 - Putting on washed clothing, being always pure and being adorned with turmeric, sandalwood pulp and other auspicious items, before breakfast one should worship the cows, the br\'e4hma\'ebas, the goddess of
 fortune and the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.53 - With flower garlands, sandalwood pulp, ornaments and other paraphernalia, a woman following this vow should worship women who have sons and whose husbands are living. The pregnant wife should w
orship her husband and offer him prayers. She should meditate upon him, thinking that he is situated in her womb.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.54 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: If you perform this ceremony called pu\'e0savana, adhering to the vow with faith for at least one year, you
 will give birth to a son destined to kill Indra. But if there is any discrepancy in the discharge of this vow, the son will be a friend to Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.55 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, Diti, the wife of Ka\'e7yapa, agreed to undergo the purificatory process known as pu\'e0
savana. "Yes," she said, "I shall do everything according to your instructions." With great jubilation she became pregnant, having taken semen from Ka\'e7yapa, and faithfully began discharging the vow.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.56 - O King, who are respectful to everyone,
 Indra understood Diti's purpose, and thus he contrived to fulfill his own interests. Following the logic that self-preservation is the first law of nature, he wanted to break Diti's promise. Thus he engaged himself in the service of Diti, his aunt, who w
as residing in an \'e4\'e7rama.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.57 - Indra served his aunt daily by bringing flowers, fruits, roots and wood for yaj\'efas from the forest. He also brought ku\'e7a grass, leaves, sprouts, earth and water exactly at the proper time.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.58 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1i
t, as the hunter of a deer becomes like a deer by covering his body with deerskin and serving the deer, so Indra, although at heart the enemy of the sons of Diti, became outwardly friendly and served Diti in a faithful way. Indra's purpose was to cheat Di
ti as soon as he could find some fault in the way she discharged the vows of the ritualistic ceremony. However, he wanted to be undetected, and therefore he served her very carefully.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.59 - O master of the entire world, when Indra could find no faults, he thought, "How will there be good fortune for me?" Thus he was full of deep anxiety.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.60 - Having grown weak and thin because of strictly following the principles of the vow, Diti once unfortunately neglected to wash her mouth, hands and feet after eating and went to sleep during the evening twilight.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.61 - Finding this fault, Indra, who has all the mystic powers [the yoga-siddhis such as a\'ebim\'e4 and laghim\'e4], entered Diti's womb while she was unconscious, being fast asleep.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.62 
- After entering Diti's womb, Indra, with the help of his thunderbolt, cut into seven pieces her embryo, which appeared like glowing gold. In seven places, seven different living beings began crying. Indra told them, "Do not cry," and then he cut each of 
them into seven pieces again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.63 - O King, being very much aggrieved, they pleaded to Indra with folded hands, saying, "Dear Indra, we are the Maruts, your brothers. Why are you trying to kill us?"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.64 - When Indra saw that actually they were his devoted followers, he said to them: If you are all my brothers, you have nothing more to fear from me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.65 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, you were burned by the brahm\'e4stra of A\'e7vatth\'e4m\'e4, but when Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba entered the womb 
of your mother, you were saved. Similarly, although the one embryo was cut into forty-nine pieces by the thunderbolt of Indra, they were all saved by the mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.66-67 - If one worships the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the original person, even once, he receives the benefit of being promoted to the spiritual world and possessing the same bodily features as Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Diti worshiped Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu for almost one year, adhering to a great vow. Because of such strength 
in spiritual life, the forty-nine Maruts were born. How, then, is it wonderful that the Maruts, although born from the womb of Diti, became equal to the demigods by the mercy of the Supreme Lord ?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.68 - Because of worshiping the Supreme Personality
 of Godhead, Diti was completely purified. When she got up from bed, she saw her forty-nine sons along with Indra. These forty-nine sons were all as brilliant as fire and were in friendship with Indra, and therefore she was very pleased.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.69 - Thereafter, Diti said to Indra: My dear son, I adhered to this difficult vow just to get a son to kill you twelve \'c4dityas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.70 - I prayed for only one son, but now I see that there are forty-nine. How has this happened? My dear son Indra, if you know, please tell me the truth. Do not try to speak lies.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.71 - Indra replied: My dear mother, because I was grossly blinded by selfish interests, I lost sight of religion. When I understood that you were observing a great vow in spiritual life, I wanted
 to find some fault in you. When I found such a fault, I entered your womb and cut the embryo to pieces.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.72 - First I cut the child in the womb into seven pieces, which became seven children. Then I cut each of the children into seven pieces again. By the grace of the Supreme Lord, however, none of them died.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.73 - My dear mother, when I saw that all forty-nine sons were alive, I was certainly struck with wonder. I decided that this was a secondary result of your having regularly executed devotional service in worship of Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.74 - Although those who are interested only in worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead do not desire anything material from the Lord and do not even want liberation, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba fulfills all their desires.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.18.75 - The ultimate goal of all ambitions is to become a servant of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. If an intelligent man serves the most dear Lord, who gives Himself to His devotees, how can he desire material happiness, which is availa
ble even in hell?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.18.76 - O my mother, O best of all women, I am a fool. Kindly excuse me for whatever offenses I have committed. Your forty-nine sons have been born unhurt because of your devotional service. As an enemy, I cut them to pieces, but be
cause of your great devotional service they did not die.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.77 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Diti was extremely satisfied by Indra's good behavior. Then Indra offered his respects to his aunt with profuse obeisances, and with her permission he we
nt away to the heavenly planets with his brothers the Maruts.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.78 - My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, I have replied as far as possible to the questions you have asked me, especially in regard to this pure, auspicious narration about the Maruts. Now you may i
nquire further, and I shall explain more.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\f35\fs28\cf2\insrsid10252087 Diti Vows to Kill King Indra
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat8 {\fs28\cf2\insrsid10252087   \bullet   }{
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {
\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.1 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: P\'e5\'e7ni, who was the wife of Savit\'e4, the fifth of the twelve sons of Aditi, gave birth to three daughters-S\'e4
vitr\'e9, Vy\'e4h\'e5ti and Tray\'e9-and the sons named Agnihotra, Pa\'e7u, Soma, C\'e4turm\'e4sya and the five Mah\'e4yaj\'efas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.2 - O King, Siddhi, who was the wife of Bhaga, the sixth son of Aditi, bore three sons, named Mahim\'e4, Vibhu and Prabhu, and one extremely beautiful daughter, whose name was \'c4\'e7\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.3-4 - Dh\'e4t\'e4, the seventh son of Aditi, had four wives, named Kuh\'fc, Sin\'e9v\'e4l\'e9, R\'e4k\'e4 and Anumati. These wives begot four sons, named S\'e4yam, Dar\'e7a, Pr\'e4ta\'f9 and P\'fcr\'ebam\'e4
sa respectively. The wife of Vidh\'e4t\'e4, the eighth son of Aditi, was named Kriy\'e4. In her Vidh\'e4t\'e4 begot the five fire-gods named the Pur\'e9\'f1yas. The wife of Varu\'eba, the ninth son of Aditi, was named Car\'f1a\'eb\'e9. Bh\'e5
gu, the son of Brahm\'e4, took birth again in her womb.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.5 - By the semen of Varu\'eba, the great mystic V\'e4lm\'e9ki took birth from an anthill. Bh\'e5gu and V\'e4lm\'e9ki were specific sons of Varu\'eba, whereas Agastya and Vasi\'f1\'f6ha \'c5\'f1is were the common sons of Varu
\'eba and Mitra, the tenth son of Aditi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.6 - Upon seeing Urva\'e7\'e9, the celestial society girl, both Mitra and Varu\'eba discharged semen, which they preserved in an earthen pot. The two sons Agastya and Vasi\'f1\'f6
ha later appeared from that pot, and they are therefore the common sons of Mitra and Varu\'eba. Mitra begot three sons in the womb of his wife, whose name was Revat\'e9. Their names were Utsarga, Ari\'f1\'f6a and Pippala.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.7 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, Indra, the King of the heavenly planets and eleventh son of Aditi, begot three sons, named Jayanta, \'c5\'f1abha and M\'e9\'f2hu\'f1a, in the womb of his wife, Paulom\'e9. Thus we have heard.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.8 - By His own potency, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who has multifarious potencies, appeared in the form of a dwarf as Urukrama, the twelfth son of Aditi. In the womb of His wife, whose name was K\'e9
rti, He begot one son, named B\'e5hat\'e7loka, who had many sons, headed by Saubhaga.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.9 - Later [in the Eighth Canto of \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam] I shall describe how Urukrama, Lord V\'e4manadeva, appeared as the son of the great sage Ka\'e7
yapa and how He covered the three worlds with three steps. I shall describe the uncommon activities He performed, His qualities, His power and how He took birth from the womb of Aditi.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.10 - Now let me describe the sons of Diti, who were begotten by Ka\'e7yapa but who became demons. In this demoniac family the great devotee Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja appeared, and Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja also
 appeared in that family. The demons are technically known as Daityas because they proceeded from the womb of Diti.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.11 - First the two sons named Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu and Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a took birth from Diti's womb. Both of them were very powerful and were worshiped by the Daityas and D\'e4navas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.12-13 - The wife of Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu was known as Kay\'e4dhu. She was the daughter of Jambha and a descendant of Danu. She gave birth to four consecutive sons, known as Sa\'e0hl\'e4da, Anuhl\'e4da, Hl\'e4da and Prahl\'e4
da. The sister of these four sons was known as Si\'e0hik\'e4. She married the demon named Vipracit and gave birth to another demon, named R\'e4hu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.14 - While R\'e4hu, in disguise, was drinking nectar among the demigods, the Supreme Personality of Godhead severed his head. The wife of Sa\'e0hl\'e4da was named K\'e5ti. By union with Sa\'e0hl\'e4da, K\'e5
ti gave birth to a son named Pa\'efcajana.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.15 - The wife of Hl\'e4da was named Dhamani. She gave birth to two sons, named V\'e4t\'e4pi and Ilvala. When Agastya Muni became Ilvala's guest, Ilvala served him a feast by cooking V\'e4t\'e4
pi, who was in the shape of a ram.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.16 - The wife of Anuhl\'e4da was named S\'fcry\'e4. She gave birth to two sons, named B\'e4\'f1kala and Mahi\'f1a. Prahl\'e4da had one son, Virocana, whose wife gave birth to Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.17 - Thereafter, Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4ja begot one hundred sons in the womb of A\'e7an\'e4. Of these one hundred sons, King B\'e4\'eba was the eldest. The activities of Bali Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, which are very laudable, will be described later [in the Eighth Canto].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.18 - Since King B\'e4\'eba was a great worshiper of Lord \'c7iva, he became one of Lord \'c7iva's most celebrated associates. Even now, Lord \'c7iva protects King B\'e4\'eba's capital and always stands beside him.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.19 - The forty-nine Marut demigods were also born from the womb of Diti. None of them had sons. Although they were born of Diti, King Indra gave them a position as demigods.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.20 - King Par\'e9k\'f1it inquired: My dear lord, due to their birth, the forty-nine Maruts must have been obsessed with a demoniac mentality. Why
 did Indra, the King of heaven, convert them into demigods? Did they perform any rituals or pious activities?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.21 - My dear br\'e4hma\'eba, I and all the sages present with me are eager to know about this. Therefore, O great soul, kindly explain to us the reason.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.22 - \'c7r\'e9 S\'fcta Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: O great sage \'c7aunaka, after hearing Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it speak respectfully and briefly on topics essential to hear, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, who was well aware of everything, praised his endeavor with great pleasure and replied.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.23 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Just to help Indra, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu killed the two brothers Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7
ipu. Because of their being killed, their mother, Diti, overwhelmed with lamentation and anger, contemplated as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.24 - Lord Indra, who is very much fond of sense gratification, has killed the two brothers Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu by means of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Therefore Indra is cruel, hardhearted and sinful. When will I, having killed him, rest with a pacified mind?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.18.25 - When dead, the bodies of all the rulers known as kings and great leaders will be transformed into worms, stool or ashes. If one enviously kills others for the protection of such a body, does he actually know the true interest of life? Cert
ainly he does not, for if one is envious of other entities, he surely goes to hell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.26 - Diti thought: Indra considers his body eternal, and thus he has become unrestrained. I therefore wish to have a son who can remove Indra's madness. Let me adopt some means to help me in this.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.27-28 - Thinking in this way [with a desire for a son to kill Indra], Diti began constantly acting to satisfy Ka\'e7yapa by her pleasing behavior. O King, Diti always carried out Ka\'e7yapa's orders very faithfully, as 
he desired. With service, love, humility and control, with words spoken very sweetly to satisfy her husband, and with smiles and glances at him, Diti attracted his mind and brought it under her control.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.29 - Although Ka\'e7yapa Muni was a learned sch
olar, he was captivated by Diti's artificial behavior, which brought him under her control. Therefore he assured his wife that he would fulfill her desires. Such a promise by a husband is not at all astonishing.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.30 - In the beginning of creation, Lord Brahm\'e4
, the father of the living entities of the universe, saw that all the living entities were unattached. To increase population, he then created woman from the better half of man's body, for woman's behavior carries away a man's mind.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.31 - O my dear one, the most powerful sage Ka\'e7yapa, being extremely pleased by the mild behavior of his wife Diti, smiled and spoke to her as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.32 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni said: O beautiful woman, O irreproachable lady, since I am very much pleased by y
our behavior, you may ask me for any benediction you want. If a husband is pleased, what desires are difficult for his wife to obtain, either in this world or in the next?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.33-34 - A husband is the supreme demigod for a woman. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord V\'e4
sudeva, the husband of the goddess of fortune, is situated in everyone's heart and is worshiped through the various names and forms of the demigods by fruitive workers. Similarly, a husband represents the Lord as the object of worship for a woman.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.35 - My dear wife, whose body is so beautiful, your waist being thin, a conscientious wife should be chaste and should abide by the orders of her husband. She should very devoutly worship her husband as a representative of V
\'e4sudeva.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.18.36 - My dear gentle wife, because you have worshiped me with great devotion, considering me a representative of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, I shall reward you by fulfilling your desires, which are unobtainable for an unchaste wife.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.37 - Diti replied: O my husband, O great soul, I have now lost my sons. If you want to give me a benediction, I ask you for an immortal son who can kill Indra. I pray for this because Indra, with the help of Vi\'f1\'eb
u, has killed my two sons Hira\'eby\'e4k\'f1a and Hira\'ebyaka\'e7ipu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.38 - Upon hearing Diti's request, Ka\'e7yapa Muni was very much aggrieved. "Alas," he lamented, "now I face the danger of the impious act of killing Indra."
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.39 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni thought: Alas, I have now become too attached to mat
erial enjoyment. Taking advantage of this, my mind has been attracted by the illusory energy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in the form of a woman [my wife]. Therefore I am surely a wretched person who will glide down toward hell.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.40 - This
 woman, my wife, has adopted a means that follows her nature, and therefore she is not to be blamed. But I am a man. Therefore, all condemnation upon me! I am not at all conversant with what is good for me, since I could not control my senses.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.41 
- A woman's face is as attractive and beautiful as a blossoming lotus flower during autumn. Her words are very sweet, and they give pleasure to the ear, but if we study a woman's heart, we can understand it to be extremely sharp, like the blade of a razor
. In these circumstances, who could understand the dealings of a woman?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.42 - To satisfy their own interests, women deal with men as if the men were most dear to them, but no one is actually dear to them. Women are supposed to be very saintly, but f
or their own interests they can kill even their husbands, sons or brothers, or cause them to be killed by others.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.43 - I promised to give her a benediction, and this promise cannot be violated, but Indra does not deserve to be killed. In these circumstances, the solution I have is quite suitable.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.44 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: Ka\'e7yapa Muni, thinking in this way, became somewhat angry. Condemning himself, O Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, descendant of Kuru, he spoke to Diti as follows.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.45 - Ka\'e7
yapa Muni said: My dear gentle wife, if you follow my instructions regarding this vow for at least one year, you will surely get a son who will be able to kill Indra. However, if you deviate from this vow of following the Vai\'f1\'eb
ava principles, you will get a son who will be favorable to Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.46 - Diti replied: My dear br\'e4hma\'eba, I must accept your advice and follow the vow. Now let me understand what I have to do, what is forbidden and what will not break the vow. Please clearly state all this to me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.47 - Ka\'e7
yapa Muni said: My dear wife, to follow this vow, do not be violent or cause harm to anyone. Do not curse anyone, and do not speak lies. Do not cut your nails and hair, and do not touch impure things like skulls and bones.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.48 - Ka\'e7
yapa Muni continued: My dear gentle wife, never enter the water while bathing, never be angry, and do not even speak or associate with wicked people. Never wear clothes that have not been properly washed, and do not put on a garland that has already 
been worn.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.49 - Never eat leftover food, never eat pras\'e4da offered to the goddess K\'e4l\'e9 [Durg\'e4], and do not eat anything contaminated by flesh or fish. Do not eat anything brought or touched by a \'e7\'fc
dra nor anything seen by a woman in her menstrual period. Do not drink water by joining your palms.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.50 - After eating, you should not go out to the street without having washed your mouth, hands and feet. You should not go out in the evening or with your hair loose, nor should you go out unless y
ou are properly decorated with ornaments. You should not leave the house unless you are very grave and are sufficiently covered.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.51 - You should not lie down without having washed both of your feet or without being purified, nor with wet feet or w
ith your head pointed west or north. You should not lie naked, or with other women, or during the sunrise or sunset.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.52 - Putting on washed clothing, being always pure and being adorned with turmeric, sandalwood pulp and other auspicious items, before breakfast one should worship the cows, the br\'e4hma\'eb
as, the goddess of fortune and the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.53 - With flower garlands, sandalwood pulp, ornaments and other paraphernalia, a woman following this vow should worship wome
n who have sons and whose husbands are living. The pregnant wife should worship her husband and offer him prayers. She should meditate upon him, thinking that he is situated in her womb.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.54 - Ka\'e7yapa Muni continued: If you perform this ceremony called pu\'e0
savana, adhering to the vow with faith for at least one year, you will give birth to a son destined to kill Indra. But if there is any discrepancy in the discharge of this vow, the son will be a friend to Indra.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.55 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, Diti, the wife of Ka\'e7yapa, agreed to undergo the purificatory process known as pu\'e0
savana. "Yes," she said, "I shall do everything according to your instructions." With great jubilation she became pregnant, having taken semen from Ka\'e7yapa, and faithfully began discharging the vow.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.18.56 - O King, who are respectful to everyone, Indra understood Diti's purpose, and thus he contrived to fulfill his own interests. Following the logic that self-preservation is the first law of nature, he wanted to break Diti's 
promise. Thus he engaged himself in the service of Diti, his aunt, who was residing in an \'e4\'e7rama.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.57 - Indra served his aunt daily by bringing flowers, fruits, roots and wood for yaj\'efas from the forest. He also brought ku\'e7a grass, leaves, sprouts, earth and water exactly at the proper time.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.58 - O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, as the hunter of a deer becomes like a deer by covering his body with deerskin and serving the deer, so Indra, although at heart the enemy of the sons of Diti, became outwardly fri
endly and served Diti in a faithful way. Indra's purpose was to cheat Diti as soon as he could find some fault in the way she discharged the vows of the ritualistic ceremony. However, he wanted to be undetected, and therefore he served her very carefully.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.59 - O master of the entire world, when Indra could find no faults, he thought, "How will there be good fortune for me?" Thus he was full of deep anxiety.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.60 - Having grown weak and thin because of strictly following the principles of the vow, Diti once unfortunately neglected to wash her mouth, hands and feet after eating and went to sleep during the evening twilight.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.61 - Finding this fault, Indra, who has all the mystic powers [the yoga-siddhis such as a\'ebim\'e4 and laghim\'e4], entered Diti's womb while she was unconscious, being fast asleep.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.62 - After entering Diti's womb, Indra, with the help of his thunderbolt, cut into seven pieces her embryo, which appeared like glowing gold. In seven places, seven different living bein
gs began crying. Indra told them, "Do not cry," and then he cut each of them into seven pieces again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.63 - O King, being very much aggrieved, they pleaded to Indra with folded hands, saying, "Dear Indra, we are the Maruts, your brothers. Why are you trying to kill us?"
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.64 - When Indra saw that actually they were his devoted followers, he said to them: If you are all my brothers, you have nothing more to fear from me.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.65 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, you were burned by the brahm\'e4stra of A\'e7vatth\'e4m\'e4, but when Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a entered the womb of your mother, you were saved. Similarly, although the one embryo was cut into forty-nine pieces by the thunderbolt of Indra, they were all saved by the mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.66-67 - If one worships the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the original person, even once, he receives the benefit of being promoted to the spiritual world and possessing the same bodily features as Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Diti worshiped Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u for almost one year, adhering to a great vow. Because of such strength in spiritual life, the forty-nine Maruts were born. How, then, is it wonderful that the Maruts, although born from the womb of Diti, became equal to the demigods by the mercy of the 
Supreme Lord ?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 
SB 6.18.68 - Because of worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Diti was completely purified. When she got up from bed, she saw her forty-nine sons along with Indra. These forty-nine sons were all as brilliant as fire and were in frie
ndship with Indra, and therefore she was very pleased.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.69 - Thereafter, Diti said to Indra: My dear son, I adhered to this difficult vow just to get a son to kill you twelve \'c4dityas.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.70 - I prayed for only one son, but now I see that there are forty-nine. How has this happened? My dear son Indra, if you know, please tell me the truth. Do not try to speak lies.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.71 - Indra replied: My dear mother, because I was grossly blinded by selfish interests, I lost sight of religion. When I u
nderstood that you were observing a great vow in spiritual life, I wanted to find some fault in you. When I found such a fault, I entered your womb and cut the embryo to pieces.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.72 - First I cut the child in the womb into seven pieces, which became seven children. Then I cut each of the children into seven pieces again. By the grace of the Supreme Lord, however, none of them died.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.73 - My dear mother, when I saw that all forty-nine sons were alive, I was certainly struck with wonder. I decided that this was a secondary result of your having regularly executed devotional service in worship of Lord Vi
\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.74 - Although those who are interested only in worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead do not desire anything material from the Lord and do not even want liberation, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba fulfills all their desires.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.75 - The ultimate goal of all ambitions is to become a servant of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. If an intelligent man serves the most dear Lord, who gives Himse
lf to His devotees, how can he desire material happiness, which is available even in hell?
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.76 - O my mother, O best of all women, I am a fool. Kindly excuse me for whatever offenses I have committed. Your forty-nine sons have been born unhurt beca
use of your devotional service. As an enemy, I cut them to pieces, but because of your great devotional service they did not die.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.77 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Diti was extremely satisfied by Indra's good behavior. Then Indra offered his re
spects to his aunt with profuse obeisances, and with her permission he went away to the heavenly planets with his brothers the Maruts.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.18.78 - My dear King Par\'e9k\'f1it, I have replied as far as possible to the questions you have asked me, especially in 
regard to this pure, auspicious narration about the Maruts. Now you may inquire further, and I shall explain more.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Translations 1-78
\par }\pard \s97\ql \fi-605\li720\ri720\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\brdrcf14 \brdrl\brdrs\brdrw45\brsp20\brdrcf13 \tx1080\faauto\rin720\lin720\rtlgutter\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn 
{\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \shading10000\cfpat16 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{
\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.1 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it said: My dear lord, you have already spoken about the pu\'e0savana vow. Now I want to hear about it in detail, for I understand that by observing this vow one can please the Supreme Lord, Vi
\'f1\'ebu.
\par }\pard \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.2-3 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: On the first day of the bright fortnight of the month of Agrah\'e4ya\'eba [November-December], following the instructions of her husband, a 
woman should begin this regulative devotional service with a vow of penance, for it can fulfill all one's desires. Before beginning the worship of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, the woman should hear the story of how the Maruts were born. Under the instructions of qualified br\'e4hma\'eb
as, in the morning she should wash her teeth, bathe, and dress herself with white cloth and ornaments, and before taking breakfast she should worship Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and Lak\'f1m\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.4 - [She should then pray to the Lord as follows.] My dear Lord, You are full in all opulences, but I do not beg You for opulence. I simply offer my respectful obeisances unto You. You are the husband and master of Lak\'f1m
\'e9dev\'e9, the goddess of fortune, who has all opulences. Therefore You are the master of all mystic yoga. I simply offer my obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.5 - O my Lord, because You are endowed with causeless mercy, all opulences, all prowess and all glories, strength and transcendental qualities, You are the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the master of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.6 - [After profusely offering obeisances unto Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, the devotee should offer respectful obeisances unto mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, the goddess of fortune, and pray as follows.] O wife of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, O internal energy of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, you are as good as Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu Himself, for you have all of His qualities and opulences. O goddess of fortune, please be kind to me. O mother of the entire world, I offer my respectful obeisances unto you.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.7 - "My Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, full in six opulences, You are the best of all enjoyers and the most powerful. O husband of mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
, I offer my respectful obeisances unto You, who are accompanied by many associates, such as Vi\'e7vaksena. I offer all the paraphernalia for worshiping You." One should chant this mantra every day with great attention while worshiping Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u with all paraphernalia, such as water for washing His feet, hands and mouth and water for His bath. One must offer Him various presentations for His worship, such as garments, a sacred thread, ornaments, scents, flowers, incense and lamps.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.8 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After worshiping the Lord with all the paraphernalia mentioned above, one should chant the following mantra while offering twelve oblations of ghee on the sacred fire: o\'e0 namo b
hagavate mah\'e4-puru\'f1\'e4ya mah\'e4vibh\'fcti-pataye sv\'e4h\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.9 - If one desires all opulences, his duty is to daily worship Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu with His wife, Lak\'f1m\'e9. With great devotion one should worship Him according to the above-mentioned process. Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and t
he goddess of fortune are an immensely powerful combination. They are the bestowers of all benedictions and the sources of all good fortune. Therefore the duty of everyone is to worship Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.10 - One should offer obeisances unto the Lord with a mind humbled through devotion. While offering da\'eb\'f2
avats by falling on the ground like a rod, one should chant the above mantra ten times. Then one should chant the following prayer.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.11 - My Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, goddess of fortune, you are the proprietors of the entire creation. Indeed, you are the cause of the creation. Mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
 is extremely difficult to understand because she is so powerful that the jurisdiction of her power is difficult to overcome. Mother Lak\'f1m\'e9 is repres
ented in the material world as the external energy, but actually she is always the internal energy of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.12 - My Lord, You are the master of energy, and therefore You are the Supreme Person. You are sacrifice [yaj\'efa] personified. Lak\'f1m\'e9, th
e embodiment of spiritual activities, is the original form of worship offered unto You, whereas You are the enjoyer of all sacrifices.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.13 - Mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, who is here, is the reservoir of all spiritual qualities, whereas You manifest and enjoy all
 these qualities. Indeed, You are actually the enjoyer of everything. You live as the Supersoul of all living entities, aid the goddess of fortune is the form of their bodies, senses and minds. She also has a holy name and form, whereas You are the suppor
t of all such names and forms and the cause for their manifestation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.14 - You are both the supreme rulers and benedictors of the three worlds. Therefore, my Lord, Uttama\'e7loka, may my ambitions be fulfilled by Your grace.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.15 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Thus one should worship Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who is known as \'c7r\'e9niv\'e4sa, along with mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
, the goddess of fortune, by offering prayers according to the process mentioned above. After removing all the paraphernalia of worship, one should offer them water to wash their hands and mouths, and then one should worship them again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.16 - Thereafter, with devotion and humility, one should offer prayers to the Lord and mother Lak\'f1m\'e9. Then one should smell the remnants of the food offered and then again worship the Lord and Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.17 - Accepting her husband as the representative of the Supreme Person, a wife should worship him with unalloyed devotion by offering him pras\'e4da. The husband, being very pleased with his wife, should enga
ge himself in the affairs of his family.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.18 - Between the husband and wife, one person is sufficient to execute this devotional service. Because of their good relationship, both of them will enjoy the result. Therefore if the wife is unable to exe
cute this process, the husband should carefully do so, and the faithful wife will share the result.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.19-20 - One should accept this vi\'f1\'ebu-vrata, which is a vow in devotional service, and should not deviate from its execution to engage in anything else. By offering the remnants of pras\'e4
da, flower garlands, sandalwood pulp and ornaments, one should daily worship the br\'e4hma\'ebas and worship women who peacefully live with their husbands and children. Every day the wife must continue following the regulati
ve principles to worship Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu with great devotion. Thereafter, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu should be laid in His bed, and then one should take pras\'e4da. In this way, husband and wife will be purified and will have all their desires fulfilled.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.21 - The chaste wife must perform such devotional service continuously for one year. After one year passes, she should fast on the full-moon day in the month of K\'e4rttika [October-November].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.22 - On the morning of the next day, one should wash oneself, and after worshiping Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba as before, one should cook as one cooks for festivals as stated in the G\'e5hya-s\'fc
tras. Sweet rice should be cooked with ghee, and with this preparation the husband should offer oblations to the fire twelve times.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.23 - Thereafter, he should satisfy the br\'e4hma\'ebas. When the satisfied br\'e4hma\'eb
as bestow their blessings, he should devotedly offer them respectful obeisances with his head, and with their permission he should take pras\'e4da.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.24 - Before taking his meal, the husband must first seat the \'e4c\'e4rya comfortably, and, along with his relatives and friends, should control his speech and offer pras\'e4
da to the guru. Then the wife should eat the remnants of the oblation of sweet rice cooked with ghee. Eating the remnants insures a learned, devoted son and all good fortune.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.25 - If this vow or ritualistic ceremony is observed according to the description of \'e7\'e4stra, even in this life a man will be able to achieve all the benedictions he desires from the Lord. A wife who perfo
rms this ritualistic ceremony will surely receive good fortune, opulence, sons, a long-living husband, a good reputation and a good home.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.26-28 - If an unmarried girl observes this vrata, she will be able to get a very good husband. If a woman who is av\'e9r\'e4
-who has no husband or son-executes this ritualistic ceremony, she can be promoted to the spiritual world. A woman whose children have died after birth can get a child with a long duration of life and also become very fortunate in possessing wealt
h. If a woman is unfortunate she will become fortunate, and if ugly she will become beautiful. By observing this vrata, a diseased man can gain relief from his disease and have an able body with which to work. If one recites this narration while offering 
oblations to the pit\'e4s and demigods, especially during the \'e7r\'e4ddha ceremony, the demigods and inhabitants of Pit\'e5
loka will be extremely pleased with him and bestow upon him the fulfillment of all desires. After one performs this ritualistic ceremony, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and His wife, mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, the goddess of fortune, are very pleased with him. O King Par\'e9
k\'f1it, now I have completely described how Diti performed this ceremony and had good children-the Maruts-and a happy life. I have tried to explain this to you as elaborately as possible.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }}}{\f35\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  19. }{\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid10252087\charrsid10252087 \chftn {\footnote\ftnalt \pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 
\b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1867\fs14\up12\insrsid5731824\charrsid10252087 \chftn }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.1 - Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it said: My dear lord, you have already spoken about the pu\'e0
savana vow. Now I want to hear about it in detail, for I understand that by observing this vow one can please the Supreme Lord, Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.2-3 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 said: On the first day of the bright fortnight of the month of Agrah\'e4ya\'eb
a [November-December], following the instructions of her husband, a woman should begin this regulative devotional service with a vow of penance, for it can fulfill all one's desires. Before beginning the worship of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, the woman should hear the story of how the Maruts were born. Under the instructions of qualified br\'e4hma\'ebas, in the morning she should wash her teeth, bathe, and dress herself with white 
cloth and ornaments, and before taking breakfast she should worship Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and Lak\'f1m\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.4 - [She should then pray to the Lord as follows.] My dear Lord, You are full in all opulences, but I do not beg You for opulence. I simply offer my respectful obeisances unto You. You are the husband and master of Lak\'f1m
\'e9dev\'e9, the goddess of fortune, who has all opulences. Therefore You are the master of all mystic yoga. I simply offer my obeisances unto You.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.5 - O my Lord, because You are endowed with causeless mercy, all opulences, all prowess and all glories, strength and transcendental qualities, You are the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the master of everyone.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.6 - [After profusely offering obeisances unto Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, the devotee should offer respectful obeisances unto mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, the goddess of fortune, and pray as follows.] O wife of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, O internal energy of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, you are as good as Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu Himself, for you have all of His qualities and opulences. O goddess of fortune, please be kind to me. O mother of the entire world, I offer my respectful obeisances unto you.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.7 - "My Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, full in six opulences, You are the best of all enjoyers and the most powerful. O husband of mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, I offer my respectful
 obeisances unto You, who are accompanied by many associates, such as Vi\'e7vaksena. I offer all the paraphernalia for worshiping You." One should chant this mantra every day with great attention while worshiping Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u with all paraphernalia, such as water for washing His feet, hands and mouth and water for His bath. One must offer Him various presentations for His worship, such as garments, a sacred thread, ornaments, scents, flowers, incense and lamps.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.8 - \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: After worshiping the Lord with all the paraphernalia mentioned above, one should chant the following mantra while offering twelve oblations of ghee on the sacred fire: o\'e0
 namo bhagavate mah\'e4-puru\'f1\'e4ya mah\'e4vibh\'fcti-pataye sv\'e4h\'e4.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.9 - If one desires all opulences, his duty is to daily worship Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu with His wife, Lak\'f1m\'e9. With great devotion one should worship Him according to the above-mentioned process. Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u and the goddess of fortune are an immensely powerful combination. They are the bestowers of all benedictions and the sources of all good fortune. Therefore the duty of everyone is to worship Lak\'f1m\'e9-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.10 - One should offer obeisances unto the Lord with a mind humbled through devotion. While offering da\'eb\'f2avats by falling on the groun
d like a rod, one should chant the above mantra ten times. Then one should chant the following prayer.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.11 - My Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, goddess of fortune, you are the proprietors of the entire creation. Indeed, you are the cause of the creation. Mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
 is extremely difficult to understand because she is so powerful that the jurisdiction of her power is difficult to overcome. Mother Lak\'f1m\'e9 is represented in the material world as the external energy, but actually she is always the intern
al energy of the Lord.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.12 - My Lord, You are the master of energy, and therefore You are the Supreme Person. You are sacrifice [yaj\'efa] personified. Lak\'f1m\'e9
, the embodiment of spiritual activities, is the original form of worship offered unto You, whereas You are the enjoyer of all sacrifices.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.13 - Mother Lak\'f1m\'e9, who is here, is the reservoir of all spiritual qualities, whereas You manifest and enjoy all these qualities. Indeed, You are actually the enjoyer of everything. You live as the Sup
ersoul of all living entities, aid the goddess of fortune is the form of their bodies, senses and minds. She also has a holy name and form, whereas You are the support of all such names and forms and the cause for their manifestation.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.14 - You are both the supreme rulers and benedictors of the three worlds. Therefore, my Lord, Uttama\'e7loka, may my ambitions be fulfilled by Your grace.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.15 - \'c7r\'e9 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continued: Thus one should worship Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who is known as \'c7r\'e9niv\'e4sa, along with mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
, the goddess of fortune, by offering prayers according to the process mentioned above. After removing all the paraphernalia of worship, one should offer them water to wash their hands and mouths, and then one should worship them again.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.16 - Thereafter, with devotion and humility, one should offer prayers to the Lord and mother Lak\'f1m\'e9. Then one should smell the remnants of the food offered and then again worship the Lord and Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.17 - Accepting her husband as the representative of the Supreme Person, a wife should worship him with unalloyed devotion by offering him pras\'e4
da. The husband, being very pleased with his wife, should engage himself in the affairs of his family.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.18 - Between the husband and wife, one 
person is sufficient to execute this devotional service. Because of their good relationship, both of them will enjoy the result. Therefore if the wife is unable to execute this process, the husband should carefully do so, and the faithful wife will share 
the result.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.19-20 - One should accept this vi\'f1\'ebu-vrata, which is a vow in devotional service, and should not deviate from its execution to engage in anything else. By offering the remnants of pras\'e4
da, flower garlands, sandalwood pulp and ornaments, one should daily worship the br\'e4hma\'eb
as and worship women who peacefully live with their husbands and children. Every day the wife must continue following the regulative principles to worship Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu with great devotion. Thereafter, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu should be
 laid in His bed, and then one should take pras\'e4da. In this way, husband and wife will be purified and will have all their desires fulfilled.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.21 - The chaste wife must perform such devotional service continuously for one year. After one year passes, she should fast on the full-moon day in the month of K\'e4rttika [October-November].
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.22 - On the morning of the next day, one should wash oneself, and after worshiping Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba as before, one should cook as one cooks for festivals as stated in the G\'e5hya-s\'fc
tras. Sweet rice should be cooked with ghee, and with this preparation the husband should offer oblations to the fire twelve times.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.23 - Thereafter, he should satisfy the br\'e4hma\'ebas. When the satisfied br\'e4hma\'ebas bestow their blessings, h
e should devotedly offer them respectful obeisances with his head, and with their permission he should take pras\'e4da.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.24 - Before taking his meal, the husband must first seat the \'e4c\'e4rya comfortably, and, along with his relatives and friends, should control his speech and offer pras\'e4
da to the guru. Then the wife should eat the remnants of the oblation of sweet rice cooked with ghee. Eating the remnants insures a learned, devoted son and all good fortune.
\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.25 - If this vow or ritualistic ceremony is observed according to the description of \'e7\'e4
stra, even in this life a man will be able to achieve all the benedictions he desires from the Lord. A wife who performs this ritualistic ceremony will surely receive good fortune, opulence, sons, a long-living husband, a good reputation and a good home.

\par }{\b0\cf0\insrsid5731824 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid5731824 SB 6.19.26-28 - If an unmarried girl observes this vrata, she will be able to get a very good husband. If a woman who is av\'e9r\'e4-who has no husband or son-executes this ritualistic ceremony, she can be promot
ed to the spiritual world. A woman whose children have died after birth can get a child with a long duration of life and also become very fortunate in possessing wealth. If a woman is unfortunate she will become fortunate, and if ugly she will become beau
tiful. By observing this vrata, a diseased man can gain relief from his disease and have an able body with which to work. If one recites this narration while offering oblations to the pit\'e4s and demigods, especially during the \'e7r\'e4
ddha ceremony, the demigods and inhabitants of Pit\'e5loka will be extremely pleased with him and bestow upon him the fulfillment of all desires. After one performs this ritualistic ceremony, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and His wife, mother Lak\'f1m\'e9
, the goddess of fortune, are very pleased with him. O King Par\'e9k\'f1it, now I have completely described how Diti performed this ceremony and had good children-the Maruts-and a happy life. I have tried to explain this to you as elaborately as possible.

