\par }\pard\plain \s20\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf18\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\insrsid7479917 
\par }{\insrsid10252087 SB 6.1: The History of the Life of Aj\'e4mila
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.1 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 Throughout }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid10252087 
 there are descriptions of ten subject matters, including creation, subsequent creation and the planetary systems. \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, the speaker of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\insrsid10252087 
 has already described creation, subsequent creation and the planetary systems in the Third, Fourth and Fifth Cantos. Now, in this Sixth Canto, which consists of nineteen chapters, he will describe }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 po\'f1a\'eba,}{
\insrsid10252087  or protection by the Lord.
\par The first chapter relates the history of Aj\'e4mila, who was considered a greatly sinful man, but was liberated when four order carriers of Vi\'f1\'ebu came to rescue him from the hands of the order carriers of Yamar\'e4
ja. A full description of how he was liberated, having been relieved 
of the reactions of his sinful life, is given in this chapter. Sinful activities are painful both in this life and in the next. We should know for certain that the cause of all painful life is sinful action. On the path of fruitive work one certainly comm
its sinful activities, and therefore according to the considerations of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\insrsid10252087 
 different types of atonement are recommended. Such methods of atonement, however, do not free one from ignorance, which is the root of sinful life. Consequently one is pron
e to commit sinful activities even after atonement, which is therefore very inadequate for purification. On the path of speculative knowledge one becomes free from sinful life by understanding things as they are. Therefore the acquirement of speculative k
nowledge is also considered a method of atonement. While performing fruitive activities one can become free from the actions of sinful life through austerity, penance, celibacy, control of the mind and senses, truthfulness and the practice of mystic }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yoga.}{\insrsid10252087  By awakening knowledge one may also neutralize sinful reactions. Neither of these methods, however, can free one from the tendency to commit sinful activities.
\par By }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bhakti-yoga}{\insrsid10252087  one can completely avoid the tendency for sinful life; other methods are not very 
feasible. Therefore the Vedic literature concludes that devotional service is more important than the methods of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a.}{
\insrsid10252087  Only the path of devotional service is auspicious for everyone. Fruitive activities and speculative knowledge cannot independently liberate anyone, but devotional service, independent of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 karma}{
\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na,}{\insrsid10252087  is so potent that one who has fixed his mind at the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eba is guaranteed not to meet the Yamad\'fctas, the order carriers of Yamar\'e4
ja, even in dreams.
\par To prove the strength of devotional service, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 described the history of Aj\'e4mila. Aj\'e4mila was a resident of K\'e4nyakubja (the modern Kanauj). He was trained by his parents to become a perfect }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br
\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid10252087  by studying the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Vedas}{\insrsid10252087  and following the regulative principles, but because of his past, this youthful }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid10252087 
 was somehow attracted by a prostitute, and because of her association he became most fallen and abandoned all regulative principles. Aj\'e4mila begot in the womb of the prostitute ten sons, the last of whom was called N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. At the time of Aj
\'e4mila's death, when the order carriers of Yamar\'e4ja came to take him, he loudly called the name N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba in fear because he was attached to his youngest son. Thus he remembered the original N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Although he did not chant the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba completely offenselessly, it acted nevertheless. As soon as he chanted the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, the order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u immediately appeared on the scene. A discussion ensued between the order carriers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu and those of Yamar\'e4ja, and by hearing that discussion Aj\'e4
mila was liberated. He could then understand the bad effect of fruitive activities and could also understand how exalted is the process of devotional service.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.1.1
\par }\pard\plain \s2995\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 TEXT 1
