\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it said; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash the path of liberation; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 kathita\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash described; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e4dau}{
\insrsid10252087 \emdash in the beginning; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bhagavat\'e4}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash by Your Holiness; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yath\'e4}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash duly; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 krama}{\insrsid10252087 
\emdash gradually; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yoga-upalabdhena}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash obtained by the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yoga}{\insrsid10252087  process; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 brahma\'eb\'e4}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
along with Lord Brahm\'e4 (after reaching Brahmaloka); }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yat}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash by which way; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 asa\'e0s\'e5ti\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash cessation of the repetition of birth and death.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3004\fs28\cf9\insrsid10252087\charrsid6360924 Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it said: }{
\cs3002\fs28\insrsid10252087\charrsid741136 O my lord, O \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, you have already described [in the Second Canto] the path of liberation [niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga]. By foll
owing that path, one is certainly elevated gradually to the highest planetary system, Brahmaloka, from which one is promoted to the spiritual world along with Lord Brahm\'e4. Thus one's repetition of birth and death in the material world ceases.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 Since Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it was a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava, when he heard the description, at the end of the Fifth Canto, of the different hellish conditions of life, he was very much concerned with how to liberate the conditioned souls from the clutches of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4y\'e4}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  and take them back home, back to Godhead. Therefore he reminded his spiritual master, \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, about the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  or path of liberation, which he had described in the Second Canto. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1it, who at the time of death was fortunate to have met \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, inquired from \'c7
ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 about the path of liberation at that crucial time. \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 very much appreciated his question and congratulated him by saying:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 var\'e9y\'e4n e\'f1a te pra\'e7na\'f9\line k\'e5to loka-hita\'e0 n\'e5pa\line \'e4
tmavit-sammata\'f9 pu\'e0s\'e4\'e0\line \'e7rotavy\'e4di\'f1u ya\'f9 para\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"My dear King, your question is glorious because it is very beneficial for all kinds of people. The answer to this question is the prime subject matter for hearing, and it is approved by all transcendentalists." (}{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid1651685\charrsid1651685 Bh\'e4g.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  2.1.1)
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja 
was astonished that the living entities in the conditional stage do not accept the path of liberation, devotional service, instead of suffering in so many hellish conditions. This is the symptom of a Vai\'f1\'ebava. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 V\'e4\'efch
\'e4-kalpa-tarubhya\'e7 ca k\'e5p\'e4-sindhubhya eva ca:}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  a Vai\'f1\'ebava is an ocean of mercy. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Para-du\'f9kha-du\'f9kh\'e9:}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 he is unhappy because of the unhappiness of others. Therefore Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, being compassionate toward the conditioned souls suffering in hellish life, suggested that \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 continue d
escribing the path of liberation, which he had explained in the beginning of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 asa\'e0s\'e5ti}{
\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  is very important in this connection. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Sa\'e0s\'e5ti}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  refers to continuing on the path of birth and death. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Asa\'e0s
\'e5ti,}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  on the contrary, refers to }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga,}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 or the path of liberation, by which one's birth and death cease and one gradually progresses to Brahmaloka, unless one is a pure devotee who does not care about going to the higher planetary systems, in which case one immediately returns home, bac
k to Godhead, by executing devotional service (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0 punar janma naiti}{\insrsid10252087 ). Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, therefore, was very eager to hear from \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 about the path of liberation for the conditioned soul.
\par According to the opinion of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e4c\'e4ryas,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 krama-yogopalabdhena}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  indicates that by first performing }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 karma-yoga}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and then }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-yoga}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and finally coming to the platform of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bhakti-yoga,}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  one can be liberated. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Bhakti-yoga,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  however, is so powerful that it does not depend on }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 karma-yoga}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  or }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-yoga.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Bhakti-yoga}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 itself is so powerful that even an impious man with no assets in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 karma-yoga}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  or an illiterate with no assets in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-yoga}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 can undoubtedly be elevated to the spiritual world if he simply adheres to }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bhakti-yoga.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 M\'e4m evai\'f1yasy asa\'e0\'e7aya\'f9.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (8.7) that by the process of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bhakti-yoga}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 one undoubtedly goes back to Godhead, back home to the spiritual world. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Yog\'e9s,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 however, instead of going directly to the spiritual world, sometimes want to see other planetary systems, and therefore they ascend to the planetary system where Lord Brahm\'e4 lives, as indicated here by the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 brahma\'eb
\'e4.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  At the time of dissolution, Lord Brahm\'e4, along with all the inhabitants of Brahmaloka, goes directly to the spiritual world. This is confirmed in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Vedas}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  as follows:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 brahma\'eb\'e4 saha te sarve\line sampr\'e4pte pratisa\'efcare\line parasy\'e4nte k\'e5
