ish life in this body and the next. Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, therefore, anxiously wanted to know from \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 how humanity can be saved from gliding down to hell. \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 had already explained how people enter hellish life, and he could also explain how they could be saved from it. Intelligent men must take advantage of these instructions. Unfortunately, however, the entire world is lacking K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, and therefore people are suffering from the grossest ignorance and do not even believ
e in a life after this one. To convince them of their next life is very difficult because they have become almost mad in their pursuit of material enjoyment. Nevertheless, our duty, the duty of all sane men, is to save them. Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1
it is the representative of one who can save them.
