\par }\pard\plain \s3000\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid741136 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, the son of Vedavy\'e4
sa, answered: My dear King, since acts meant to neutralize impious actions are also fruitive, they will not release one from the tendency to act fruitively. Pers
ons who subject themselves to the rules and regulations of atonement are not at all intelligent. Indeed, they are in the mode of darkness. Unless one is freed from the mode of ignorance, trying to counteract one action through another is useless because t
his will not uproot one's desires. Thus even though one may superficially seem pious, he will undoubtedly be prone to act impiously. Therefore real atonement is enlightenment in perfect knowledge, Ved\'e4
nta, by which one understands the Supreme Absolute Truth.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 guru,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, has examined Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, and it appears that the King has passed one phase of the examination by rejecting the process of atonement because it involves fruitive activities. Now \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 is suggesting the platform of speculative knowledge. Progressing from }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  to }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  he is proposing, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pr\'e4ya\'e7citta\'e0 vimar\'e7anam:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  "Real atonement is full knowledge." }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vimar\'e7ana}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  refers to the cultivation of speculative knowledge. In }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karm
\'e9s,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  who are lacking in knowledge, are compared to asses. K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  (7.15):

\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 na m\'e4\'e0 du\'f1k\'e5tino m\'fc\'f2h\'e4\'f9\line prapadyante nar\'e4dham\'e4\'f9
\line m\'e4yay\'e4pah\'e5ta-j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\line \'e4sura\'e0 bh\'e4vam \'e4\'e7rit\'e4\'f9
