"Those miscreants who are grossly foolish, lowest among mankind, whose knowledge is stolen by illusion, and who partake of the atheistic nature of demons, do not surrender unto Me." Thus }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karm\'e9s}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  who engage in sinful acts and who do not know the true objective of life are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'fc\'f2has,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  asses. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vimar\'e7ana,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  however, is also explained in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (15.15), where K
\'e5\'f1\'eba says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vedai\'e7 ca sarvair aham eva vedya\'f9:}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  the purpose of Vedic study is to understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead. If one studies Ved\'e4
nta but merely advances somewhat in speculative knowledge and does not understand the Supreme Lord, one remains the same }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'fc\'f2ha.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  As stated in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (7.19), one attains real knowledge when he understands K\'e5\'f1\'eba and surrenders unto Him (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bah\'fcn\'e4\'e0
 janman\'e4m ante j\'ef\'e4nav\'e4n m\'e4\'e0 prapadyate}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ). To become learned and free from material contamination, therefore, one should try to understand K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, for thus one is immediately liberated from all pious and impious activities and their reactions.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.1.12
