\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sm\'e5ti-\'e7\'e4stra}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  as follows: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 manasa\'e7 cendriy\'e4\'eb\'e4\'e0 ca aik\'e4grya\'e0 parama\'e0 tapa\'f9.}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  "Complete control of the mind and senses and their complete concentration on one kind of activity is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tapa\'f9.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
" Our K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement is teaching people how to concentrate the mind on devotional service. This is first-class }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tapa\'f9.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Brahmacarya,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  the life of celibacy, has eight aspects: one shou
ld not think of women, speak about sex life, dally with women, look lustfully at women, talk intimately with women or decide to engage in sexual intercourse, nor should one endeavor for sex life or engage in sex life. One should not even think of women or
 look at them, to say nothing of talking with them. This is called first-class }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 brahmacarya.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  If a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 brahmac\'e4r\'e9}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sanny\'e4s\'e9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 talks with a woman in a secluded place, naturally there will be a possibility of sex life without anyone's knowledge. Therefore a complete }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 brahmac\'e4r\'e9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 practices just the opposite. If one is a perfect }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 brahmac\'e4r\'e9,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 he can very easily control the mind and senses, give charity, speak truthfully and so forth. To begin, however, one must control the tongue and the process of eating.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 In the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhakti-m\'e4rga,}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  the path of devotional service, one must strictly follow the regulative principles by first controlling the tongue (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sevonmukhe hi jihv\'e4dau svayam eva sphuraty ada
\'f9}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ). The tongue (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 jihv\'e4}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ) can be controlled if one chants the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mah\'e4-mantra,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  does not speak of any subjects other than those concerning K\'e5\'f1\'eba and does not taste anything not offered to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. If one can control the tongue in this way, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 brahmacarya}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and other purifying processes will automatically follow. It will be explained in the next v
