\par }\pard\plain \s3019\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb240\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1521817 \f35\fs28\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 kecit}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash some people; }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 kevalay\'e4 bhakty\'e4}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash by executing unalloyed devotional service; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 v\'e4sudeva}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the all-pervading Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 par\'e4ya\'eb\'e4\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
completely attached (only to such service, without dependence on austerity, penance, cultivation of knowledge or pious activities); }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 agham}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash all kinds of sinful reactions; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 
dhunvanti}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash destroy; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 k\'e4rtsnyena}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash completely (with no possibility that sinful desires will revive); }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 n\'e9h\'e4ram}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash fog; }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 iva}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash like; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4skara\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash the sun.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3000\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid741136 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
Only a rare person who has adopted complete, unalloyed devotional service to K\'e5\'f1\'eba can uproot the weeds of sinful actions with no possibility that they will revive. He can do this simply b
y discharging devotional service, just as the sun can immediately dissipate fog by its rays.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 In the previous verse \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
 gave the example that the dried leaves of creepers beneath a bamboo tree may be completely burnt to ashes by a fire,
 although the creepers may sprout again because the root is still in the ground. Similarly, because the root of sinful desire is not destroyed in the heart of a person who is cultivating knowledge but who has no taste for devotional service, there is a po
ssibility that his sinful desires will reappear. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  (10.14.4):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7reya\'f9-s\'e5ti\'e0 bhaktim udasya te vibho\line kli\'e7
yanti ye kevala-bodha-labdhaye
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
Speculators who undergo great labor to gain a meticulous understanding of the material world b
y distinguishing between sinful and pious activities, but who are not situated in devotional service, are prone to material activities. They may fall down and become implicated in fruitive activities. If one becomes attached to devotional service, however
,}{\cs3027\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  his desires for material enjoyment }{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 are automatically vanquished without separate endeavor. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhakti\'f9 pare\'e7\'e4
nubhavo viraktir anyatra ca: }{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 if one is advanced in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, material activities, both sinful and pious, automatically become distasteful to him. That is the test of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness. Both pious and impious activities are actually due to ignorance because a living entity, as an eternal servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, has no need to act for his personal sense gratification. Therefore as soon as one is re}{
\cs3027\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 claimed to the platform of devotional service, he relinquishes his attachment for pio}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
us and impious activities and is interested only in what will satisfy K\'e5\'f1\'eba. This process of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhakti,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  devotional service to K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 v\'e4sudeva-par\'e4ya\'eba}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ), relieves one from the reactions of all activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 Since Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Par\'e9k\'f1
it was a great devotee. the answers of his }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 guru,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, concerning }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  could not satisfy him. Therefore \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9
, knowing very well the heart of his disciple, explained the transcendental bliss of devotional service. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 kecit,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  whi}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid1115024 
ch is used in this verse, means,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  "a few people but not all." Not everyone can become K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba explains in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (7.3):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 manu\'f1y\'e4\'eb\'e4\'e0 sahasre\'f1u\line ka\'e7cid yatati siddhaye\line yatat\'e4
m api siddh\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line ka\'e7cin m\'e4\'e0 vetti tattvata\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s3023\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9723571 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
"Out of many thousands among men, one may endeavor for perfection, and of those who have achieved perfection, hardly one knows Me in truth." Practically no one understands K\'e5\'f1\'eba as He is, for K\'e5\'f1\'eba can
not be understood through pious activities or attainment of the most elevated speculative knowledge. Actually the highest knowledge consists of understanding K\'e5\'f1\'eba. Unintelligent men who do not understand K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a are grossly puffed up, thinking that they are liberated or have themselves become K\'e5\'f1\'eba or N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. This is ignorance.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 To indicate the purity of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
bhakti,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  devotional service, \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhakti-ras\'e4m\'e5ta-sindhu}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (1.1.11):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnya\'e0\line j\'ef\'e4na-karm\'e4dy-an\'e4v\'e5tam
\line \'e4nuk\'fclyena k\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4nu-\line \'e7\'e9lana\'e0 bhaktir uttam\'e4}{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"One should render transcendental loving service to the Supreme Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba favorably and without desire for material profit or gain through fruitive activities or philosophical speculation. That is called pure devotional service." \'c7r\'e9la R
\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 further explains that }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhakti}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 kle\'e7aghn\'e9 \'e7ubhad\'e4,}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  which means if one takes to devotional service, all kinds of unnecessary labor and material distress cease entirely and one achieves all good fortune. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhakti}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  is so powerful that it is also said to be }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mok\'f1a-laghut\'e4k\'e5t;}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 in other words, it minimizes the importance of liberation.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
Nondevotees must undergo material hardships because they are prone to commit sinful fruitive activities. The desire to commit sinful actions continues in their hearts due to ignorance. These sinful actions are divided into three categories\emdash }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 p\'e4taka, mah\'e4-p\'e4taka}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 atip\'e4taka}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 \emdash and also into two divisions; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pr\'e4
rabdha}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 apr\'e4rabdha.}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Pr\'e4rabdha}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 refers to sinful reactions from which one is suffering at the present, and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 apr\'e4rabdha}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  refers to sources of potential suffering. When the seeds (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 b\'e9ja}{
\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ) of sinful reactions have not yet fructified, the reactions are called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 apr\'e4rabdha.}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 These seeds of sinful action are unseen, but they are unlimited, and no one can trace when they were first planted. Because of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pr\'e4rabdha,}{\insrsid10252087 
 sinful reactions that have already fructified, one is seen to have taken birth in a low family or to be suffering from other miseries.
\par When one takes to devotional service, however, all phases of sinful life, including }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pr\'e4rabdha, apr\'e4rabdha}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 b\'e9ja,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 are vanquished. In }{\cs2542\i\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (11.14.19) Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba tells Uddhava:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yath\'e4gni\'f9 susam\'e5ddh\'e4rci\'f9\line karoty edh\'e4\'e0si bhasmas\'e4t\line 
tath\'e4 mad-vi\'f1ay\'e4 bhaktir\line uddhavain\'e4\'e0si k\'e5tsna\'e7a\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 "My dear Uddhava, devotional service in relationship with Me
 is like a blazing fire that can burn to ashes all the fuel of sinful activities supplied to it." How devotional service vanquishes the reactions of sinful life is explained in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (3.33.6) in a verse spoken during Lord Kapiladeva's instructions to His mother, Devah\'fcti. Devah\'fcti said:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yan-n\'e4madheya-\'e7rava\'eb\'e4nuk\'e9rtan\'e4d\line yat-prahva\'eb\'e4d yat-smara
\'eb\'e4d api kvacit\line \'e7v\'e4do 'pi sadya\'f9 savan\'e4ya kalpate\line kuta\'f9 punas te bhagavan nu dar\'e7an\'e4t
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"My dear Lord, if even a person born in a family of dog-eaters hears and repeats the chanting of Your glories, offers respects to You and remembers You, he is immediately greater than a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  and is therefore eligible to perform sacrifices. Therefore, what is to be said of one who has seen You directly?"
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 In the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba}{
\insrsid10252087  there is a statement that persons whose hearts are always attached to the devotional service of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u are immediately released from all the reactions of sinful life. These reactions generally exist in four phases. Some of them are ready to produce re
sults immediately, some are in the form of seeds, some are unmanifested, and some are current. All such reactions are immediately nullified by devotional service. When devotional service is present in one's heart, desires to perform sinful activities have
 no place there. Sinful life is due to ignorance, which means forgetfulness of one's constitutional position as an eternal servant of God, but when one is fully K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious he realizes that he is God's eternal servant.
\par In this regard, \'c7r\'e9la J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9 comments that }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bhakti}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  may be divided into two divisions: (1) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 santat\'e4,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 devotional service that continues incessantly with faith and love, and (2) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 k\'e4d\'e4citk\'e9,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 devotional service that does not continue incessantly but is sometimes awakened. Incessantly flowing devotional service (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 santat\'e4}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
) may also be divided into two categories: (1) service performed with slight attachment and (2) spontaneous devotional service. Intermittent devotional service (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 k\'e4d\'e4citk\'e9}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
) may be divided into three categories: (1) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 r\'e4g\'e4bh\'e4samay\'e9,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  devotional service in which one is almost attached, (2) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 r\'e4g\'e4bh\'e4sa-\'e7\'fcnya-svar
\'fcpa-bh\'fct\'e4,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  devotional service in which there is no spontaneous love but one likes the constitutional position of serving, and (3) }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e4bh\'e4sa-r\'fcp\'e4,}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  a slight glimpse of devotional service. As for atonement, if one has caught even a slight glimpse of devotional service, all needs to undergo }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pr\'e4ya\'e7citta,}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  atonement, are superseded. Therefore atonement is certainly unnecessary when one has achieved spontaneous love and, above that, attachment with love, which are signs of increasing advancement in }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 k\'e4d\'e4citk\'e9.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  Even in the stage of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e4bh\'e4sa-r\'fcp\'e4 bhakti,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 all the reactions of sinful life are uprooted and vanquished. \'c7r\'e9la J\'e9va Gosv\'e4m\'e9 expresses the opinion that the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 k\'e4rtsnyena}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  means that even if
 one has a desire to commit sinful actions, the roots of that desire are vanquished merely by }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e4bh\'e4sa-r\'fcp\'e4 bhakti.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  The example of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4skara,}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  the sun, is most appropriate. The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e4bh\'e4sa}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  feature of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bhakti}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 is compared to twilight, and the accumulation of one's sin
ful activities is compared to fog. Since fog does not spread throughout the sky, the sun need do no more than merely manifest its first rays, and the fog immediately disappears. Similarly, if one has even a slight relationship with devotional service, all
 the fog of his sinful life is immediately vanquished.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.1.16
\par }\pard\plain \s2995\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 TEXT 16
