\'f2a}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  but are not at least slight
ly devoted cannot be purified simply by following these other paths. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pr\'e4ya\'e7citt\'e4ni}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  is plural in number to indicate both }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  Narottama d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4
kura therefore says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a, j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a, kevala vi\'f1era bh\'e4\'eb\'f2a.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  Thus Narottama d\'e4sa \'d6h\'e4kura compares the paths of }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-k\'e4\'eb\'f2a}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 to pots of poison. Liquor and poison are in the same category. According to this verse from }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 a person who has heard a good deal about the path of devotional service, but who is not attached to it, who is not K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious, is like a pot of liquor. Such a person cannot be purified without at least a slight touch of devotional service.

\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.1.19
