Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  (18.66):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya\line m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja\line aha\'e0 tv
\'e4\'e0 sarva-p\'e4pebhyo\line mok\'f1ayi\'f1y\'e4mi m\'e4 \'e7uca\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"Abandon all varieties of religion and just surrender unto Me. I shall deliver you from all sinful reaction. Do not fear." This same principle is described here (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sak\'e5n mana\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pad\'e4ravindayo\'f9}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ). If by studying }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  one decides to surrender to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, he is immediately freed from all sinful reactions. It is also significant that \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9, having several times repeated the words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 v\'e4sudeva-par\'e4ya\'eba}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-par\'e4ya\'eba,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  finally says }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pad\'e4
ravindayo\'f9.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  Thus he indicates that K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the origin of both N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba and V\'e4sudeva. Even though N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba and V\'e4sudeva are not different from K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, simply by surrendering to K\'e5\'f1\'eba one fully surrenders to all His expansions, such as N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, V\'e4sudeva and Govinda. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (7.7), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 matta\'f9 paratara\'e0 n\'e4nyat:}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 "There is no truth superior to Me." There are many names and forms of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the supreme form (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5\'f1\'ebas tu bhagav\'e4n svayam}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ). Therefore K\'e5\'f1\'eba recommends to neophyte devotees that one should surrender unto Him only (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4m ekam}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
). Because neophyte devotees cannot understand what the forms of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, V\'e4sudeva and Govinda are, K\'e5\'f1\'eba directly says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4m ekam.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 Herein, this is also supported by the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pad\'e4ravindayo\'f9.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba does not speak personally, but K\'e5\'f1\'eba, or V\'e4
sudeva does, as in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  for example. Therefore, to follow the direction of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  means to surrender unto K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and to surrender in this way is the highest perfection of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhakti-yoga.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 Par\'e9k\'f1it Mah\'e4r\'e4ja had inquired from \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4
m\'e9 how one can be saved from falling into the various conditions of hellish life. In this verse \'c7ukadeva Gosv\'e4m\'e9 answers that a soul who has surrendered to K\'e5\'f1\'eba certainly cannot go to }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 naraka,}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  hellish existence. To say nothing of going there, even in his dreams he does not see Yamar\'e4
ja or his order carriers, who are able to take one there. In other words, if one wants to save himself from falling into }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 naraka,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  hell
ish life, he should fully surrender to K\'e5\'f1\'eba. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sak\'e5t}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  is significant because it indicates that if one sincerely surrenders to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a once, he is saved even if by chance he falls down by committing sinful activities. Therefore K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (9.30):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 api cet su-dur\'e4c\'e4ro\line bhajate m\'e4m ananya-bh\'e4k\line s\'e4
dhur eva sa mantavya\'f9\line samyag vyavasito hi sa\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s3023\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9723571 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
"Even if one commits the most abominable actions, if he is engaged in devotional service he is to be considered saintly because he is properly situated." If one never for a moment forgets K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, he is safe even if by chance he falls down by committing sinful acts.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 In the Second Chapter of }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
