\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 The sinful actions of one who has surrendered unto K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a are compared to a snake with its poison fangs removed (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 protkh\'e4ta-da\'e0\'f1\'f6r\'e4yate}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
). Such a snake is no longer to be feared. Of course, one should not commit sinful activities on the strength of having surrendered to K\'e5\'f1\'eba. However, even if one who has surrendered to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a happens to do something sinful because of his former habits, such sinful actions no longer have a destructive effect. Therefore one should adhere to the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eba very tightly and serve Him under the
 direction of the spiritual master. Thus in all conditions one will be }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 akuto-bhaya,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  free from fear.
