ja were snatching the soul from the core of the heart of Aj\'e4mila, the husband of the prostitute, but with resounding voices the messengers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, forbade them to do so.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s3008\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3348640 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 A Vai\'f1\'ebava, one who has surrendered to the lotus feet of Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u, is always protected by Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu's order carriers. Because Aj\'e4mila had chanted the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas not only immediately arrived on the spot but also at once ordered the Yamad\'fc
tas not to touch him. By speaking with resounding voices, the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas threatened to punish the Yamad\'fctas if they continued trying to snatch Aj\'e4mila's soul from his heart. The order carriers of Yamar\'e4
ja have jurisdiction over all sinful living entities, but the messengers of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, are capable of punishing anyone, including Yamar\'e4ja, if he wrongs a Vai\'f1\'ebava.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
Materialistic scientists do not know where to find the soul within the body with their material instruments, but this verse clearly explains that the soul is within the core of the heart (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 h\'e5daya}{
\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ); it is from the heart that the Yamad\'fctas were extracting the soul of Aj\'e4mila. Similarly, we learn that the Supersoul, Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, is also situated within the heart (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e9\'e7
vara\'f9 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0 h\'e5d-de\'e7e 'rjuna ti\'f1\'f6hati}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ). In the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Upani\'f1ads}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 it is said that the Supersoul and the individual soul are living in the same tree of the body as two friendly birds. The Supersoul is said to be friendly because the Supreme Personality of Godhead is so kind to the original soul that when th
e original soul transmigrates from one body to another, the Lord goes with him. Furthermore, according to the desire and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 karma}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  of the individual soul, the Lord, through the agency of }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 m\'e4y\'e4,}{\insrsid10252087  creates another body for him.
\par The heart of the body is a mechanical arrangement. As the Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (18.61):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line h\'e5d-de\'e7e 'rjuna ti\'f1\'f6hati
\line bhr\'e4mayan sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni\line yantr\'e4r\'fc\'f2h\'e4ni m\'e4yay\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"The Supreme Lord is situated in everyone's heart, O Arjuna, and is directing the wanderings of all living entities, who are seated as on a machine, made of the material energy." }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Yantra}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  means a machine, such as an automobile. The driver of the machine of the body is the individual soul, who is also its director or proprietor, but the supreme proprietor is the 
Supreme Personality of Godhead. One's body is created through the agency of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4y\'e4}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma\'eb\'e4 daiva-netre\'eba}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ), and according to one's activities in this life, another vehicle is created, again under the supervision of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 daiv\'e9 m\'e4y\'e4}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 daiv\'e9 hy e\'f1\'e4 gu\'eba-may\'e9 mama m\'e4y\'e4 duratyay\'e4}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
). At the appropriate time, one's next body is immediately chosen, and both the individual soul and the Supersoul transfer to that particular bodily machine. This is the process of transmigration. During transmigration from one body to the next,
 the soul is taken away by the order carriers of Yamar\'e4ja and put into a particular type of hellish life (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 naraka}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
) in order to become accustomed to the condition in which he will live in his next body.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.1.32
