Before even being introduced to a foreigner, one becomes acquainted with him through his dress, bodily features and behavior and can thus understand his position. Therefore when the Yamad\'fctas saw the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fc
tas for the first time, they were surprised. They said, "By your bodily features you appear to be very exalted gentlemen, and you have such celestial power that you have dissipated the darkness of this material world with 
your own effulgences. Why then should you endeavor to stop us from executing our duty?" It will be explained that the Yamad\'fctas, the order carriers of Yamar\'e4ja, mistakenly considered Aj\'e4
mila sinful. They did not know that although he was sinful throughout his entire life, he was purified by constantly chanting the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. In other words, unless one is a Vai\'f1\'ebava, one cannot understand the activities of a Vai
\'f1\'ebava.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 The dress and bodily features of the residents of Vaiku\'eb\'f6
haloka are properly described in these verses. The residents of Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha, who are decorated with garlands and yellow silken garments, have four arms holding various weapons. Thus they conspicuously resemble Lord Vi\'f1\'eb
u. They have the same bodily features as N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba because they have attained the liberation of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 s\'e4r\'fcpya,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 but they nevertheless act as servants. All the residents of Vaiku\'eb\'f6haloka know perfectly well that their master is N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, or K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and that they are all His servants. They are all self-realized souls who are }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 nitya-mukta,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  everlastingly liberated. Although they could conceivably declare themselves N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba or Vi\'f1\'ebu, they never do so; they always remain K\'e5\'f1
\'eba conscious and serve the Lord faithfully. Such is the atmosphere of Vaiku\'eb\'f6haloka. Similarly, one who learns the faithful service of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba through the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement will always remain in Vaiku\'eb\'f6
haloka and have nothing to do with the material world.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.1.37
