ja replied quite properly. They did not manufacture principles of religion or irreligion. Instead, they explained what they had heard from the authority Yamar\'e4ja. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Mah\'e4jano yena gata\'f9 sa panth\'e4\'f9:}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  one should follow the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mah\'e4jana,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  the authorized person. Yamar\'e4
ja is one of twelve authorities. Therefore the servants of Yamar\'e4ja, the Yamad\'fctas, replied with perfect clarity when they said }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7u\'e7ruma}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 ("we have heard"). The members of modern civilization manufacture defective religious principles through speculative concoction. This is not }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 They do not know what is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  and what is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 adharma.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 Therefore, as stated in the beginning of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam, dharma\'f9 projjhita-kaitavo 'tra:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  not supported by the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vedas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  is rejected from }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7r\'e9mad-bh\'e4gavata-dharma.}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  comprises only that which is given by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja:}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  one must accept the authority of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and surrender to Him and whatever He says. That is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma.}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  Arjuna, for example, thinking that violence was }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 adharma,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  was declining to fight, but K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a urged him to fight. Arjuna abided by the orders of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and therefore he is actually a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharm\'e9}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  because the order of K\'e5\'f1\'eba is }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  (15.15), }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vedai\'e7 ca sarvair aham eva vedya\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  "The real purpose of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 veda,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 knowledge, is to know Me." One who knows K\'e5\'f1\'eba perfectly is liberated. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  (4.9):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 janma karma ca me divyam\line eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9\line tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0
 punar janma\line naiti m\'e4m eti so 'rjuna
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"One who knows the transcendental nature of My appearance and activities does not, upon leaving the body, take his birth again in this material world, but attains My eternal abode, O Arjuna." One who understands K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a and abides by His order is a candidate for returning home, back to Godhead. It may be concluded that }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  religion, refers to that which is ordered in the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vedas,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 adharma,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  irreligion, refers to that which is not supported in the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vedas.
\par }\pard\plain \s3022\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid14314150 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 Dharma is not actually manufactured by N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. As stated in the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Vedas, asya mahato bh\'fctasya ni\'e7vasitam etad yad \'e5g-veda\'f9 iti:}{\insrsid10252087  the injunctions of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 dharma}{\insrsid10252087  emanate from the breathing of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a, the supreme living entity. N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba exists eternally and breathes eternally, and therefore }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 dharma,}{\insrsid10252087  the injunctions of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, also exist eternally. \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4
rya, the original }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e4c\'e4rya}{\insrsid10252087  for those who belong to the M\'e4dhva-Gau\'f2\'e9ya-samprad\'e4ya, says:
