\b\f35\fs36\cf8\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid741136 CHAPTER TWO\line }{\insrsid10252087 Aj\'e4mila Delivered by the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.2 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 In this chapter the messengers from Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha explain to the Yamad\'fc
tas the glories of chanting the holy name of the Lord. The Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas said, "Now impious acts are being performed even in an assembly of devotees, for a person who is not punishable is going to be punished in the assembly of Yamar\'e4
ja. The mass of people are helpless and must depend upon the government for their safety and security, but if the government takes advantage of this to harm the citizens, where will they go? We see perfectly that Aj\'e4
mila should not be punished, although you are attempting to take him to Yamar\'e4ja for punishment."
\par It was due to Aj\'e4mila's glorifying the holy name of the Supreme Lord that he was not punishable. The Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas explained this as follows: "Simply by once chanting the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, this }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma
\'eba}{\insrsid10252087  has become free from the reactions of sinful life. Indeed, he has been freed not only from the sins of this life, but from the sins of many, many thousands o
f other lives. He has already undergone true atonement for all his sinful actions. If one atones according to the directions of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras,}{\insrsid10252087 
 one does not actually become free from sinful reactions, but if one chants the holy name of the Lord, even a glimps
e of such chanting can immediately free one from all sins. Chanting the glories of the Lord's holy name awakens all good fortune. Therefore there is no doubt that Aj\'e4mila, being completely free from all sinful reactions, should not be punished by Yamar
\'e4ja."
\par As they were saying this, the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas released Aj\'e4mila from the ropes of the Yamad\'fctas and left for their own abode. The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid10252087  Aj\'e4
mila, however, offered his respectful obeisances to the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas. He could understand how fortunate he was to have chanted the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a at the end of his life. Indeed, he could realize the full significance of this good fortune. Having thoroughly understood the discussion between the Yamad\'fctas and the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, he became a pure devotee of the Supreme Pers
onality of Godhead. He lamented very much for how very sinful he had been, and he condemned himself again and again.
\par Finally, because of his association with the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas, Aj\'e4mila, his original consciousness aroused, gave up everything and went to Hardwa
r, where he engaged in devotional service without deviation, always thinking of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Thus the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fctas went there, seated him on a golden throne and took him away to Vaiku\'eb\'f6haloka.
\par In summary, although the sinful Aj\'e4mila meant to call his son, the holy name of Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, even though chanted in the preliminary stage, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 n\'e4m\'e4bh\'e4sa,}{\insrsid10252087 
 was able to give him liberation. Therefore one who chants the holy name of the Lord with faith and devotion is certainly exalted. He is protected even in his material, conditional life.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.2.1
