a-k\'e9rtana\'f9\line h\'e5dy anta\'f9-stho hy abhadr\'e4\'ebi\line vidhunoti suh\'e5t sat\'e4m
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 "\'c7r\'e9 K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the Personality of Godhead, who is the Param\'e4tm\'e4 [Supersoul] in everyone's heart and the benefactor of the truthful devotee, cleanses desire for material enjoyment from 
the heart of the devotee who relishes His messages, which are in themselves virtuous when properly heard and chanted." It is the special mercy of the Supreme Lord that as soon as He knows that one is glorifying His name, fame and attributes, He personally
 }{\cs3027\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 helps cleanse the dirt from one's heart. Therefore simply by such glorification one not only becomes purifie}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
d, but also achieves the results of pious activities (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pu\'ebya-\'e7rava\'eba-k\'e9rtana}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ). }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Pu\'ebya-\'e7rava\'eba-k\'e9rtana}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  refers to the process of devotional service. Eve
n if one does not understand the meaning of the Lord's name, pastimes or attributes, one is purified simply by hearing or chanting of them. Such purification is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sattva-bh\'e4vana.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
One's main purpose in human life should be to purify his existence and a
chieve liberation. As long as one has a material body, one is understood to be impure. In such an impure, material condition, one cannot enjoy a truly blissful life, although everyone seeks it. Therefore }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9
mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (5.5.1) says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tapo divya\'e0 putrak\'e4 yena sattva\'e0 \'e7uddhyet:}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  one must perform }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tapasya,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  austerity, to purify his existence in order to come to the spiritual platform. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tapasya}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  of chanting and glorifying the name, fame and attributes of the Lord is a very easy purifying process by which every
one can be happy. Therefore everyone who desires the ultimate cleansing of his heart must adopt this process. Other processes, such as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma, j\'ef\'e4na}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yoga,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  cannot cleanse the heart absolutely.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.2.13
