Just as the driver of a bullock cart ties ropes through the nostrils of his bulls to control them, the Supreme Personality of Godhead binds al
l men through the ropes of His words in the Vedas, which set forth the names and activities of the distinct orders of human society [br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya and \'e7\'fc
dra]. In fear, the members of these orders all worship the Supreme Lord by offering Him presentations according to their respective activities.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
In this material world, everyone is conditioned, regardless of who he is. One may be a human being, a demigod or an animal, tree or plant, but everything is controlled by the laws of nature, and
 behind this natural control is the Supreme Personality of Godhead. This is confirmed by }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  (9.10), wherein K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 may\'e4dhyak\'f1e\'eba prak\'e5ti\'f9 s\'fcyate sa-car\'e4caram:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  "The material nature is working under My direction and producing all moving and n
onmoving beings." Thus K\'e5\'f1\'eba is behind the natural machine, which works under His control.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
Apart from other living entities, the living being in the human form of body is systematically controlled by the Vedic injunctions in terms of the divisions of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 var\'eba}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e4\'e7rama.}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  A human being is expected to follow the rules and regulations of }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 var\'eba}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e4\'e7rama;}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  otherwise he cannot escape punishment by Yamar\'e4
ja. The point is that every human being is expected to elevate himself to the position of a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  the most in
telligent man, and then one must transcend that position to become a Vai\'f1\'ebava. This is the perfection of life. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'fcdra}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  can elevate themselves by worshiping the Lord according to their activities (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sve sve karma\'eby abhirata\'f9 sa\'e0
siddhi\'e0 labhate nara\'f9}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ). The divisions of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 var\'eba}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e4\'e7rama}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  are necessary to insure the proper execution of duties and peaceful existence for everyone, but everyone is directed to worship the Supreme Lord, who is all-pervading (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
yena sarvam ida\'e0 tatam}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ). The Supreme Lord exists vertically and horizontally (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ota\'e0 protam}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
), and therefore if one follows the Vedic injunctions by worshiping the Supreme Lord according to one's ability, his life will be perfect. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (1.2.13):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ata\'f9 pumbhir dvija-\'e7re\'f1\'f6h\'e4\line var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-vibh\'e4ga\'e7a\'f9
\line svanu\'f1\'f6hitasya dharmasya\line sa\'e0siddhir hari-to\'f1a\'ebam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"O best among the twice-born, it is therefore concluded that the highest perfection one can achieve, by discharging his prescribed duties }{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid7592 [}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma}{
\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid7592 ]}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  according to caste divisions and orders of life, is to please the Lord Hari." The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  institution offers the perfect process for making one eligible to return home, back to Godhead, because the aim of every }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 var\'eba}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e4\'e7rama}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  is to please the Supreme Lord. One can please the L
