is who occupy the topmost planets cannot ascertain the real religious principles, nor can the demigods or the leaders of Siddhaloka, to say nothing of the asuras, ordinary human beings, Vidy\'e4dharas and C\'e4ra\'ebas.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 When challenged by the Vi\'f1\'ebud\'fc
tas to describe the principles of religion, the Yamad\'fctas said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 veda-pra\'ebihito dharma\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 the religious principles are the principles enacted in the Vedic literature. They did not know, however, that the Vedic
 literature contains ritualistic ceremonies that are not transcendental, but are meant to keep peace and order among materialistic persons in the material world. Real religious principles are }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 nistraigu\'ebya,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  above the three modes of material nature, or transcendental. The Yamad\'fctas did not know these transcendental religious principles, and therefore when prevented from arresting Aj\'e4
mila they were surprised. Materialistic persons who attach all their faith to the Vedic rituals are described in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  (2.42), wherein K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 veda-v\'e4da-rat\'e4\'f9 p\'e4rtha n\'e4nyad ast\'e9ti v\'e4dina\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  the supposed followers of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vedas}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  say that there is nothing beyond the Vedic ceremonies. Indeed, there is a group of men in India who are very fond of the Vedic rituals, not underst
anding the meaning of these rituals, which are intended to elevate one gradually to the transcendental platform of knowing K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vedai\'e7 ca sarvair aham eva vedya\'f9}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 ). Those who do not know this principle but who simply attach their faith to the Vedic rituals are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 veda-v\'e4da-rat\'e4\'f9.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
Herein it is stated that the real religious principle is that which is given by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. That principle is stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4.}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja:}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  one should give up all other duties and surrender unto the lotus feet of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. That is the real religious principle everyone should follow. Even though one follows Vedic scriptures, one may not know this transcendental principle, for it is not known to everyone. To say not
hing of human beings, even the demigods in the upper planetary systems are unaware of it. This transcendental religious principle must be understood from the Supreme Personality of Godhead directly or from His special representative, as stated in the next
 verses.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.3.20, SB 6.3.21, SB 6.3.20-21
