\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba refers to }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  as the most confidential religious principle (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sarva-guhyatamam, guhy\'e4d guhyataram}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 ). K\'e5\'f1\'eba says to Arjuna, "Because you are My very dear friend, I am explaining to you the most confidential religion." }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 "Give up all other duties and surrender unto Me." One may ask, "If this principle is very rarely understood, what is the use of it?" In answer, Yamar\'e4ja states herein that this religious principle is understandable if one follows the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 parampar\'e4}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  system of Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva, the four Kum\'e4
ras and the other standard authorities. There are four lines of disciplic succession: one from Lord Brahm\'e4, one from Lord \'c7iva, one from Lak\'f1m\'e9, the goddess of fortune, and one from the Kum\'e4ras. The disciplic succession from Lord Brahm\'e4
 is called the Brahma-samprad\'e4ya, the succession from Lord \'c7iva (\'c7ambhu) is called the Rudra-samprad\'e4ya, the one from the goddess of fortune, Lak\'f1m\'e9j\'e9, is called the \'c7r\'e9-samprad\'e4ya, and the one from the Kum\'e4
ras is called the Kum\'e4ra-samprad\'e4ya. One must take shelter of one of these four }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 samprad\'e4yas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 in order to understand the most confidential religious system. In the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 samprad\'e4ya-vih\'e9n\'e4
 ye mantr\'e4s te ni\'f1phal\'e4 mat\'e4\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  if one does not follow the four recognized disciplic successions, his }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mantra}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  or initiation is useless. In the present day there are many }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 apasamprad\'e4yas,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  or }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 samprad\'e4yas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  which are not bona fide, which have no link to authorities like Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva, the Kum\'e4ras or Lak\'f1m\'e9
. People are misguided by such }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 samprad\'e4yas.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 say that being initiated in such a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 samprad\'e4ya}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  is a useless waste of time, for it will never enable one to understand the real religious principles.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.3.22
