\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  the preliminary study of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  What are these principles? The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh
\'e4gavatam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma\'f9 projjhita-kaitavo 'tra:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  there are no cheating religious systems. Everything in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  is directly connected with the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavatam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  further says, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sa vai pu\'e0s\'e4\'e0 paro dharmo yato bhaktir adhok\'f1aje:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
the supreme religion is that which teaches its followers how to love the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is beyond the reach of experimental knowledge. Such a religious system begins with }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tan-n\'e4ma-graha\'eba,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  chanting of the holy name of the Lord (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7rava\'eba\'e0 k\'e9rtana\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebo\'f9 smara\'eba\'e0 p\'e4da-sevanam}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 ). After chanting the holy name of the Lord and dancing in ecstasy, one gradually sees the form of the Lord, the pastimes of the Lord and the transcendental qualities of the Lord. This way
 one fully understands the situation of the Personality of Godhead. One can come to this understanding of the Lord, how He descends into the material world, how He takes His births and what activities He performs, but one can know this only by executing d
evotional service. As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhakty\'e4 m\'e4m abhij\'e4n\'e4ti:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 simply by devotional service one can understand everything about the Supreme Lord. If one fortunately understands the Supreme Lord in this way, the result is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tyaktv\'e4
 deha\'e0 punar janma naiti:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
after giving up his material body, he no longer has to take birth in this material world. Instead, he returns home, back to Godhead. That is the ultimate perfection. Therefore K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4
}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  (8.15):
