\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
All these quotations prove that one who constantly engages in chanting and hearing of the holy activities, name, fame and form of the Lord is liberated. As stated wonderfully in this verse, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 et\'e4vat\'e4
lam agha-nirhara\'eb\'e4ya pu\'e0s\'e4m:}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  simply by uttering the name of the Lord, one is freed from all sinful reactions.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 alam,}{
\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  which is used in this verse, indicates that simply uttering the holy name of the Lord is sufficient. This word is used with different imports. As stated in the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Amara-ko\'e7a,}{
\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  the most authorized dictionary in the Sanskrit language, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 ala\'e0 bh\'fc\'f1a\'eba-pary\'e4pti-\'e7akti-v\'e4ra\'eba-v\'e4cakam:}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  the word }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 alam}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  is used to mean "ornament," "sufficiency," "power" and "restraint." Here the word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 alam}{\insrsid10252087 
 is used to indicate that there is no need of any other process, for the chanting of the holy name of the Lord is sufficient. Even if one chants imperfectly, one becomes free from all sinful reactions by chanting.
\par This power of chanting the holy name was proved by the liberation of Aj\'e4mila. When Aj\'e4mila chanted the holy name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, he did not precisely remember the Supreme Lord; instead, he remembered his own son. At the time of death, Aj\'e4
mila certainly was not very clean; indeed, he was famous as a great sinner. Furthermore, one's physiological condition is completely disturbed at the time of death, and in such an awkward condition it would certainly have been very difficult for Aj\'e4
mila to have chanted clearly. Nevertheless, Aj\'e4mila achieved liberation simply by chanting the holy name of the Lord. Therefore, what is to be said of those who are not sinful like Aj\'e4
mila? It is to be concluded that with a strong vow one should chant the holy name of the Lord\emdash Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4ma, Hare Hare\emdash 
for thus one will certainly be delivered from the clutches of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 m\'e4y\'e4}{\insrsid10252087  by the grace of K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par The chanting of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 is recommended even for persons who commit offenses, because if they continue chanting they will gradually chant offenselessly. By chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 without offenses, one increases his love for K\'e5\'f1\'eba. As stated by \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 prem\'e4 pum-artho mah\'e4n:}{\insrsid10252087 
 one's main concern should be to increase one's attachment to the Supreme Personality of Godhead and to increase one's love for Him.
\par In this regard \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura quotes the following verse from }{\cs2542\i\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (11.19.24):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 eva\'e0 dharmair manu\'f1y\'e4\'eb\'e4m\line uddhav\'e4tmani vedin\'e4m\line mayi sa
