\line j\'e4n\'e4ti tattva\'e0 bhagavan-mahimno\line na c\'e4nya eko 'pi cira\'e0 vicinvan
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
The purport is that even though one is a very learned scholar of the Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 he may be completely unaware of the existence of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and His name, fame, qualities and so forth, where
as one who is not a great scholar can understand the position of the Supreme Personality of Godhead if he somehow or other becomes a pure devotee of the Lord by engaging in devotional service. Therefore this verse spoken by Yamar\'e4ja says, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 eva\'e0 vim\'e5\'e7ya sudhiyo bhagavati:}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  those who engage in the loving service of the Lord become }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sudhiya\'f9,}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  intelligent, but this is not so of a Vedic scholar who does not understand K\'e5\'f1\'eba's name, fame and qualities. A pure devotee is one whose intelligence is clear; he is truly t
houghtful because he engages in the service of the Lord\emdash 
not as a matter of show, but with love, with his mind, words and body. Nondevotees may make a show of religion, but it is not very effective because although they ostentatiously attend a temple or chu
rch, they are thinking of something else. Such persons are neglecting their religious duty and are punishable by Yamar\'e4
ja. But a devotee who commits sinful acts, which he may do unwillingly or accidentally because of his former habits, is excused. That is the value of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sa\'eck\'e9rtana}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  movement.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.3.27
