\par }\pard\plain \s3000\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid741136 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
Anything expressed by material vibrations, anything ascertained by material i
ntelligence and anything experienced by the material senses or concocted within the material mind is but an effect of the modes of material nature and therefore has nothing to do with the real nature of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The Supreme Lord
 is beyond the creation of this material world, for He is the source of the material qualities and creation. As the cause of all causes, He exists before the creation and after the creation. I wish to offer my respectful obeisances unto Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 One who
 manufactures names, forms, qualities or paraphernalia pertaining to the Supreme Personality of Godhead cannot understand Him, since He is beyond creation. The Supreme Lord is the creator of everything, and this means that He existed when there was no cre
ation. In other words, His name, form and qualities are not materially created entities; they are transcendental always. Therefore by our material concoctions, vibrations and thoughts we cannot ascertain the Supreme Lord. This is explained in the verse }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ata\'f9 \'e7r\'e9-k\'e5\'f1\'eba-n\'e4m\'e4di na bhaved gr\'e4hyam indriyai\'f9.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 Pr\'e4cetasa, Dak\'f1
a, herein offers prayers unto the Transcendence, not to anyone within the material creation. Only fools and rascals think God a material creation. This is confirmed by the Lord Himself in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (9.11):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 avaj\'e4nanti m\'e4\'e0 m\'fc\'f2h\'e4\line m\'e4nu\'f1\'e9\'e0 tanum \'e4\'e7ritam
\line para\'e0 bh\'e4vam aj\'e4nanto\line mama bh\'fcta-mahe\'e7varam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"Fools deride Me when I descend in the human form. They do not know My transcendental nature and My supreme dominion over all that be." Therefore, one mu
st receive knowledge from a person to whom the Lord has revealed Himself; there is no value in creating an imaginary name or form for the Lord. \'c7r\'e9p\'e4da \'c7a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya was an impersonalist, but nevertheless he said, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba\'f9 paro 'vyakt\'e4t:}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is not a person of the material world. We cannot assign N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a a material designation, as the foolish attempt to do when they speak of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 daridra-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (poor N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba). N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a is always transcendental, beyond this material creation. How can He become }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 daridra-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
? Poverty is found within this material world, but in the spiritual world, there is no such thing as poverty. Therefore the idea of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 daridra-n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 is merely a concoction.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 Dak\'f1a very carefully points out that mat
erial designations cannot be names of the worshipable Lord: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yad yan nirukta\'e0 vacas\'e4 nir\'fcpitam.}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Nirukta}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  refers to the Vedic dictionary. One cannot properly understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead merely by picking up expressions from a dictionary. In praying to the Lord, Dak\'f1
a does not wish material names and forms to be the objects of his worship; rather, he wants to worship the Lord, who existed before the creation of material dictionaries and names. As confirmed in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vedas, yato v\'e4
co nivartante/ apr\'e4pya manas\'e4 saha:}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 the name, form, attributes and paraphernalia of the Lord cannot be ascertained through a material dictionary. However, if one reaches the transcendental platform of understanding the Supreme Personality of Godhead, he becomes well acqua
inted with everything, material and spiritual. This is confirmed in another Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mantra:}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tam eva viditv\'e4ti m\'e5tyum eti.}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  If one can somehow or other, by the grace of the Lord, understand the transcendental position of the Lord, one becomes eternal. This is further confirmed by the Lord Himself in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (4.9):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 janma karma ca me divyam\line eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9\line tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0
