\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid3943952 SYNONYMS}{\v\fs28\insrsid10252087 
\par }\pard\plain \s3019\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb240\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1521817 \f35\fs28\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 ya\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
who (the Supreme Personality of Godhead); }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 anugraha-artham}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash to show His causeless mercy; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bhajat\'e4m}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
to the devotees who always render devotional service; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 p\'e4da-m\'fclam}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash to His transcendental lotus feet; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 an\'e4ma}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash with no material name; }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 r\'fcpa\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash or material form; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bhagav\'e4n}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 ananta\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
unlimited, all-pervading and eternally existing; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 n\'e4m\'e4ni}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash transcendental holy names; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 r\'fcp\'e4\'ebi}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash His transcendental forms; }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 ca}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash also; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 janma-karmabhi\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash with His transcendental birth and activities; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 bheje}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash manifests; }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 sa\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash He; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mahyam}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash unto me; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 parama\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash the Supreme; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pras\'e9datu}{
\insrsid10252087 \emdash may He be merciful.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3000\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid741136 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
The Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is inconceivably opulent, who is devoid of all material names, forms and pastimes, and who is all-pervading, is especially merciful to the devotees who worship His lotus feet. Thus He exhib
its transcendental forms and names with His different pastimes. May that Supreme Personality of Godhead, whose form is eternal and full of knowledge and bliss, be merciful to me.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 In regard to the significant word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 an\'e4ma-r\'fcpa\'f9
,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  \'c7r\'e9 \'c7r\'e9dhara Sv\'e4m\'e9 says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pr\'e4k\'e5ta-n\'e4ma-r\'fcpa-rahito 'pi.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 an\'e4ma,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  which means "having no name," indicates that the Supreme Personality of Godhead has no material name. Simply by chanting the name of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba to call his son, Aj\'e4mila attained salvation. This means that N\'e4r\'e4ya
\'eba is not an ordinary mundane name; it is nonmaterial. The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 an\'e4ma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 therefore, indicates that the names of the Supreme Lord do not belong to this material world. The vibration of the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mah\'e4-mantra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 is not a material sound, and similarly the form of the Lord and His appearance and activities are all nonmaterial. To show His causeless mercy to the devotees, as well as to the nondevotees, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, appears in this material world with names, forms and pastimes, all 
of which are transcendental. Unintelligent men who cannot understand this think that these names, forms and pastimes are material, and therefore they deny that He has a name or a form.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
Considered with scrutiny, the conclusion of nondevotees, who say that G
od has no name, and that of devotees, who know that His name is not material, are practically the same. The Supreme Personality of Godhead has no material name, form, birth, appearance or disappearance, but nevertheless, He takes His birth (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 janma}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ). As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (4.6):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ajo 'pi sann avyay\'e4tm\'e4\line bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4m \'e9\'e7varo 'pi san\line prak\'e5
ti\'e0 sv\'e4m adhi\'f1\'f6h\'e4ya\line sambhav\'e4my \'e4tma-m\'e4yay\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 Although the Lord is unborn (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 aja
}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ) and His body never undergoes material changes, He nevertheless appears as an incarnation, maintaining Himself always in the transcendental stage (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7uddha-sattva}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ). Thus He exhibits His transcendental forms, names and activities. That is His special mercy toward His devotees. Others may continue merely arguing about whether the Absolute Truth has form or no
t, but when a devotee, by the grace of the Lord, sees the Lord personally, he becomes spiritual}{\cs3027\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ly ecstatic.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
Unintelligent persons say that the Lord does nothing. Actually He has nothing to do, but nevertheless He has to do everything, because without His s
anction no one can do anything. The unintelligent, however, cannot see how He is working and how the entire material nature is working under His direction. His different potencies work perfectly.
\par }\pard\plain \s1434\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 na tasya k\'e4rya\'e0 kara\'eba\'e0 ca vidyate\line na tat-sama\'e7 c\'e4bhyadhika\'e7
 ca d\'e5\'e7yate\line par\'e4sya \'e7aktir vividhaiva \'e7r\'fcyate\line sv\'e4bh\'e4vik\'e9 j\'ef\'e4na-bala-kriy\'e4 ca\line (}{\cs2542\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7vet\'e4\'e7vatara Upani\'f1ad}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  6.8)}{
\cs1998\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
\par }\pard\plain \s3023\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9723571 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
He has nothing to do personally, for since His potencies are perfect, everything is immediately done by His will. Persons to whom the Supreme Personali
ty of Godhead is not revealed cannot see how He is working, and therefore they think that even if there is God, He has nothing to do or has no particular name.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
Actually the Lord's name already exists because of His transcendental activities. The Lord is sometimes called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 gu\'eba-karma-n\'e4ma}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 because He is named according to His transcendental activities. For example, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 K\'e5\'f1\'eba}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 means "all-attractive." This is the Lord's name because His transcendental qualities make Him very attractive. As a small boy He lifted Govard
hana Hill, and in His childhood He killed many demons. Such activities are very attractive, and therefore He is sometimes called Giridh\'e4r\'e9, Madhus\'fcdana, Agha-ni\'f1\'fcdana and so on. Because He acted as the son of Nanda Mah\'e4r\'e4
ja, He is called Nanda-tanuja. These names already exist, but since nondevotees cannot understand the names of the Lord, He is sometimes called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 an\'e4ma,}{\insrsid10252087 
 or nameless. This means that He has no material names. All His activities are spiritual, and therefore He has spiritual names.
\par Generally, less intelligent men are under the impression that the Lord has no form. Therefore He appears in His original form as K\'e5\'f1\'eba, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 to carry out His mission of participating in the Battle of Kuruk\'f1etra and pastimes to protect the devotees and vanquish the demons (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 paritr\'e4\'eb\'e4ya s\'e4dh\'fcn\'e4\'e0 vin\'e4\'e7\'e4ya ca du\'f1k\'e5t\'e4m}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ). This is His mercy. For those who think that He has no form and no work to do, K\'e5\'f1\'eba comes to show that indeed He works. He works so gloriously that no one else can perform such uncommon act
s. Although He appeared as a human being, He married 16,108 wives, which is impossible for a human being to do. The Lord performs such activities to show people how great He is, how affectionate He is and how merciful He is. Although His original name is 
K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 k\'e5\'f1\'ebas tu bhagav\'e4n svayam}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ), He acts in unlimited ways, and therefore according to His work He has many, many thousands of names.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.4.34
\par }\pard\plain \s2995\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs28\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 TEXT 34
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 TEXT
