YaQaaiNal/" PaaiQaRvMaai\'e9[Taae Gau<a&\line  Sa wR\'ecrae Mae ku-\'e5Taa& MaNaaerQaMa( )) 34 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 ya\'f9 pr\'e4k\'e5tair j\'ef\'e4na-pathair jan\'e4n\'e4\'e0
\par yath\'e4\'e7aya\'e0 deha-gato vibh\'e4ti
\par yath\'e4nila\'f9 p\'e4rthivam \'e4\'e7rito gu\'eba\'e0
\par sa \'e9\'e7varo me kurut\'e4\'e0 manoratham
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid3943952 SYNONYMS}{\v\fs28\insrsid10252087 
\par }\pard\plain \s3019\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb240\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1521817 \f35\fs28\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 ya\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash who; }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pr\'e4k\'e5tai\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash lower grade; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4na-pathai\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash by the paths of worship; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 jan\'e4n\'e4m}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
of all living entities; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yath\'e4-\'e4\'e7ayam}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash according to the desire; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 deha-gata\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash situated within the core of the heart; }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 vibh\'e4ti}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash manifests; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yath\'e4}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash just as; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 anila\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash the air; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 p\'e4
rthivam}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash earthly; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e4\'e7rita\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash receiving; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 gu\'ebam}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash the quality (like flavor and color); }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 sa
\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash He; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 me}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash my; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 kurut\'e4m}{
\insrsid10252087 \emdash may He fulfill; }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 manoratham}{\insrsid10252087 \emdash desire (for devotional service).
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3000\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid741136 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
As the air carries various characteristics of the physical elements, like the aroma of a flower or colors resulti
ng from a mixture of dust in the air, the Lord appears through lower systems of worship according to one's desires, although He appears as the demigods and not in His original form. What is the use of these other forms? May the original Supreme Personalit
y of Godhead please fulfill my desires.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The impersonalists imagine the various demigods to be forms of the Lord. For example, the M
\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9s worship five demigods (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pa\'efcop\'e4san\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). They do not actually believe in the form of the Lord, but for the sake o
f worship they imagine some form to be God. Generally they imagine a form of Vi\'f1\'ebu, a form of \'c7iva, and forms of Ga\'ebe\'e7a, the sun-god and Durg\'e4. This is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pa\'efcop\'e4san\'e4.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Dak\'f1a, however, wanted to worship not an imaginary form, but the supreme form of Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 In this regard, \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart
\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura describes the difference between the Supreme Personality of Godhead and an ordinary living being. As pointed out in a previous verse, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 sarva\'e0 pum\'e4n veda gu\'eb\'e4\'e0\'e7 ca taj-j\'efo na veda sarva j
\'efam anantam \'e9\'f2e:}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  the omnipotent Supreme Lord knows everything, but the living being does not actually know the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  "I know everything, but no one knows Me." This is the difference between the Supreme Lord and an ordinary living being. In a prayer in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{
\insrsid10252087  Queen Kunt\'e9 says, "My dear Lord, You exist inside and outside, yet no one can see You."
\par The conditioned soul cannot understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead by speculative knowledge or by 
imagination. One must therefore know the Supreme Personality of Godhead by the grace of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. He reveals Himself, but He cannot be understood by speculation. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam
}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (10.14.29):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ath\'e4pi te deva pad\'e4mbuja-dvaya-\line pras\'e4da-le\'e7\'e4nug\'e5h\'e9ta eva hi
\line j\'e4n\'e4ti tattva\'e0 bhagavan-mahimno\line na c\'e4nya eko 'pi cira\'e0 vicinvan
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"My Lord, if one is favored by even a slight trace of the mercy of Your lotus feet, he can understand the greatness of Your personality. But those who specul
ate to understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead are unable to know You, even though they continue to study the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vedas}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  for many years."
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 This is the verdict of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 
\'e7\'e4stra.}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  An ordinary man may be a great philosopher and may speculate upon what the Absolute Truth is, what His form is and where He is existing, but be cannot understand these truths. }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Sevonmukhe hi jihv\'e4dau svayam eva sphuraty ada\'f9:}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  one can understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead only through devotional service. This is also explained by 
the Supreme Personality of Godhead Himself in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (18.55). }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Bhakty\'e4 m\'e4m abhij\'e4n\'e4ti y\'e4v\'e4n ya\'e7 c\'e4smi tattvata\'f9:}{
\insrsid10252087  "One can understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead as He is only by devotional service." Unintelligent persons want to imagine or con
coct a form of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but devotees want to worship the actual Personality of Godhead. Therefore Dak\'f1
a prays, "One may think of You as personal, impersonal or imaginary, but I wish to pray to Your Lordship that You fulfill my desires to see You as You actually are."
\par \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura comments that this verse is especially meant for the impersonalist, who thinks that he himself is the Supreme because there is no difference between the living being and God. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d
\'e9 philosopher thinks that there is only one Supreme Truth and that he is also that Supreme Truth. Actually this is not knowledge but foolishness, and this verse is especially meant for such fools, whose knowledge has been stolen by illusion (}{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 m\'e4yay\'e4pah\'e5ta j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'f9}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ). Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura says that such persons, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4ni-m\'e4nina\'f9,}{\insrsid10252087 
 think themselves very advanced, but actually they are unintelligent.
\par In regard to this verse, \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 svadeha-stha\'e0 hari\'e0 pr\'e4hur\line adham\'e4 j\'e9vam eva tu\line madhyam\'e4\'e7
 c\'e4py anir\'eb\'e9ta\'e0\line j\'e9v\'e4d bhinna\'e0 jan\'e4rdanam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 There are three classes of men\emdash the lowest (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 adhama}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ), those in the middle (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 madhyama}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ), and the best (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 uttama}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ). The lowest (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 adhama}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
) think that there is no difference between God and the living entity except that the livi
ng entity is under designations whereas the Absolute Truth has no designations. In their opinion, as soon as the designations of the material body are dissolved, the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'e9va,}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  the living entity, will mix with the Supreme. They give the argument of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 gha\'f6\'e4k\'e4\'e7a-pa\'f6\'e4k\'e4\'e7a,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 in which the body is compared to a pot with the sky within and the sky without. When the pot breaks, the sky inside becomes one with the sky outside, and so the impersonalists say that the living being becomes one with the Supreme. This is their ar
gument, but \'c7r\'e9la Madhv\'e4c\'e4
rya says that such an argument is put forward by the lowest class of men. Another class of men cannot ascertain what the actual form of the Supreme is, but they agree that there is a Supreme who controls the activities of the ordinary}{
\cs3027\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  living being. Such philosophers are accepted as m}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ediocre. The best, however. are those who understand the Supreme Lord (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ). }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 P\'fcr\'eb\'e4nand\'e4di-gu\'ebaka\'e0 sarva j\'e9va-vilak\'f1a\'ebam:}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  His form is completely spiritual, full of bliss, and completely distinct from that of the conditioned soul or any other living entity. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Uttam\'e4s tu hari\'e0 pr\'e4
hus t\'e4ratamyena te\'f1u ca:}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  such philosophers are the best because they know that the Supreme Personality of Godhead reveals Himself differently to worshipers in vari
ous modes of material nature. They know that there are thirty-three million demigods just to convince the conditioned soul that there is a supreme power and to induce him to agree to worship one of these demigods so that by the association of devotee}{
\cs3027\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 s he may be able to understand that K\'e5\'f1\'eba is the Supreme Personality of }{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 Godhead. As Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba says in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 matta\'f9 paratara\'e0 n\'e4nyat ki\'efcid asti dhana\'efjaya:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 "There is no truth superior to Me." }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Aham \'e4dir hi dev\'e4n\'e4m:}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  "I am the origin of all the demigods." }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Aha\'e0 sarvasya prabhava\'f9: }{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 "I am superior to everyone, even Lord Brahm\'e4, Lord \'c7iva and the other demigods." These are the conclusions of the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  and one who accepts these conclusions should be considered a first-class philosopher. Such a philosopher kno
ws that the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the Lord of the demigods (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 deva-deve\'e7vara\'e0 s\'fctram \'e4nanda\'e0 pr\'e4\'eba-vedina\'f9}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ).
