s not come to this platform, he must continue in material existence perpetually, sometimes in the upper planets and sometimes in the lower planets. As confirmed in }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{
\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (}{\cs2542\i\insrsid10252087 Madhya}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  20.118), }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 kabhu svarge u\'f6h\'e4ya, kabhu narake \'f2ub\'e4ya:}{\insrsid10252087  the condition
ed soul sometimes descends into nescience and sometimes gets some relief by being relatively freed from it. This is the life of the conditioned soul.
\par Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a is trying to benefit the conditioned souls by begetting them to give them a life with a chance for liberation. Liberation means surrender to K\'e5\'f1\'eba. If one begets children with the purpose of training them to surrender to K
\'e5\'f1\'eba, fatherhood is very good. Similarly, when the spiritual master trains the conditioned souls to become K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious, his position is successful. If one gives the conditioned souls a chance to become K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious, all his activities are approved by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is extremely pleased, as stated here (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pr\'e9to 'ham}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ). Following the examples of the previous }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e4c\'e4ryas,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  all the members of the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement should try to benefit the conditioned souls by inducing them to become K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious and giving them all facilities to do so. Such activities constitute real welfare work. By such activities, a preacher or anyone who endeavors to spread K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness is recognized by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As the Lord Himself confirms in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (18.68-69):
