\par }\pard\plain \s3000\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid741136 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
Before the creation of this cosmic manifestation, I alone existed with My specific spiritual potencies. Consciousness was then unmanifested, just as one's consciousness is unmanifested during the time of sleep.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 aham}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 indicates a person. As explained in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vedas, nityo nity\'e4n\'e4\'e0 cetana\'e7 cetan\'e4n\'e4m:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 the Lord is the supreme eternal among innumerable eternals and the supreme living being among the innumerable living beings. The Lord is a person who also has impersonal features. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4
gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (1.2.11):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vadanti tat tattva-vidas\line tattva\'e0 yaj j\'ef\'e4nam advayam\line brahmeti param
\'e4tmeti\line bhagav\'e4n iti \'e7abdyate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
"Learned transcendentalists who know the Absolute Truth call this nondual substance Brahman, Param\'e4tm\'e4 or Bhagav\'e4n." Consideration of the Param\'e4tm\'e4
 and impersonal Brahman arose after the creation; before the creation, only the Supreme Personality of Godhead existed. As firmly declared in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 (18.55), the Lord can be understood only by }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhakti-yoga.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  The ultimate cause, the supreme
 cause of creation, is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who can be understood only by }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhakti-yoga.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 He cannot be understood by speculative philosophical research or by meditation, since all such processes came into existence after the material creation. 
The impersonal and localized conceptions of the Supreme Lord are more or less materially contaminated. The real spiritual process, therefore, is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhakti-yoga.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 As the Lord says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhakty\'e4 m\'e4m abhij\'e4n\'e4ti:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 "Only by devotional service can I be understood." Before
 the creation, the Lord existed as a person, as indicated here by the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 aham.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  When Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1
a saw Him as a person, who was beautifully dressed and ornamented, he actually experienced the meaning of this word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 aham}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  through devotional service.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 Each pe
rson is eternal. Because the Lord says that He existed as a person before the creation (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 agre}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
) and will also exist after the annihilation, the Lord is a person eternally. \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4kura therefore quotes these verses from }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (10.9.13-14):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 na c\'e4ntar na bahir yasya\line na p\'fcrva\'e0 n\'e4pi c\'e4param\line p\'fcrv\'e4
para\'e0 bahi\'e7 c\'e4ntar\line jagato yo jagac ca ya\'f9
\par ta\'e0 matv\'e4tmajam avyakta\'e0\line martya-li\'ecgam adhok\'f1ajam\line gopikol\'fckhale d\'e4mn\'e4\line babandha pr\'e4k\'e5ta\'e0 yath\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 The Personality of Godhead appeared in V\'e5nd\'e4vana a
s the son of mother Ya\'e7od\'e4, who bound the Lord with rope just as an ordinary mother binds a material child. There are actually no divisions of external and internal for the form of the Supreme Personality of Godhead (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ), but when He appears in His own form the unintelligent think Him an ordinary person. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Avaj\'e4nanti m\'e4
\'e0 m\'fc\'f2h\'e4 m\'e4nu\'f1\'e9\'e0 tanum \'e4\'e7ritam:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 although He comes in Hi}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid2641942 s own body, which never changes,}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'fc\'f2has,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  the unintelligent, think that the impersonal Brahman has assumed a material bo
dy to come in the form of a person. Ordinary living beings assume material bodies, but the Supreme Personality of Godhead does not. Since the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the supreme consciousness, it is stated herein that }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sa\'e0j\'ef\'e4na-m\'e4tram,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  the original consciousness, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, was unmanifested before the creation, although the consciousness of the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the origin of everything. The Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (2.12), "Never was there a time when I did not exist, n
or you, nor all these kings; nor in the future shall any of us cease to be." Thus the Lord's person is the Absolute Truth in the past, present and future.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 In this regard, Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya quotes two verses from the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Matsya Pur\'e4\'eba:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 n\'e4n\'e4-var\'ebo haris tv eko\line bahu-\'e7\'e9r\'f1a-bhujo r\'fcp\'e4t\line \'e4s
\'e9l laye tad-anyat tu\line s\'fck\'f1ma-r\'fcpa\'e0 \'e7riya\'e0 vin\'e4
\par asupta\'f9 supta iva ca\line m\'e9lit\'e4k\'f1o 'bhavad dhari\'f9\line anyatr\'e4n\'e4dar\'e4d vi\'f1\'ebau\line \'e7r\'e9\'e7 ca l\'e9neva kathyate\line s\'fck\'f1matvena harau sth\'e4n\'e4l\line l\'e9nam anyad ap\'e9\'f1yate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 After the annihilation of everything, the Supreme Lor
d, because of His }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 remains in His original form, but since the other living entities have material bodies, the matter merges into matter, and the subtle form of the spirit soul remains within the body of the Lord. The Lord does not s
leep, but the ordinary living entities remain asleep until the next creation. An unintelligent person thinks that the opulence of the Supreme Lord is nonexistent after the annihilation, but that is not a fact. The opulence of the Supreme Personality of Go
dhead remains as it is in the spiritual world; only in the material world is everything dissolved. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Brahma-l\'e9na,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  merging into the Supreme Brahman, is not actual }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 l\'e9na,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  or annihilation, for the subtle form remaining in the Brahman effulgence will return to the
 material world after the material creation and again assume a material form. This is described as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'fctv\'e4 bh\'fctv\'e4 pral\'e9yate.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
