a were delivered from the clutches of the material energy by following the advice of N\'e4rada, who was therefore cursed by Dak\'f1a.
\par Influenced by the external energy of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a begot ten thousand sons in the womb of his wife, P\'e4\'efcajan\'e9. These sons, who were all of the same character and mentality, were known as the Harya\'e7
vas. Ordered by their father to create more and more population, the Harya\'e7vas went west to the place where the River Sindhu (now the Indus) meets the Arabian Sea. In those days this was the site of a holy lake named N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-saras, wher
e there were many saintly persons. The Harya\'e7vas began practicing austerities, penances and meditation, which are the engagements of the highly exalted renounced order of life. However, when \'c7r\'e9la N\'e4
rada Muni saw these boys engaged in such commendable austerities simply for material creation, he thought it better to release them from this tendency. N\'e4
rada Muni described to the boys their ultimate goal of life and advised them not to become ordinary }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 karm\'e9s}{\insrsid10252087  to beget children. Thus all the sons of Dak\'f1a became enlightened and left, never to return.

\par Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a, who was very sad at the loss of his sons, begot one thousand more sons in the womb of his wife, P\'e4\'efcajan\'e9, and ordered them to increase progeny. These sons, who were named the Saval\'e4\'e7vas, also engage
d in worshiping Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu to beget children, but N\'e4rada Muni convinced them to become mendicants and not beget children. Foiled twice in his attempts to increase population, Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a became most angry at N\'e4
rada Muni and cursed him, saying that in the future he would not be able to stay anywhere. Since N\'e4rada Muni, being fully qualified, was fixed in tolerance, he accepted Dak\'f1a's curse.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.5.1
