\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 prav\'e5tti\'e0 ca niv\'e5tti\'e0 ca jan\'e4 na vidur \'e4sur\'e4\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  demons, who are less than human beings but are not called animals, do not know the meaning of }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 prav\'e5tti}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 niv\'e5tti,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 work to be done and work not to be done. In the material world, every living entity has a desire to lord it over the material world as much as possible. This is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 prav\'e5tti-m\'e4rga.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 All the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  however, advise }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 niv\'e5tti-m\'e4rga,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  or release from the materialistic way of life. Apart from the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  of the Vedic civilization, which is the oldest of the world, other }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 agree on this point. For example, in the Buddhist }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Lord Buddha advises that one achieve }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 nirv\'e4\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 by giving up the materialistic way of life. In the Bible, which is also }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  one will find the same advice: one should cease materialistic li
fe and return to the kingdom of God. In any }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  one may examine, especially the Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 the same advice is given: one should give up his materialistic life and return to his original, spiritual life. \'c7a\'eckar\'e4c\'e4rya also propounds the same conclusion. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Brahma satya\'e0 jagan mithy\'e4:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  this material world or materialistic life is simply illusion, and therefore one should stop his illusory activities and come to the platform of Brahman.
\par }\pard\plain \s3005\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3824524 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 The word }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra}{
\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  refers to the scriptures, particularly the Vedic books of knowledge. The }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Vedas}{\cs3006\insrsid8088079\charrsid3824524 \emdash }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 S\'e4ma, Yajur, \'c5g}{
\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  and }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Atharva}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 \emdash and any other books deriving knowledge from these }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Vedas}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 are considered Vedic literatures. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  is the essence of all Vedic knowledge, and therefore it is the scripture whose instructions should be 
especially accepted. In this essence of all }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras,}{\cs3006\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  K\'e5\'f1\'eba personally advises that one give up all other duties and surrender unto Him (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 
sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja}{\insrsid10252087 ).
\par One should be initiated into following the principles of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  In offering initiation, our K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement asks one to come to the conclusion of }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  by taking the advice of the supreme speaker of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra,}{\insrsid10252087  K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, forgetting the principles of the materialistic way of life. Therefore the principles we advis
e are no illicit sex, no intoxication, no gambling and no meat-eating. These four types of engagement will enable an intelligent person to get free from the materialistic life and return home, back to Godhead.
\par In regard to the instructions of the father an
d mother, it may be said that every living entity, including even the insignificant cats, dogs and serpents, takes birth of a father and mother. Therefore, getting a material father and mother is not a problem. In every form of life, birth after birth, th
e living entity gets a father and mother. In human society, however, if one is satisfied with his material father and mother and their instructions and does not make further progress by accepting a spiritual master and being educated in the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  he cert
ainly remains in darkness. The material father and mother are important only if they are interested in educating their son to become free from the clutches of death. As instructed by \'c5\'f1abhadeva (}{\cs2542\i\insrsid1651685\charrsid1651685 Bh\'e4g.}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  5.5.18): }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pit\'e4 na sa sy\'e4j janan\'e9 na s\'e4 sy\'e4t/ na mocayed ya\'f9 samupeta-m\'e5tyum.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 One should not strive to become a mother or father if one cannot save one's dependent son from the impending danger of death. A parent who does not know how to save his son has no value because such fathers and mothers may be had in an
y form of life, even among the cats, dogs and so on. Only a father and mother who can elevate their son to the spiritual platform are bona fide parents. Therefore according to the Vedic system it is said, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 janman\'e4 j\'e4yate 
\'e7\'fcdra\'f9:}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  one is born of a material father and mother as a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'fcdra.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  The purpose of life, however, is to become a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br
\'e4hma\'eba,}{\insrsid10252087  a first-class man.
\par A first-class intelligent man is called a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  because he knows the Supreme Brahman, the Absolute Truth. According to the Vedic instructions, }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 tad-vij\'ef
\'e4n\'e4rtha\'e0 sa gurum ev\'e4bhigacchet:}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  to know this science, one must approach a bona fide }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 guru,}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 a spiritual master who will initiate the disciple with the sacred thread so that he may understand the Vedic knowledge. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Janman\'e4 j\'e4yate \'e7\'fcdra\'f9 sa\'e0sk\'e4r\'e4d dhi bhaved dvija\'f9.}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  Becoming a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  through the endeavor of a bona fide spiritual master is called }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 sa\'e0sk\'e4ra.}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  After initiation, one is engaged in study of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra,}{\insrsid10252087  which teaches the student how to gain release from materialistic life and return home, back to Godhead.
\par The K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement is teaching this higher knowledge of retiring from materialistic life to return to Godhead, but unfortunately many parents are not very satisfied with this movement. Aside from the parents of our students, many business
men are also dissatisfied because we teach our students to abandon intoxication, meat-eating, illicit sex and gambling. If the K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness movement spreads, the so-called businessmen will have to close their slaughterhouses, breweries and cigarette
 factories. Therefore they are also very much afraid. However, we have no alternative than to teach our disciples to free themselves from materialistic life. We must instruct them in the opposite of material life to save them from the repetition of birth 
and death.
\par N\'e4rada Muni, therefore, advised the Harya\'e7vas, the sons of Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a, that instead of begetting progeny, it would be better to leave and achieve the perfection of spiritual understanding according to the instructions of the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras.}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  The importance of the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras}{\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  is mentioned in }{\cs2542\i\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (16.23):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ya\'f9 \'e7\'e4stra-vidhim uts\'e5jya\line vartate k\'e4ma-k\'e4rata\'f9\line 
na sa siddhim av\'e4pnoti\line na sukha\'e0 na par\'e4\'e0 gatim
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 "One who disregards the injunctions of the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  and acts whimsically, as he likes, never achieves the perfection of life, not to speak of happiness. Nor does he return home to the spiritual world."

