\cs3002\fs28\insrsid10252087\charrsid741136  My dear King, after hearing the instructions of N\'e4rada, the Harya\'e7vas, the sons of Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1
a, were firmly convinced. They all believed in his instructions and reached the same conclusion. Having accepted him as their spiritual master, they circumambulated that great sage and followed the path by which one never returns to this world.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
From this verse we can understand the meaning of initiation and the duties of a disciple and spiritual master. The spiritual master never instructs his disciple, "Take a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 from me, pay me some money, and by practicing this }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yoga}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  system
 you will become very expert in materialistic life." This is not the duty of a spiritual master. Rather, the spiritual master teaches the disciple how to give up materialistic life, and the disciple's duty is to assimilate his instructions and ultimately 
follow the path back home, back to Godhead, from whence no one returns to this material world.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 After hearing the instructions of N\'e4rada Muni, the Harya\'e7
vas, the sons of Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a, decided not to be entangled in materialistic life by begetting hundreds of children and having to take care of them. This would have been unnecessarily entangling. The Harya\'e7
vas did not consider pious and impious activities. Their materialistic father had instructed them to increase the population, but because of the words of N\'e4rada Muni, they could not heed that instruction. N\'e4
rada Muni, as their spiritual master, gave them the \'e7\'e4stric instructions that they should give up this material world, and as bona fide disciples they followed his instructions. One should not endeavor 
to wander to different planetary systems within this universe, for even if one goes to the topmost planetary system, Brahmaloka, one must return again (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'f1\'e9\'ebe pu\'ebye martya-loka\'e0 vi\'e7anti}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 ). The endeavors of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karm\'e9s}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  are a useless waste of time. One should endea
vor to return home, back to Godhead. This is the perfection of life. As the Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  (8.16):
