\par m\'e4dhur\'e9-p\'fcra,     \'e4saba pa\'e7i',\line m\'e4t\'e4ya jagata-jane\line keha v\'e4 k\'e4\'ecde,     keha v\'e4 n\'e4ce,\line keha m\'e4te mane mane
\par pa\'efca-vadana,     n\'e4rade dhari',\line premera saghana rola\line kamal\'e4sana,     n\'e4ciy\'e4 bale,\line 'bola bola hari bola'
\par sahasr\'e4nana,     parama-sukhe,\line 'hari hari' bali' g\'e4ya\line n\'e4ma-prabh\'e4ve,     m\'e4tila vi\'e7va,\line n\'e4ma-rasa sabe p\'e4ya
\par \'e7r\'e9-k\'e5\'f1\'eba-n\'e4ma,     rasane sphuri',\line pur\'e4'la \'e4m\'e4ra \'e4\'e7a\line \'e7r\'e9-r\'fcpa-pade,     y\'e4caye ih\'e4,\line bhakativinoda d\'e4sa
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 The purport of this song is that N\'e4
rada Muni, the great soul, plays a stringed instrument called a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 v\'e9\'eb\'e4,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  vibrating the sound }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 r\'e4dhik\'e4-rama\'eba,}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  which is another name for K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. As soon as he strokes the strings, all the devotees begin responding, making a very beautiful vibration. Accompanied by the stringed instrument, the singing seems like a shower of nectar, and all the devotees dance i
n ecstasy to the fullest extent of their satisfaction. While dancing, they appear madly intoxicated with ecstasy, as if drinking the beverage called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4dhur\'e9-p\'fcra.}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  Some of them cry, some of them dance, and some of them, although unable to dance publicly, dance within their hearts. Lord \'c7iva embraces N\'e4
rada Muni and begins talking in an ecstatic voice, and seeing Lord \'c7iva dancing with N\'e4rada, Lord Brahm\'e4 also joins, saying, "All of you kindly chant 'Hari bol! Hari bol!' " The King of he}{\cs3027\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
aven, Indra, also gradually joins with great satisfaction and begins dancing and chanting "Hari bol! Hari bol!" In this way, by the influence of the transcendental vibration of the holy name of God, the whole universe becomes ecstatic. Bhaktivinoda \'d6h
\'e4kura says, "When the universe becomes ecstatic, my desire is satisfi}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 ed. I therefore pray unto the lotus feet of R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9 that this chanting of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 harer n
\'e4ma}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  may go on nicely like this."
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 Lord Brahm\'e4 is the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 guru}{
\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  of N\'e4rada Muni, who is the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 guru}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  of Vy\'e4sadeva, and Vy\'e4sadeva is the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 guru
}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524  of Madhv\'e4c\'e4rya. Thus the Gau\'f2\'e9ya-M\'e4dhva-samprad\'e4ya is in the disciplic succession from N\'e4rada Muni. The members of this disciplic succession\emdash 
in other words, the members of the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement\emdash should follow in the footsteps of N\'e4rada Muni by chanting the transcendental vibration Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eb
