rada Muni, O personality of sinful action, you have obstructed their progress toward good fortune in this world and the next because they are still indebted to the saintly persons, the demigods and their father.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 As soon as a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  takes birth, he assumes three kinds of debts\emdash debts to great saints, debts to the demigods and debts to his father. The son of a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 must undergo celibacy (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 brahmacarya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
) to clear his debts to the saintly persons, he must perform ritualistic ceremonies to clear his debts to the demigods, and he must beget children to become free from his debts to his father. Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a argued th
at although the renounced order is recommended for liberation, one cannot attain liberation unless one fulfills his obligations to the demigods, the saints and his father. Since Dak\'f1
a's sons had not liberated themselves from these three debts, how could N\'e4rada Muni have led them to the renounced order of life? Apparently, Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a did not know the final decision of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4
stras.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (11.5.41):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 devar\'f1i-bh\'fct\'e4pta-n\'e5\'eb\'e4\'e0 pit\'e8\'eb\'e4\'e0\line na ki\'eckaro n
