\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
Everyone is indebted to the demigods, to living entities in general, to his family, to the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pit\'e4s}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  and so on, but if one fully surrenders to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, Mukunda, who can give one liberation, even if one performs no }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yaj\'efas,}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571 
 one is freed from all debts. Even if one does not repay his debts, he is freed from all debts if he renounces the material world for the sake of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, whose lotus feet are the shelter of everyone. This is the verdict of the 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra.}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  Therefore N\'e4rada Muni was completely right in instructing the sons of Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1
a to renounce this material world immediately and take shelter of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Unfortunately, Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a, the father of the Harya\'e7vas and Saval\'e4\'e7vas, did not understand the great service rendered by N\'e4
rada Muni. Dak\'f1a therefore addressed him as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 p\'e4pa}{\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (the personality of sinful activities) and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 as\'e4dhu}{
\cs3025\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid9723571  (a nonsaintly person). Since N\'e4rada Muni was a great saint and Vai\'f1\'ebava, he tolerated all such accusations from Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a. He merely performed his duty as a Vai\'f1\'eb
ava by delivering all the sons of Praj\'e4pati Dak\'f1a, enabling them to return home, back to Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.5.38
