\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sam\'e4dhin\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 is very important. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Sam\'e4dhi}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  means complete absorption with an undiverted mind. Vi\'e7var\'fcpa, who was a most learned }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  not only accepted the request of the demigods, but
 took their request seriously and performed the activities of priesthood with an undiverted mind. In other words, he accepted the priesthood not for material gain, but to profit the demigods. Such is the duty of a priest. The word }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pura\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  means "family," and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 hita}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  means "benefit." Thus the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 purohita}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  indicates that the priest is the well-wisher of the family. Another meaning of the word }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pura\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 is "first." A priest's first duty is to see that his disciples benefit spiritually and materially by all means. Then he is satisfied. A priest should never be interested in performing Vedic rituals for his personal benefit.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.7.39
