 on his hands. The eight-syllable }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\insrsid10252087  is }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 o\'e0 namo n\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb\'e4ya.}{\insrsid10252087  This }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\insrsid10252087 
 should be distributed all over the front and back of the body. The twelve-syllable }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra,}{\insrsid10252087  which begins with the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pra\'ebava, o\'e0k\'e4ra,}{\insrsid10252087  is }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 o\'e0 namo bhagavate v\'e4sudev\'e4ya.}{\insrsid10252087  One syllable should be placed on each of the fingers and should be preceded by the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 pra\'ebava, o\'e0k\'e4ra.}{\insrsid10252087 
 Thereafter, one must chant }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 o\'e0 vi\'f1\'ebave nama\'f9,}{\insrsid10252087  which is a six-syllable }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra.}{\insrsid10252087  One must progressively place the syllables of the }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\insrsid10252087  on the heart, the head, between the two eyebrows, on the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e7ikh\'e4}{\insrsid10252087  and between the eyes, and then one should chant }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 ma\'f9 astr
\'e4ya pha\'f6}{\insrsid10252087  and with this }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\insrsid10252087  protect himself from all directions. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 N\'e4devo devam arcayet:}{\insrsid10252087  one who has not risen to the level of a }{
