\par After finishing this dedication, one must offer a prayer to the eight-armed Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, who sits on the shoulders of Garu\'f2adeva. One also has to think of the fish incarnation, V\'e4mana, K\'fcrma, N\'e5si\'e0ha, Var\'e4ha, Para\'e7ur\'e4ma, R\'e4
macandra (the elder brother of Lak\'f1ma\'eba). Nara-N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, Datt\'e4treya (an empowered incarnation), Kapila, Sanat-kum\'e4ra, Hayagr\'e9va, N\'e4radadeva (the incarnation of a devotee). Dhanvantari, \'c5\'f1abhadeva, Yaj\'efa, Balar\'e4ma, Vy
\'e4sadeva, Buddhadeva and Ke\'e7ava. One should also think of Govinda, the master of V\'e5nd\'e4vana, and one should think of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, the master of the spiritual sky. One should think of Madhus\'fcdana, Tridh\'e4m\'e4, M\'e4dhava, H\'e5\'f1
\'e9ke\'e7a, Padman\'e4bha, Jan\'e4rdana, D\'e4modara and Vi\'e7ve\'e7vara, as well as the Supreme Personality of Godhead K\'e5\'f1\'eba Himself. After offering prayers to the Lord's personal expansions known as the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 sv\'e4\'e0
