var\'fcpa's father performed a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yaj\'efa}{\insrsid10252087  to kill Indra. When V\'e5tr\'e4sura appeared from that }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yaj\'efa,}{\insrsid10252087 
 the demigods, in fear, sought shelter of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and glorified Him.
\par Because of affection for the demons, Vi\'e7var\'fcpa secretly supplied them the remnants of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yaj\'efa.}{\insrsid10252087  When Indra learned about this, he beheaded Vi\'e7var\'fcpa, but he later regretted killing Vi\'e7var\'fc
pa because Vi\'e7var\'fcpa was a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\insrsid10252087  Although competent to neutralize the sinful reactions for killing a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{\insrsid10252087  Indra did not do so. 
Instead he accepted the reactions. Later, he distributed these reactions among the land, water, trees and women in general. Since the land accepted one fourth of the sinful reactions, a portion of the land turned into desert. The trees were also given one
 
fourth of the sinful reactions, and therefore they drip sap, which is prohibited for drinking. Because women accepted one fourth of the sinful reactions, they are untouchable during their menstrual period. Since water was also infested with sinful reactio
ns, when bubbles appear in water it cannot be used for any purpose.
\par After Vi\'e7var\'fcpa was killed, his father, Tva\'f1\'f6\'e4, performed a sacrifice to kill King Indra. Unfortunately, if }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantras}{\insrsid10252087  are chanted irregularly, they yield an opposite result. This happened whe
n Tva\'f1\'f6\'e4 performed this }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 yaj\'efa.}{\insrsid10252087  While performing the sacrifice to kill Indra. Tva\'f1\'f6\'e4 chanted a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\insrsid10252087 
 to increase Indra's enemies, but because he chanted the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\insrsid10252087  wrong, the sacrifice produced an }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 asura}{\insrsid10252087  named V\'e5tr\'e4sura, of whom Indra was the enemy. When V
\'e5tr\'e4
sura was generated from the sacrifice, his fierce features made the whole world afraid, and his personal effulgence diminished even the power of the demigods. Finding no other means of protection, the demigods began to worship the Supreme Personality of
 Godhead, the enjoyer of all the results of sacrifice, who is supreme throughout the entire universe. The demigods all worshiped Him because ultimately no one but Him can protect a living entity from fear and danger. Seeking shelter of a demigod instead o
f worshiping the Supreme Personality of Godhead is compared to trying to cross the ocean by grasping the tail of a dog. A dog can swim, but that does not mean that one can cross the ocean by grasping a dog's tail.
\par Being pleased with the demigods, the Supreme Personality of Godhead advised them to approach Dadh\'e9ci to beg him for the bones of his own body. Dadh\'e9ci would comply with the request of the demigods, and with the help of his bones V\'e5tr\'e4
sura could be killed.
