 and when He expands Himself in different forms for material creation He is called K\'f1\'e9rodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu, Garbhodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu and K\'e4ra\'ebodaka\'e7\'e4y\'e9 Vi\'f1\'ebu. When He is realized as V\'e4sudeva, Sa\'eckar
\'f1a\'eba, Pradyumna and Aniruddha\emdash the Caturvy\'fcha, who are beyond the three forms of Vi\'f1\'ebu\emdash He is the Vaiku\'eb\'f6ha N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Above realization of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba is realization of Baladeva, and ab
ove that is realization of K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. All these realizations are possible when one engages fully in devotional service. The covered core of one's heart is then completely open to receiving an understanding of the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His various forms.
