 (5.37) says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 goloka eva nivasaty akhil\'e4tma-bh\'fcta\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  the Supreme Personality of Godhead, K\'e5\'f1\'eba, is always situated in Goloka V\'e5nd\'e4vana. It is also said, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 v\'e5nd\'e4vana\'e0 parityajya padam eka\'e0 na gacchati:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  K\'e5\'f1\'eba never goes even a step from V\'e5nd\'e4vana. Nevertheless, although K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is situated in His own abode, Goloka V\'e5nd\'e4vana, He is simultaneously all-pervading and is therefore present everywhere. This is very difficult for a conditioned soul to understand, but devotees can understand how K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, without undergoing any changes, can simultaneously be in His abode and be all-pervasive. The demigods
 are understood to be various limbs of the Supreme Lord's body, although the Supreme Lord has no material body and does not need anyone's help. He is spread everywhere (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 may\'e4 tatam ida\'e0 sarva\'e0 jagad avyakta-m
\'fcrtin\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). Nevertheless, He is not present everywhere in His spiritual form. According to the M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4da philosophy, the Supreme Truth, being all-pervasive, does not need a transcendental form. The M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d
\'e9s suppose that since His form is distributed everywhere, He has no form. This is untrue. The Lord keeps His transcendental form, and at the same time He extends everywhere, in every nook and corner of the material creation.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.9.35
