to relieve the devotees and kill demons or
 nondevotees. These two kinds of action are the same for the Absolute Truth. When the Lord comes to punish the demons, He bestows His favor upon them, and similarly when He delivers His devotees and gives them relief, He also bestows His favor. Thus the L
o
rd bestows His favor equally upon the conditioned souls. When a conditioned soul gives relief to others he acts piously, and when he gives trouble to others he acts impiously, but the Lord is neither pious nor impious; He is always full in His spiritual p
otency, by which He shows equal mercy to the punishable and the protectable. The Lord is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ap\'e4pa-viddham;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  He is never contaminated by the reactions of so-called sinful activities. When K
\'e5\'f1\'eba was present on this earth, He killed many inimical nondevotees, but they all received }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 s\'e4r\'fcpya;}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 in other words, they returned to their original spiritual bodies. One who does not know the Lord's position says that God is unkind to him but merciful to others. Actually the Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (9.29), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 samo 'ha\'e0 sarva-bh\'fcte\'f1u na me dve\'f1yo 'sti na priya\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 "I am equal to everyone. No one is My enemy, and no one is My friend." But He also says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ye bhajanti tu m\'e4\'e0 bhakty\'e4 mayi te te\'f1u c\'e4py aham:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 "If one becomes My devotee and fully surrenders unto Me, I give him special attention."
