u%<@" SaPaaRidiDaYaaMa( )) 37 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s904\qc \li251\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin251\itap0\pararsid751198 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sama-vi\'f1ama-mat\'e9n\'e4\'e0 matam anusarasi yath\'e4 rajju-kha\'eb\'f2a\'f9
 sarp\'e4di-dhiy\'e4m.
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid3943952 SYNONYMS}{\v\fs28\insrsid10252087 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb240\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 sama}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash equal or proper; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 vi\'f1ama}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash and unequal or mistaken; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 mat\'e9n\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash of those having intelligence; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 matam}{
\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash conclusion; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 anusarasi}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash You follow; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 yath\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash just as; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 rajju-kha
\'eb\'f2a\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash a piece of rope; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 sarpa-\'e4di}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash a snake, etc.; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 dhiy\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash of those who perceive.

\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 
A rope causes fear for a bewildered person who considers it a snake, but not for a person with proper intelligence who knows it to be only a rope
. Similarly, You, as the Supersoul in everyone's heart, inspire fear or fearlessness according to one's intelligence, but in You there is no duality.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 (4.11) the Lord says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ye yath\'e4 m\'e4\'e0 prapadyante t\'e4\'e0s tathaiva bhaj\'e4my aham:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  "As on
e surrenders unto Me, I reward him accordingly." The Supreme Personality of Godhead is the reservoir of everything, including all knowledge, all truth and all contradictions. The example cited herein is very appropriate. A rope is one truth, but some mist
ake it for a snake, whereas others know it to be a rope. Similarly, devotees who know the Supreme Personality of Godhead do not see contradictions in Him, but nondevotees regard Him as the snakelike source of all fear. For example, when }{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid8670799 N\'e5si\'e0hadeva}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  appeared, Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja saw the Lord as the supreme solace, whereas his father, a demon, saw Him as the ultimate death. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
\'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (11.2.37), }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bhaya\'e0 dvit\'e9y\'e4bhinive\'e7ata\'f9 sy\'e4t:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  fear results from being absorbed in duality. When one is in knowl
edge of duality, one knows both fear and bliss. The same Supreme Lord is a source of bliss to devotees and fear to nondevotees who have a poor fund of knowledge. God is one, but people understand the Absolute Truth from different angles of vision. The uni
ntelligent see contradictions in Him, but sober devotees find no contradictions.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.9.38
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 TEXT 38
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 TEXT
