\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 
O Lord, as the small sparks of a fire cannot possibly perform the actions of the whole fire, we sparks of Your Lordship cannot infor
m You of the necessities of our lives. You are the complete whole. Therefore, of what do we need to inform You? You know everything because You are the original cause of the cosmic manifestation, the maintainer and the annihilator of the entire universal 
c
reation. You always engage in Your pastimes with Your spiritual and material energies, for You are the controller of all these varied energies. You exist within all living entities, within the cosmic manifestation, and also beyond them. You exist internal
ly as }{\fs28\insrsid10775694 Parabrahman}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 
 and externally as the ingredients of the material creation. Therefore, although manifested in various stages, at different times and places, and in various bodies, You, the Personality of Godhead, are the original cause of all causes. Inde
ed, You are the original element. You are the witness of all activities, but because You are as great as the sky, You are never touched by any of them. You are the witness of everything as }{\fs28\insrsid10775694 Parabrahman}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 
 and Param\'e4tm\'e4. O Supreme Personality of Godhead, nothing is unknown to You.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The Absolute Truth exists in three phases of spiritual understanding\emdash Brahman, Param
\'e4tm\'e4 and Bhagav\'e4n (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 brahmeti param\'e4tmeti bhagav\'e4n iti \'e7abdyate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). Bhagav\'e4n, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is the cause of Brahman and Param\'e4tm\'e4
. Brahman, the impersonal Absolute Truth, is all-pervading, and Param\'e4tm\'e4 is locally situated in everyone's heart, but Bhagav\'e4
n, who is worshipable by the devotees, is the original cause of all causes. A pure devotee is aware that since nothing is unkno
wn to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, He need not be informed of a devotee's conveniences and inconveniences. A pure devotee knows that there is no need to ask the Absolute Truth for any material necessities. Therefore, while informing the Supreme Lor
d about their distress in being attacked by V\'e5tr\'e4
sura, the demigods apologized for offering prayers for their safety. A neophyte devotee, of course, approaches the Supreme Lord for relief from distress or poverty, or for speculative knowledge of the Lord. }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g
\'e9t\'e4 }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (7.16) mentions four kinds of pious men who begin devotional service to the Lord\emdash one who is distressed (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e4rta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ), one in need of money (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 arth\'e4rth\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ), one who is inquisitive (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 jij\'ef\'e4su}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ) and one who is searching for the Absolute Truth (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). A pure 
devotee, however, knows that since the Lord is omnipresent and omniscient, there is no need to offer prayers or worship Him for one's personal benefit. A pure devotee always engages in the service of the Lord without demanding anything. The Lord is presen
t everywhere and knows the necessities of His devotees; consequently there is no need to disturb Him by asking Him for material benefits.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.9.43
