s that they sometimes give up their material desires and become pure. When the demigods are utterly helpless, they approach the Supreme Personality of Godhead in grief and with tears in their eyes, praying to the Lord, and thus they become almost pure dev
o
tees, free from material desires. Admitting that they have forgotten pure devotional service because of extensive material opportunities, they fully surrender to the Lord, leaving to His consideration whether to maintain them or annihilate them. Such surr
ender is necessary. Bhaktivinoda \'d6h\'e4kura sings, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4rabi r\'e4khabi-yo icch\'e4 toh\'e4r\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 "O Lord, I fully surrender unto Your lotus feet. Now, as You desire, You may protect me or annihilate me. You have the full right to do either."
