Those who think material assets to be everything or to be the ultimate goal of life are called misers [k\'e5pa\'ebas]. They do not know the ultimate necessity of the soul. Moreover, if one awards that which is desired by such
 fools, he must also be considered foolish.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 There are two classes of men\emdash namely the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5pa
\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  A }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 is one who knows Brahman, the Absolute Truth, and who thus knows his real interest. A }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5pa\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  however, is one who has a material
, bodily concept of life. Not knowing how to utilize his human or demigod life, a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5pa\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  is attracted by things created by the material modes of nature. The }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5pa\'ebas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  who always desire material benefits, are foolish, whereas }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'ebas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  who always desire spi
ritual benefits, are intelligent. If a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5pa\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  not knowing his self-interest, foolishly asks for something material, one who awards it to him is also foolish. K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, however, is not a foolish person; He is supremely intelligent. If someone comes to K\'e5\'f1\'eba asking for material benefits, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a does not award him the material things he desires. Instead, the Lord gives him intelligence so that he will forget his material desires and become attached to the Lord's lotus feet. In such cases, although the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5
pa\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  offers prayers to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba for material things, the Lord takes away whatever material possessions the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5pa\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 has and gives him the sense to become a devotee. As stated by the Lord in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Caitanya-carit\'e4m\'e5ta}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (}{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Madhya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  22.39):

\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e4mi-vij\'efa, ei m\'fcrkhe 'vi\'f1aya' kene diba?\line sva-cara\'eb\'e4m\'e5ta diy
\'e4 'vi\'f1aya' bhul\'e4iba
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"Since I am very intelligent, why should I give this fool material prosperity? Instead I shall induce him to take the nectar of the shelter of My lotus feet and make him forget illusory material enjoyment." If on
e sincerely prays to God for material possessions in exchange for devotional service, the Lord, who is not foolish like such an unintelligent devotee, shows him special favor by taking away whatever material possessions he has and gradually giving him the
 intelligence to be satisfied only by rendering service to His lotus feet. \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4
kura comments in this regard that if a foolish child requests his mother to give him poison, the mother, being intelligent, will certainly not give him
 poison, even though he requests it. A materialist does not know that to accept material possessions means to accept poison, or the repetition of birth and death. An intelligent person, a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  aspires for liberation from material bondage. That is the real self-interest of a human being.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.9.50
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 TEXT 50
