\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb240\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 svayam}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash personally; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ni\'f9\'e7reyasam}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash the supreme goal of life, namely the means of obtaining ecstatic love for the Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 vit-v\'e4n}{
\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash one who is accomplished in devotional service; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 na}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 vakti}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash teaches; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 aj\'ef\'e4ya}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash unto a foolish person not conversant with the ultimate goal of life; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 karma}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash fruitive activities; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 hi}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash indeed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 na}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash not; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 r\'e4ti}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash administers; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 rogi\'eba\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash unto the patient; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 apathyam}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash something unconsumable; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 v\'e4\'efchata\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash desiring; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 api}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash although; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 bhi\'f1ak-tama\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash an experienced physician.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 
A pure devotee who is fully accomplished in the science of devotional service will never instruct a foolish person to engage in fruitive activities for material enjoyment, not to speak of helping him in such activities. Such a devotee is like 
an experienced physician, who never encourages a patient to eat food injurious to his health, even if the patient desires it.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
Here is the difference between the benedictions awarded by the demigods and those awarded by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Vi\'f1\'eb
u. Devotees of the demigods ask for benedictions simply for sense gratification, and therefore they have been described in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (7.20) as bereft of intelligence.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e4mais tais tair h\'e5ta-j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'f9\line prapadyante 'nya-devat\'e4\'f9
\line ta\'e0 ta\'e0 niyamam \'e4sth\'e4ya\line prak\'e5ty\'e4 niyat\'e4\'f9 svay\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"Those whose minds are distorted by material desires surrender unto demigods and follow the particular rules and regulations of worship according to their own natures."
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 Conditioned souls are generally bereft of intelligence becau
se of profound desires for sense gratification. They do not know what benedictions to ask. Therefore nondevotees are advised in the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stras}{\cs3006\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3824524 
 to worship various demigods to achieve material benefits. For example, if one wants a beautiful wife, he is advised to worship Um\'e4, or goddess Durg\'e4
. If one wants to be cured of a disease, he is advised to worship the sun-god. All requests for benedictions from the demigods, however, are due to material lust. The benedictions will be finished at the end of the cosmic ma
nifestation, along with those who bestow them. If one approaches Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu for benedictions, the Lord will give him a benediction that will help him return home, back to Godhead. This is also confirmed by the Lord Himself in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (10.10):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 te\'f1\'e4\'e0 satata-yukt\'e4n\'e4\'e0\line bhajat\'e4\'e0 pr\'e9ti-p\'fcrvakam\line 
dad\'e4mi buddhi-yoga\'e0 ta\'e0\line yena m\'e4m upay\'e4nti te
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, or Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a, instructs a devotee who constantly engages in His service how to approach Him at the end of his material body. The Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (4.9):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 janma karma ca me divyam\line eva\'e0 yo vetti tattvata\'f9\line tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0
 punar janma\line naiti m\'e4m eti so 'rjuna
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"One who knows the transcendental nature of My appearance and activities, does not, upon leaving the body, take his birth again in this material world, but attains My eternal abode, O Arjuna." This is the benediction of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu, K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a. After giving up his body, a devotee returns home, back to Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 A devotee may foolishly ask for material benedictions, but Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a does not give him such benedictions, despite the devotee's prayers. Therefore people who are very attached to material life do not generally become devotees of K\'e5\'f1\'eba or Vi\'f1\'ebu. Instead they become devotees of the demigods (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e4mais tais tair h\'e5ta j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'f9 prapadyante 'nya-devat\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). The benedictions of the demigods, however, are condemned in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Antavat tu phala\'e0 te\'f1\'e4\'e0 tad bhavaty alpa-medhas\'e4m: }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"Men of small intelligence worship the demigods, and their fruits are limited and temporary." A non-Vai\'f1\'ebava, one who is not engaged in the service of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, is considered a fool with a small quantity of brain substance.

