ce of the demigods. He placed himself, the spirit soul, at the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead and in this way gave up his gross material body made of five elements.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 As indicated by the words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pare bhagavati brahma\'eby 
\'e4tm\'e4na\'e0 sannayan,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Dadh\'e9ci placed himself, as spirit soul, at the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. In this regard, one may refer to the incident of Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6
ra's leaving his body, as described in the First Canto of }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (1.13.55). Dh\'e5tar\'e4\'f1\'f6ra
 analytically divided his gross material body into the five different elements of which it was made\emdash earth, water, fire, air and ether\emdash 
and distributed them to the different reservoirs of these elements; in other words, he merged these five elements into the original }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mahat-tattva.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 By identifying his material conception of life, he gradually separated his spirit soul from material connections and placed himself at the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. The example given in this connection is tha
t when an earthen pot is broken, the small portion of the sky within the pot is united with the large sky outside the pot. M\'e4y\'e4v\'e4d\'e9 philosophers misunderstand this description of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.
}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Therefore \'c7r\'e9 R\'e4m\'e4nuja Sv\'e4m\'e9, in his book }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Ved\'e4nta-tattva-s\'e4ra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 has described that this merging of the soul means that after separating himself from the material body made of eight elements\emdash earth, water, fire, air, ether, false ego, mind and intelligence\emdash 
the individual soul engages himself in devotional service to the Supreme Personality of Godhead in His eternal form (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e9\'e7vara\'f9 parama\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba\'f9 sac-cid-\'e4nanda-vigraha\'f9/ an\'e4dir \'e4di}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid77373 r govinda\'f9 sarva-k\'e4ra\'eba-k\'e4ra\'ebam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). The material cause of the material elements absorbs the material body, and the spiritual soul assumes its original position. As described by \'c7r
\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'e9vera 'svar\'fcpa' haya}{\fs28\insrsid12861454 \emdash }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5\'f1\'ebera 'nitya-d\'e4sa': }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
the constitutional position of the living entity is that he is the eternal servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba. When one overcomes the material body through cultivation of 
spiritual knowledge and devotional service, one can revive his own position and thus engage in the service of the Lord.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.10.12
