\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.11 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 This chapter describes V\'e5tr\'e4
sura's great qualities. When the prominent commanders of the demons fled, not hearing V\'e5tr\'e4sura's advice. V\'e5tr\'e4sura condemned them all as cowards. Speaking very bravely, he stood alone to face the demigods. When the demigods saw V\'e5tr\'e4
sura's attitude, they were so afraid that they practically fainted, and V\'e5tr\'e4sura began trampling them down. Unable to tolerate this, Indra, the King of the demigods, threw his club at V\'e5tr\'e4sura, but V\'e5tr\'e4
sura was such a great hero that he easily caught the club with his left hand and used it to beat Indra's elephant. Struck by the blow of V\'e5tr\'e4sura, the elephant was pushed back fourteen yards and fell, with Indra on its back.
