sura, disappointed that King Indra was reluctant despite his encouragement, took the initiative very forcefully by throwing his trident at Indra. V\'e5tr\'e4
sura was not at all interested in victory; he was interested in being killed so that he could immediately return home, back to Godhead. As confirmed in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (4.9), }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tyaktv\'e4 deha\'e0 punar janma naiti:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  after giving up his body, a devotee immediately returns to Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and never returns to accept another body. This was V\'e5tr\'e4
