kura explains that Indra, not V\'e5tr\'e4sura, was actually killed. He says that when V\'e5tr\'e4
sura swallowed King Indra and his carrier, the elephant, he thought, "Now I have killed Indra, and therefore there is no more need of fighting. Now let me return home, back to Godhead." Thus he stopped all his bodily activities and became situated
 in trance. Taking advantage of the silence of V\'e5tr\'e4sura's body, Indra pierced the demon's abdomen, and because of V\'e5tr\'e4sura's trance, Indra was able to come out. Now, V\'e5tr\'e4sura was in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yoga-samadhi,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  and therefore although King Indra wanted to cut his throat, the demon's neck was so stiff that Indra's thunderbolt took 360  days to cut it to pieces. Actually it was the body left by V\'e5tr\'e4
sura that was cut to pieces by Indra; V\'e5tr\'e4sura himself was not killed. In his original consciousness, V\'e5tr\'e4sura returned home, back to Godhead, to become an associate of Lord Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eba. Here the word }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 alokam}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  means the transcendental world, Vaiku\'eb\'f6haloka, where Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eba eternally resides.
\par }\pard\plain \s1178\ql \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Sixth Canto, Twelfth Chapter, of the}{
