\par }\pard\plain \s330\qc \li0\ri0\sb540\sa240\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0\pararsid10252087 \shading10000\cfpat10 
\b\f35\fs36\cf8\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid6360924 CHAPTER THIRTEEN\line }{\insrsid10252087 King Indra Afflicted by Sinful Reaction
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.13 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 This chapter describes Indra's fear at having killed a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba}{
\insrsid10252087  (V\'e5tr\'e4sura), and it also describes how he fled and was saved by the grace of Lord Vi\'f1\'ebu.
\par When all the demigods requested Indra to kill V\'e5tr\'e4sura, he refused because V\'e5tr\'e4sura was a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\insrsid10252087  The demigods, however, encouraged Indra not to fear killing him because Indra was pro
tected by the N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba-kavaca, or the Supreme Personality of Godhead Himself, Lord N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba. Even by a glimpse of the chanting of N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba's name, one becomes free from all the sinful reactions of killing a woman, a cow or a }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\insrsid10252087  The demigods advised Indra to perform an }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 a\'e7vamedha}{\insrsid10252087  sacrifice, by which N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eb
a would be pleased, for the performer of such a sacrifice is not implicated in sinful reactions even if he kills the entire universe.
\par Following this instruction from the demigods, King Indra fought V\'e5tr\'e4sura, but when V\'e5tr\'e4sura was killed, everyone was satisfied but King Indra, who knew V\'e5tr\'e4
sura's position. This is the nature of a great personality. Even if a great personality acquires some opulence, he is always ashamed and regretful if he acquires 
it illegally. Indra could understand that he was certainly entangled by sinful reactions for killing a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba.}{\insrsid10252087 
 Indeed, he could see sinful reaction personified following him, and thus he fled here and there in fear, thinking of how to rid himself of his sins. He went to M\'e4
nasa-sarovara, and there, under the protection of the goddess of fortune, he meditated for one thousand years. During this time, Nahu\'f1a reigned over the heavenly planets as the representative of Indra. Unfortunately, however, he was attr
acted by the beauty of Indra's wife, \'c7ac\'e9dev\'e9, and because of his sinful desire he had to accept the body of a serpent in his next life. Indra later performed a great sacrifice with the help of exalted }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'ebas}
