ja Citraketu was actually not destined to get a son. Therefore although he married hundreds and thousands of wives, all of them proved barren, and he could not beget even one child. When A\'ecgir\'e4 \'c5\'f1i came to see the Ki
ng, the King requested the great sage to enable him to have at least one son. Because of the blessing of A\'ecgir\'e4 \'c5\'f1i, a child was sent by the grace of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4y\'e4,}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  but the child was not to live for long. Therefore in the beginning A\'ecgir\'e4 \'c5\'f1i told the King that he would beget a child who would cause jubilation and lamentation.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3018\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4206485 
King Citraketu was not destined to get a child by providence, or the will of the Supreme. Just as sterile grain cannot produce more grain, a sterile person, by the will of the Supreme Lord, ca
nnot beget a child. Sometimes a child is born even to an impotent father and sterile mother, and sometimes a potent father and fertile mother are childless. Indeed, sometimes a child is born despite contraceptive methods, and therefore the parents kill th
e
 child in the womb. In the present age, killing children in the womb has become a common practice. Why? When contraceptive methods are taken, why don't they act? Why is a child sometimes produced so that the father and mother have to kill it in the womb? 
W
e must conclude that our arrangement of so-called scientific knowledge cannot determine what will take place; what is enacted actually depends on the supreme will. It is by the supreme will that we are situated in certain conditions in terms of family, co
mmunity and personality. These are all arrangements of the Supreme Lord according to our desires under the spell of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4y\'e4,}{\cs3018\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4206485 
 illusion. In devotional life, therefore, one should not desire anything, since everything depends on the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhakti-ras\'e4m\'e5ta-sindhu}{
\cs3018\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4206485  (1.1.11):
