\par }\pard\plain \s3013\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4279079 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 My dear King, now you are actually exp
eriencing the misery of a person who has sons and daughters. O King, owner of the state of \'c7\'fcrasena, one's wife, his house, the opulence of his kingdom, and his various other opulences and objects of sense perception are all the same}{
\cs3016\insrsid10252087\charrsid4279079  in that they are tempo
rary. One's kingdom, military power, treasury, servants, ministers, friends and relatives are all causes of fear, illusion, lamentation and distress. They are like a gandharva-nagara, a nonexistent palace that one imagines to exist in the for}{
\insrsid10252087 est. Because they are impermanent, they are no better than illusions, dreams and mental concoctions.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
This verse describes the entanglement of material existence. In material existence, the living entity possesses many things\emdash the material body, children, wife and so on (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 deh\'e4patya-kalatr\'e4di\'f1u}{
\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
). One may think that these will give him protection, but that is impossible. In spite of all these possessions, the spirit soul has to give up his present situation and accept another. The next situation may be unfavorable, bu
t even if it is favorable, one must give it up and again accept another body. In this way, one's tribulation in material existence continues. A sane man should be perfectly aware that these things will never be able to give him happiness. One must be situ
ated in his spiritual identity and eternally serve the Supreme Personality of Godhead as a devotee. A\'ecgir\'e4 \'c5\'f1i and N\'e4rada Muni gave this instruction to Mah\'e4r\'e4ja Citraketu.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.15.24
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 TEXT 24
