\par }\pard\plain \s3013\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4279079 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 These visible objects like wife, children and property are like
 dreams and mental concoctions. Actually what we see has no permanent existence. It is sometimes seen and sometimes not. Only because of our past actions do we create such mental concoctions, and because of these concoctions, we perform further activities
.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s3008\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3348640 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 
Everything material is a mental concoction because it is sometimes visible and sometimes not. At night when we dream of tigers and snakes, they are not actually present, but we are afraid because we are affected by what we envision in our dreams. 
Everything material is like a dream because it actually has no permanent existence.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3018\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4206485 \'c7r\'e9la Vi\'e7van\'e4tha Cakravart\'e9 \'d6h\'e4
kura writes as follows in his commentary: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 arthena vy\'e4ghra-sarp\'e4din\'e4 vinaiva d\'e5\'e7yam\'e4n\'e4\'f9 svapn\'e4di-bha\'ecge sati na d\'e5\'e7yante tad eva\'e0 d\'e4r\'e4dayo 'v\'e4stava-vastu-bh\'fct\'e4\'f9
 svapn\'e4dayo 'vastu-bh\'fct\'e4\'e7 ca sarve manobhav\'e4\'f9 mano-v\'e4san\'e4 janyatv\'e4n manobhav\'e4\'f9.}{\cs3018\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4206485 
 At night one dreams of tigers and snakes, and while dreaming he actually sees them, but as soon as the dream is broken they no longer exist. Similarly, the ma
terial world is a creation of our mental concoctions. We have come to this material world to enjoy material resources, and by mental concoction we discover many, many objects of enjoyment because our minds are absorbed in material things. This is why we r
eceive various bodies. According to our mental concoctions we work in various ways, desiring various achievements, and by nature and the order of the Supreme Personality of Godhead (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma\'eb\'e4-daiva-netre\'eba}{
\cs3018\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4206485 ) we get the advantages we desire. Thus we become more
 and more involved with material concoctions. This is the reason for our suffering in the material world. By one kind of activity we create another, and they are all products of our mental concoctions.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.15.25
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 TEXT 25
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 TEXT
