\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb240\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ayam}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash this; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 hi}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash certainly; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 dehina\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash of the living entity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 deha\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash body; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 dravya-j\'ef\'e4na-kriy\'e4-\'e4tmaka\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash consisting of the material elements, the senses for acquiring knowledge, and the acting senses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 dehina\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash of the living entity; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 vividha}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash various; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 kle\'e7a}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash sufferings; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 sant
\'e4pa}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash and of pains; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 k\'e5t}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash the cause; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ud\'e4h\'e5ta\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash is declared.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s3013\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4279079 \b\f35\fs28\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 The living entity in 
the bodily conception of life is absorbed in the body, which is a combination of the physical elements, the five senses for gathering knowledge, and the five senses of action, along with the mind. Through the mind the living entity suffers three kinds of 
tribulations\emdash adhibhautika, adhidaivika and adhy\'e4tmika. Therefore this body is a source of all miseries.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 In the Fifth Canto (5.5.4), while instructing his sons, \'c5\'f1
abhadeva said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 asann api kle\'e7ada \'e4sa deha\'f9:}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  the body, although temporary, is the cause 
of all the miseries of material existence. As already discussed in the previous verse, the entire material creation is based on mental concoction. The mind sometimes induces us to think that if we purchase an automobile we can enjoy the physical elements,
 such as earth, water, air and fire, combined in forms of iron, plastic, petrol and so on. Working with the five material elements (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pa\'efca-bh\'fctas}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
), as well as with our five knowledge-gathering senses like the eyes, ears and tongue and our five active senses like the hands and legs, we become involved in the material condition. Thus we are subjected to the tribulations known as }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 adhy\'e4tmika, adhidaivika}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 adhibhautika.}{\cs3010\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid3348640 
 The mind is the center because the mind creates all these things. As soon as the material ob
ject is struck, however, the mind is affected, and we suffer. For example, with the material elements, the working senses and the knowledge-gathering senses we create a very nice car, and when the car is accidentally smashed in a collision, the mind suffe
rs, and through the mind the living entity suffers.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs3018\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4206485 
The fact is that the living entity, while concocting with the mind, creates the material condition. Because matter is destructible, through the material condition the living entity suffers. Otherwise, the 
living entity is detached from all material conditions. When one comes to the Brahman platform, the platform of spiritual life, fully understanding that he is a spiritual soul (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 aha\'e0 brahm\'e4smi}{
\cs3018\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4206485 ), he is no longer affected by lamentation or hankering. As the Lord says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\cs3018\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4206485  (18.54):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 brahma-bh\'fcta\'f9 prasann\'e4tm\'e4\line na \'e7ocati na k\'e4\'eck\'f1ati
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"One who is thus transcendentally situated at once realizes the Supreme Brahman and becomes fully joyful. He never laments nor desires to have anything." Elsewhere in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 (15.7) the Lord says:
