\par }\pard\plain \s1178\ql \li0\ri0\sb360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Thus end the Bhaktivedanta purports of the Sixth Canto, Fifteenth Chapter, of the}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid9000157\charrsid9000157 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 , }{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 entitled "The Saints N\'e4rada and A\'ecgir\'e4 Instruct King Citraketu."
\par }\pard\plain \s20\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf18\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.16: King Citraketu Meets the Supreme Lord
\par }\pard\plain \s330\qc \li0\ri0\sb540\sa240\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \brdrb\brdrs\brdrw105\brsp140\brdrcf6 \faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0\pararsid10252087 \shading10000\cfpat10 
\b\f35\fs36\cf8\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid7478487 CHAPTER SIXTEEN\line }{\insrsid10252087 King Citraketu Meets the Supreme Lord
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.16 Summary
\par }\pard\plain \qj \fi360\li0\ri0\sb86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 As related in this cha
pter, Citraketu was able to talk with his dead son and hear from him the truth of life. When Citraketu was appeased, the great sage N\'e4rada gave him a }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra,}{\insrsid10252087  and by chanting this }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\insrsid10252087  Citraketu found shelter at the lotus feet of Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eba.
\par The living entity is eternal. Thus he has neither birth nor death (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 na hanyate hanyam\'e4ne \'e7ar\'e9re}{\insrsid10252087 
). According to the reactions of one's fruitive activities, one takes birth in various species of life among the birds, beasts, trees, human beings, demigods and so on, thus r
otating through various bodies. For a certain period of time, one receives a particular type of body as a son or father in a false relationship. All our relationships in this material world with friends, relatives or enemies consist of duality, in which o
ne feels happy and distressed on the basis of illusion. The living entity is actually a spiritual soul who is part and parcel of God and has nothing to do with relationships in the world of duality. Therefore N\'e4
rada Muni advised Citraketu not to lament for his so-called dead son.
\par After hearing instructions from their dead child, Citraketu and his wife could understand that all relationships in this material world are causes of misery. The queens who had administered poison to the son of K\'e5tadyuti were very m
uch ashamed. They atoned for the sinful act of killing a child and gave up their aspi}{\insrsid9844877 ration to have sons. Thereafter,}{\insrsid10252087  N\'e4rada Muni chanted prayers to N\'e4r\'e4ya\'eba, who exists as }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 
catur-vy\'fcha,}{\insrsid10252087  and instructed Citraketu about the Supreme Lord, who creates, maintain
s and annihilates everything and who is the master of the material nature. After instructing King Citraketu in this way, he returned to Brahmaloka. These instructions about the Absolute Truth are called the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mah\'e4-vidy\'e4.}{
\insrsid10252087  After being initiated by N\'e4rada Muni, King Citraketu chanted the }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mah\'e4-vidy\'e4,}{\insrsid10252087  and after one week he attained the presence of Lord Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eb
a, who was surrounded by the four Kum\'e4ras. The Lord was nicely dressed in bluish garments, with a helmet and ornaments of gold. His face appeared very happy. In the presence of Lord Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eb
a, Citraketu offered his obeisances and began to offer prayers.
\par In his prayers, Citraketu said that millions of universes rest in the pores of Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eba, who is limitless, having no beginning and end. The Lord is well k
nown to the devotees for His eternity. The difference between worshiping the Lord and worshiping the demigods is that the worshiper of the Lord also becomes eternal, whereas whatever benedictions one can get from the demigods are impermanent. Unless one b
ecomes a devotee, one cannot understand the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par After Citraketu finished his prayers, the unlimited Supreme Lord explained knowledge of Himself to Citraketu.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.16.1
