{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \emdash simultaneous oneness and difference\emdash is described. The living entity is eternal (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 nitya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
) like the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but the difference is that the Supreme Lord is the greatest, no one being equal to or greater than Him, whereas the living entity is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 s\'fck\'f1ma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 or extremely small. The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  describes that the magnitude of the living entity is one ten-thousandth the size of the tip of a hair. The Supreme Lord is all-pervading (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 a\'eb\'f2\'e4ntara-stha-param\'e4\'ebu-cay\'e4ntara-stham}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). Relatively, if the living entity is accepted as the smalles
t, there should naturally be inquiry about the greatest. The greatest is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and the smallest is the living entity.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Another peculiar characteristic of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'e9va}{
