\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash of devotional service; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4stra}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash of the holy scriptures; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 vigraham}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash the personified form.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 
Thereafter, by controlling his mind with his intelligence and thus restricting his senses from external engagements, he recovered suitable words with which to express his feelings. Thus he began offering prayers to the Lord, who is the
 personification of the holy scriptures [the s\'e4tvata-sa\'e0hit\'e4s like the Brahma-sa\'e0hit\'e4 and the N\'e4rada Pa\'efcar\'e4tra] and who is the spiritual master of all. He offered his prayers as follows.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 One cannot offer prayers to the Lord with mundane words. One
 must become spiritually advanced by controlling the mind and senses. Then he can find suitable words to offer in prayers to the Lord. Quoting the following verse from the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Padma Pur\'e4\'eba,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  \'c7r\'e9la San\'e4tana Gosv\'e4m\'e9 forbids us to sing any song not sung by authorized devotees.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 avai\'f1\'ebava-mukhodg\'e9r\'eba\'e0\line p\'fcta\'e0 hari-kath\'e4m\'e5tam\line \'e7
rava\'eba\'e0 naiva kartavya\'e0\line sarpocchi\'f1\'f6a\'e0 yath\'e4 paya\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The words or songs of a person not fixed in Vai\'f1\'eb
ava behavior, not strictly following the rules and regulations and chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mantra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  should not be accepted by pure devotees. The words }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 s\'e4tvata-\'e7\'e4stra-vigraham}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  indicate that the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sac-cid-\'e4nanda}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  body of the Lord can never be accepted to be made of }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4y\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Devotees do not offer prayers to the Lord in an imaginary form. The existence of the Lord's form is supported by all Vedic literature.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.16.34
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 TEXT 34
