\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid3943952 SYNONYMS}{\v\fs28\insrsid10252087 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb240\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 citraketu\'f9 uv\'e4ca}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
King Citraketu said; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ajita}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash O my unconquerable Lord; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 jita\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash conquered; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 sama-matibhi\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash by persons who have conquered the mind; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 s\'e4dhubhi\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash the devotees; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 bhav\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash Your Lordship; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 jita-\'e4tmabhi\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash who have completely controlled the senses; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 bhavat\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash by You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 vijit\'e4\'f9}
{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash conquered; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 te}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash they; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 api}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash also; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ca}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 
\emdash and; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 bhajat\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash to those who always engage in Your service; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ak\'e4ma-\'e4tman\'e4m}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash with no motives
 for material profit; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ya\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash who; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 \'e4tma-da\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash giving Yourself; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ati-karu\'eba\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash extremely merciful.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf9\insrsid10252087 Citraketu said:}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 
 O unconquerable Lord, although You cannot be conquered by anyone, You are certainly conquered by devotees who have control of the mind and 
senses. They can keep You under their control because You are causelessly merciful to devotees who desire no material profit from You. Indeed, You give Yourself to them, and because of this You also have full control over Your devotees.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The Lord an
d the devotees both conquer. The Lord is conquered by the devotees, and the devotees are conquered by the Lord. Because of being conquered by one another, they both derive transcendental bliss from their relationship. The highest perfection of this mutual
 conquering is exhibited by K\'e5\'f1\'eba and the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 gop\'e9s.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 gop\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  conquered K\'e5\'f1\'eba, and K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conquered the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 gop\'e9s.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Thus whenever K\'e5\'f1\'eba played His flute, He conquered the minds of the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 gop\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 and without seeing the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 gop\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  K\'e5\'f1\'eba could not be happy. Other transcendentalists, such as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yog\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  cannot conquer the Supreme Personality of Godhead; only pure devotees can conquer Him.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Pure devotees are described as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sama-mati,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  which means that they never deviate from devotional service under any circumstances. It is not 
that devotees worship the Supreme Lord only when happy; they worship Him even when in distress. Happiness and distress do not hamper the process of devotional service. Therefore }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  says that devotional service is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ahaituky apratihat\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  unmotivated and uninterrupted. When a devotee offers devotional service to the Lord without any motive (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid2041953 any\'e4bhil\'e4\'f1it\'e4-\'e7\'fcnyam}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid2041953\charrsid2041953 )}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 , his service cannot be hampered by any material condition (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
apratihat\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). Thus a devotee who offers service in all conditions of life can conquer the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par A special distinction between devotees and the other transcendentalists, namely the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yog\'e9s,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  is that }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 j\'ef\'e4n\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yog\'e9s}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  artificially try to become one with the Supreme, whereas devotees never aspire for suc
h an impossible accomplishment. Devotees know that their position is to be eternally servants of the Supreme Lord and never to be one with Him. Therefore they are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sama-mati}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  or }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 jit\'e4tm\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  They detest oneness with the Supreme. They have no lusty desires for oneness; instead, their desire is to be freed from all material hankering. Therefore they are called }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ni\'f1k\'e4ma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  desireless. A living entity cannot exist without desires, but desires that can never be fulfilled are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e4ma,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  lusty desires. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 K\'e4mais tais tair h\'e5ta j\'ef\'e4n\'e4\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 because of lusty desires, nondevotees are deprived of their intelligence. Thus they are unable to conquer the Supreme Lord, whereas devotees, being freed from such unreasonable desires, can conquer the Lord. Such devotees are also conque
red by the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Because they are pure, being free from all material desires, they fully surrender to the Supreme Lord, and therefore the Lord conquers them. Such devotees never aspire for liberation. They simply desire to serve 
t
he lotus feet of the Lord. Because they serve the Lord without desires for remuneration, they can conquer the mercy of the Lord. The Lord is by nature very merciful, and when He sees that His servant is working without desires for material profit, natural
ly He is conquered.
\par Devotees are always engaged in service.
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sa vai mana\'f9 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-pad\'e4ravindayor\line vac\'e4\'e0si vaiku\'eb\'f6ha-gu
\'eb\'e4nuvar\'ebane}{\cs1998\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
All the activities of their senses are engaged in the service of the Lord. Because of such devotion, the Lord gives Himself to His
 devotees as if they could use Him for any purpose they might desire. Of course, devotees have no purpose other than to serve. When a devotee fully surrenders and has no aspiration for material profit, the Lord certainly gives him all opportunities for se
rvice. This is the position of the Lord when conquered by His devotees.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.16.35
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 TEXT 35
\par }\pard\plain \s1168\qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 TEXT
\par }\pard\plain \s489\qc \li0\ri0\sa360\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f70\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 Tav iv>av" %lu/ >aGavNa(\line  JaGadudYaiSQaiTal/YaadqiNa )\line iv\'ecSa*JaSTae_&Xaa&Xaa
\'82\line  STa\}a Ma*za SPaDaRiNTa Pa*QaGai>aMaTYaa )) 35 ))
\par }\pard\plain \s23\qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 tava vibhava\'f9 khalu bhagavan
\par jagad-udaya-sthiti-lay\'e4d\'e9ni
\par vi\'e7va-s\'e5jas te '\'e0\'e7\'e4\'e0\'e7\'e4s
\par tatra m\'e5\'f1\'e4 spardhanti p\'e5thag abhimaty\'e4
\par }\pard\plain \s1146\qc \li0\ri0\sb360\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v\fs28\insrsid3943952 SYNONYMS}{\v\fs28\insrsid10252087 
\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb240\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 tava}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash Your; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 vibhava\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash opulences; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 khalu}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash indeed; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 bhagavan}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
O Supreme Personality of Godhead; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 jagat}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash of the cosmic manifestation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 udaya}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash the creation; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 
sthiti}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash maintenance; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 laya-\'e4d\'e9ni}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash dissolution and so on; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 vi\'e7va-s\'e5ja\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
the creators of the manifested world; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 te}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash they; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 a\'e0\'e7a-a\'e0\'e7\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash parts of Your plenary portion; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 tatra}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash in that; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 m\'e5\'f1\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash in vain; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 spardhanti}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
rival one another; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 p\'e5thak}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash of separateness; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 abhimaty\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash by a false conception.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087\charrsid16149108 
My dear Lord, this cosmic manifestation and its creation, maintenance and annihilation are}{\fs28\insrsid10252087  all but Your opulences. Since Lord Brahm\'e4
 and the other creators are nothing but small portions of a portion of You, their partial power to create does not make them God [\'e9\'e7vara]. Their consciousness of themselves as separate Lords is therefore merely false prestige. It is not valid.

\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
A devotee who has fully surrendered to the lotus feet of the Lord knows very well that the creative energy of the living entities, from Lord Brahm\'e4 down to the small ant, exists because the living entities are part and parcel of the Lord. In }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (15.7) the Lord says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mamaiv\'e4\'e0\'e7o j\'e9va-loke j\'e9va-bh\'fcta\'f9 san\'e4tana\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 "The living entities in this conditioned world are M
y eternal, fragmental parts." The living entities are nothing but very small portions of the supreme spirit, like sparks of a fire. Because they are part of the Supreme, they have a creative quality in a very minute quantity.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The so-called scientists of th
e modern materialistic world are proud because they have created modern facilities like great airplanes, but the credit for creating the airplanes should go to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, not to the scientists who have invented or created the so-c
alled wonderful products. The first consideration is the intelligence of the scientist; one must be elevated by the dictation of the Supreme Lord, who says in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (15.15), }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 matta\'f9 sm\'e5tir j\'ef\'e4nam apohana\'e0 ca:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  "From Me come remembrance, knowledge and 
forgetfulness." Because the Supreme Lord, as Supersoul, sits within the core of every living entity's heart, the dictation by which one advances in scientific knowledge or creative faculties comes from Him. Furthermore, the ingredients to manufacture wond
e
rful machines like airplanes are also supplied by the Lord, not by the scientists. Before the airplane was created, its ingredients already existed, having been caused by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but when the manifested creation of the airplane
 
is ruined, the remaining debris is a problem for the so-called creators. Another example is that the West is creating many automobiles. The ingredients for these cars are supplied, of course, by the Supreme Lord, and the intelligence for the so-called cre
a
tion is also supplied by the Lord. Ultimately, when the cars are demolished, the so-called creators are faced with the problem of what to do with their ingredients. The actual creator, the original creator, is the Personality of Godhead. Only in the inter
i
m does someone create something with intelligence supplied by the Lord, and later the creation again becomes a problem. Therefore the so-called creator is not to be credited with the act of creation; the only credit goes to the Supreme Personality of Godh
ead. It is rightly stated herein that the credit for all the opulences of creation, maintenance and annihilation belongs to the Supreme Lord, not to the living entities.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.16.36
