\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 Being full of contradictions, all forms of religion but bh\'e4
gavata-dharma work under conceptions of fruitive results and distinctions of "you and I" and "yours and mine." The followers of \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam have no such consciousness. They are all K\'e5\'f1\'eba conscious, thinking that they are K\'e5\'f1
\'eba's and K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a is theirs. There are other, low-class religious systems, which are contemplated for the killing of enemies or the gain of mystic power, but such religious systems, being full of passion and envy, are impure and temporary. Because they are full of envy, 
they are full of irreligion.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 has no contradictions. Conceptions of "your religion" and "my religion" are completely absent from }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  means following the orders given by the Supreme Lord, Bhagav\'e4n, as stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sarva-dharm\'e4
n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  God is one, and God is for everyone. Therefore everyone must surrender to God. That is the pure conception of religion. Whatever God orders constitutes religion (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma\'e0 tu s\'e4k\'f1\'e4d bhagavat-pra\'eb\'e9tam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). In }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 there is no question of "what you believe" and "what I believe." Everyone must believe in the Supreme Lord and carry out His orders. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c4nuk\'fclyena k\'e5\'f1\'eb\'e4nu\'e7\'e9lanam:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 whatever K\'e5\'f1\'eba says\emdash whatever God says\emdash should be directly carried out. That is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  religion.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 If one is actually K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a conscious, he cannot have any enemies. Since his only engagement is to induce others to surrender to K\'e5\'f1\'eba, or God, how can he have enemies? If one advocates the Hindu religion, the Muslim relig
ion, the Christian religion, this religion or that religion, there will be conflicts. History shows that the followers of religious systems without a clear conception of God have fought with one another. There are many instances of this in human history, 
b
ut systems of religion that do not concentrate upon service to the Supreme are temporary and cannot last for long because they are full of envy. There are many activities directed against such religious systems, and therefore one must give up the idea of 
"my belief" and "your belief." Everyone should believe in God and surrender unto Him. That is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma.
\par }\pard\plain \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs28\cf1\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4
gavata-dharma is not a concocted sectarian belief, for it entails research to find how everything is connected with K\'e5\'f1\'eba (}{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 \'e9\'e7\'e4v\'e4syam ida\'e0 sarvam}{\insrsid10252087 ). According to the Vedic injunctions, }
{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 sarva\'e0 khalv ida\'e0 brahma:}{\insrsid10252087  Brahman, the Supreme, is present in everything. }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\insrsid10252087  captures this presence of the Supreme. }{
\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\insrsid10252087  does not consider everything in the world to be false. Because every
thing emanates from the Supreme, nothing can be false; everything has some use in the service of the Supreme. For example, we are now dictating into a microphone and recording on a dictating machine, and thus we are finding how the machine can be connecte
d to the Supreme Brahman. Since we are using this machine in the service of the Lord, it is Brahman. This is the meaning of }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 sarva\'e0 khalv ida\'e0 brahma.}{\insrsid10252087 
 Everything is Brahman because everything can be used for the service of the Supreme Lord. Nothing is }{\cs1998\i\insrsid10252087 mithy\'e4,}{\insrsid10252087  false; everything is factual.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  is called }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sarvotk\'e5\'f1\'f6a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  the best of all religious systems, because those who follow }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 are not envious of anyone. Pure }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavatas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  pure devotees, invite everyone, without envy, to join the K\'e5\'f1\'eba
 consciousness movement. A devotee is therefore exactly like the Supreme Personality of Godhead. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Suh\'e5da\'e0 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4n\'e4m:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
he is the friend of all living entities. Therefore this is the best of all religious systems. Whereas so-called religions are meant for a particular type of person who believes in a particular way, such discrimination has no place in K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  If we scrutinize the religious systems meant for worship of demigods or anyone else but the Supreme Personality of 
Godhead, we will find that they are full of envy and therefore impure.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.16.42
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 TEXT 42
