\par }\pard\plain \s1140\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb240\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\cf9\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ka\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash what; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 k\'f1ema\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash benefit; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 nija}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash to oneself; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 parayo\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash and to others; 
}{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 kiy\'e4n}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash how much; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 v\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash or; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 artha\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash purpose; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 sva-para-druh\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash which is envious of the performer and of others; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 dharme\'eba}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash with the religious system; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 sva-droh\'e4t}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash from being envious of one's own self; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 tava}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash of You; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 kopa\'f9}{
\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash anger; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 para-samp\'e9\'f2ay\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash by giving pain to others; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 ca}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash also; }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 tath\'e4}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash as well as; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 adharma\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash irreligion.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 How can a religious system that produces envy
 of one's self and of others be beneficial for oneself and for them? What is auspicious about following such a system? What is actually to be gained? By causing pain to one's own self due to self-envy and by causing pain to others, one arouses Your anger 
and practices irreligion.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Any religious system but the process of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4
gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid6882524 \emdash }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 service as an eternal servant of the Supreme Personality of Godhead\emdash is a system of envy of one's own self and of others. For example, there are many systems of religi
on in which animal sacrifices are recommended. Such animal sacrifices are inauspicious both for the performer and for the animal. Although one is sometimes permitted to sacrifice an animal before the goddess K\'e4l\'e9
 and eat it instead of purchasing meat from a slaughterhouse, permission to eat meat after a sacrifice in the presence of the goddess K\'e4l\'e9
 is not the order of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. It is simply a concession for the miserable person who will not give up eating meat. It is meant to restr
ict his desire for unrestricted meat-eating. Such a religious system is condemned. Therefore K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 "Give up all other duties and surrender unto Me." That is the last word in religion.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 One may argue that the sacrifice of animals is recommended in the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vedas.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 This recommendation, however, is a restriction. Without Vedic restrictions on the purchase of meat, people will purchase meat from the market, which will be overflooded with meat shops, and slaughterhouses will increase. To restrict this, sometimes the }
{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vedas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  say that one may eat meat after sacrificing an insignificant animal like a goat before the goddess K\'e4l\'e9
. In any case, a system of religion in which animal sacrifices are recommended is inauspicious for those who perform the sacrifices and for the animals. Envious persons who perform ostentatious animal sacrifices are condemned in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (16.17) as follows:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e4tma-sambh\'e4vit\'e4\'f9 stabdh\'e4\line dhana-m\'e4na-mad\'e4nvit\'e4\'f9\line 
yajante n\'e4ma-yaj\'efais te\line dambhen\'e4vidhi-p\'fcrvakam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"Self-complacent and always impudent, deluded by wealth and false prestige, they sometimes perform sacrifices in name only without following any rules or regulations." Sometimes animal sacrifices are performed very gorgeously with grand arrangements
 for worshiping the goddess K\'e4l\'e9, but such festivals, although performed in the name of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yaj\'efa,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  are not actually }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yaj\'efa,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  for }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yaj\'efa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  means to satisfy the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore it is recommended that in this age specifically, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
yaj\'efai\'f9 sa\'eck\'e9rtana-pr\'e4yair yajanti hi sumedhasa\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  those who have good intelligence satisfy the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yaj\'efa-puru\'f1a,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Vi\'f1\'eb
u, by chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mantra.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Envious persons, however, are condemned by the Supreme Personality of Godhead as follows:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 aha\'eck\'e4ra\'e0 bala\'e0 darpa\'e0\line k\'e4ma\'e0 krodha\'e0 ca sa\'e0\'e7rit\'e4
\'f9\line m\'e4m \'e4tma-para-dehe\'f1u\line pradvi\'f1anto 'bhyas\'fcyak\'e4\'f9
\par t\'e4n aha\'e0 dvi\'f1ata\'f9 kr\'fcr\'e4n\line sa\'e0s\'e4re\'f1u nar\'e4dham\'e4n\line k\'f1ip\'e4my ajasram a\'e7ubh\'e4n\line \'e4sur\'e9\'f1v eva yoni\'f1u
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"Bewildered by false ego, strength, pride, lust and anger, the demon becomes envious of the Supreme P
ersonality of Godhead, who is situated in his own body and in the bodies of others, and blasphemes against the real religion. Those who are envious and mischievous, who are the lowest among men, are cast by Me into the ocean of material existence, into va
rious demoniac species of life." (Bg. 16.18-19) These persons are condemned by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, as indicated by the words }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tava kopa\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 A person who commits murder is envious of himself and also the person he has killed, for the result of c
ommitting murder is that he will be arrested and hanged. If one transgresses the laws of a man-made government, he may escape being killed by the state, but one cannot escape the laws of God. A killer of any animal must be killed in his next life by the s
ame animal. This is the law of nature. One must follow the instructions of the Supreme Lord: }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sarva-dharm\'e4n parityajya m\'e4m eka\'e0 \'e7ara\'eba\'e0 vraja.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 If one follows any other system of religion, he is subject to punishment by the Supreme Personality of Godhead in m
any different ways. Therefore if one follows a concocted system of religion, he is envious not only of others but also of himself. Consequently his system of religion is useless.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (1.2.8) says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma\'f9 svanu\'f1\'f6hita\'f9 pu\'e0s\'e4\'e0\line vi\'f1vaksena-kath\'e4su ya\'f9
\line notp\'e4dayed yadi rati\'e0\line \'e7rama eva hi kevalam
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 "Duties (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
) executed by men, regardless of occupation, are only so much useless labor if they do not provoke attraction for the message of the Supreme Lord." Following a system of religion that does not awaken one's K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a consciousness, or God consciousness, is merely a waste of time and labor.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.16.43
