tu}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash certainly; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 \'e4ry\'e4\'f9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash those who are advanced in civilization.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 My dear Lord, one's occupational duty is instructed in \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4
gavatam and Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4 according to Your point of view, which never deviates from the highest goal of life. Those who follow their occupational duties under You
r supervision, being equal to all living entities, moving and nonmoving, and not considering high and low, are called \'c4ryans. Such \'c4ryans worship You, the Supreme Personality of Godhead.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 k\'e5\'f1\'eba-kath\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  are identical. \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu wanted everyone to become a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 guru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 and preach the instructions of K\'e5\'f1\'eba everywhere from }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Pur\'e4\'ebas, Ved\'e4nta-s\'fctra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and similar Vedic literatures. \'c4ryans, who are advanced in civilization, follow }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja, although merely a child of five years, recommended:
\par }\pard\plain \s1434\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 kaum\'e4ra \'e4caret pr\'e4j\'efo\line dharm\'e4n bh\'e4gavat\'e4n iha\line durlabha
\'e0 m\'e4nu\'f1a\'e0 janma\line tad apy adhruvam arthadam\line }{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid1584610 (}{\cs2542\fs28\cf1\insrsid1651685\charrsid1651685 Bh\'e4g.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\i0\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid1584610 7.6.1)}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Prahl\'e4da Mah\'e4r\'e4ja preached }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma
}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  among his classmates as soon as an opportunity was afforded by the absence of his teachers from the classroom. He said that from the very beginning of life, from the age of five, children should be instructed about }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  because the human form of life, which is very rarely obtained, is meant for understanding this subject.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 means living according to the instructions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. In }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 we find that the Supreme Lord has arranged human society in four social divisions, namely }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba, k\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'fcdra.}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Again, the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Pur\'e4\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and other Vedic literatures set forth four }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e4\'e7ramas,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 which are the divisions of spiritual life. Therefore }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  means the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 var\'eb\'e4\'e7rama-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 of the four social and four spiritual divisions.
\par The members of human society who strictly follow the principles of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and live according to the instructions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead are called \'c4ryans or }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e4rya.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  A civilization of \'c4ryans who strictly follow the instructions of the L
ord and never deviate from those instructions is perfect. Such civilized men do not discriminate between trees, animals, human beings and other living entities. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Pa\'eb\'f2it\'e4\'f9 sama-dar\'e7ina\'f9:}{
\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 because they are completely educated in K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness, they see all living beings equally. \'c4
ryans do not kill even a small plant unnecessarily, not to speak of cutting trees for sense gratification. At the present moment, throughout the world, killing is prominent. Men are killing trees, they are killing animals, and th
ey are killing other human beings also, all for sense gratification. This is not an \'c4ryan civilization. As stated here, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sthira-cara-sattva-kadambe\'f1v ap\'e5thag-dhiya\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  The word }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ap\'e5thag-dhiya\'f9}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  indicates that \'c4ryans do not distinguish between lower and higher g
rades of life. All life should be protected. All living beings have a right to live, even the trees and plants. This is the basic principle of an \'c4
ryan civilization. Apart from the lower living entities, those who have come to the platform of human civilization should be divided into a society of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'ebas, k\'f1atriyas, vai\'e7yas}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'fcdras.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  The }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'ebas}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 should follow the instructions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead as stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and other Vedic literatures. The criterion must be }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  In other words, one should acquire the qualities of a }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 br\'e4hma\'eba, k
\'f1atriya, vai\'e7ya}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'fcdra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and act accordingly. This is the civilization accepted by the \'c4
ryans. Why do they accept it? They accept it because they are very much eager to satisfy K\'e5\'f1\'eba. This is perfect civilization.
\par \'c4ryans do not deviate from the instructions of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, nor do they have doubts about K\'e5\'f1\'eba, but non-\'c4ryans and other demoniac people fail to follow the instructions of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  This is because they have been trained in sense gratification at the cost of all other living entities. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 N\'fcna\'e0 pramatta\'f9 kurute vikarma:}{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 their only business is to indulge in all kinds of forbidden activities for sense gratification. }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Yad indriya-pr\'e9taya \'e4p\'e5\'eboti:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  they deviate in thi
s way because they want to gratify their senses. They have no other occupation or ambition. Their method of civilization is condemned in the previous verse. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Ka\'f9 k\'f1emo nija-parayo\'f9 kiy\'e4n v\'e4rtha\'f9
 sva-para-druh\'e4 dharme\'eba:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  "What is the meaning of a civilization that kills oneself and others?"
\par This verse, therefore, advises that everyone become a member of the \'c4ryan civilization and accept the instructions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. One should conduct his social, political and religious affairs accor
ding to His instructions. We are spreading the K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement to try to establish a society the way that K\'e5\'f1\'eba wants it. This is the meaning of K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness. We are therefore presenting }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  as it is and kicking out all kinds of mental concoction. Fools and rascals interpret }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 in their own way. When K\'e5\'f1\'eba says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 man-man\'e4 bhava mad-bhakto mad-y\'e4j\'e9 m\'e4\'e0 namaskuru}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \emdash 
"Always think of Me, become My devotee, worship Me and offer your homage unto Me"\emdash they comment that it is not K\'e5\'f1\'eba to whom we must surrender. Thus they derive imaginary meanings from }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t
\'e4.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  The K\'e5\'f1\'eba consciousness movement, however, strictly follows }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'e4gavata-dharma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  the instructions of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  for the complete welfare of human society. One who misinterprets }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  twisting out some meaning for his sense gratification, is a non-\'c4ryan. Therefore commentaries on }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
