both (namely, the form of sound and the form of spiritual identity); }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 \'e7\'e4\'e7vat\'e9}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash eternal; }{\cs1998\i\fs28\insrsid10252087 tan\'fc}{\fs28\insrsid10252087 \emdash two bodies.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 TRANSLATION
\par }\pard\plain \s1217\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sb36\sa65\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\f35\fs24\cf13\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 All living entities, moving and
 nonmoving, are My expansions and are separate from Me. I am the Supersoul of all living beings, who exist because I manifest them. I am the form of the transcendental vibrations like o\'e0k\'e4ra and Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba Hare R\'e4
ma, and I am the Supreme Absolute Truth. These two forms of Mine\emdash namely, the transcendental sound and the eternally blissful spiritual form of the Deity, are My eternal forms; they are not material.
\par }\pard\plain \s1187\qc \li0\ri0\sb240\sa120\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \b\v\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\v0\fs28\insrsid10252087 PURPORT
\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The science of devotional service has been instructed by N\'e4rada and A\'ecgir\'e4
 to Citraketu. Now, because of Citraketu's devotional service, he has seen the Supreme Personality of Godhead. By performing devotional service, one advances step by step, and when one is on the platform of love of Godhead (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 prem\'e4 pumartho mah\'e4n}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ) he sees the Supreme Lord at every moment. As stated in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 when one engages in devotional service twenty-four hours a day (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 te\'f1\'e4\'e0 satata-y}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4147046 ukt\'e4n\'e4\'e0 bhajat\'e4\'e0 pr\'e9ti-p\'fcrvakam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
) in accordance with the instructions of the spiritual master, his devotional service becomes more and more pleasing. Then the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who is within the core of everyone's heart, speaks to the devotee (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 dad\'e4mi buddhi-yoga\'e0 ta\'e0 yena m\'e4m upay\'e4nti te}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). Citraketu Mah\'e4r\'e4ja was first instructed by his }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 gurus,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  A\'ec
gir\'e4 and N\'e4rada, and now, having followed their instructions, he has come to the stage of seeing the Supreme Lord face to face. Therefore the Lord is now instructing him in the essence of knowledge.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The essence of knowledge is that there are two kinds of }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vastu,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  or substances, One is real, and the other, being illusory or temporary, is sometimes called nonfactual. One must consider these two kinds of existence. The real }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tattva,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  or truth, consists of Brahman, Param\'e4tm\'e4, and Bhagav\'e4n. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c7r\'e9mad-Bh\'e4gavatam}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (1.2.11):

\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vadanti tat tattva-vidas\line tattva\'e0 yaj j\'ef\'e4nam advayam\line brahmeti param
\'e4tmeti\line bhagav\'e4n iti \'e7abdyate
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"Learned transcendentalists who know the Absolute Truth call this nondual substance Brahman, Param\'e4tm\'e4 or Bhagav\'e4n." The Absolute Truth exists eternally in three features. Therefore, Brahman, Param\'e4tm\'e4 and Bhagav\'e4
n combined are the substance.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 The categories of emanations from the nonsubstance are two\emdash 
activities and forbidden activities (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vikarma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ). }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Karma}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  refers to the pious life or material activities performed during the day and the mental activities of dreams at night. These are more or less desired activities. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Vikarma,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  however, refers to illusory activities, which are something like the will-o'-the-wisp. These are activities that have no meaning. For example, modern sci
entists imagine that life can be produced from chemical combinations, and they are very busy trying to prove this in laboratories throughout the world, although no one in history has been able to produce the substance of life from material combinations. S
uch activities are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vikarma.
\par }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 All material activities are actually illusory, and progress in illusion is simply a waste of time. These illusory activities are called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ak\'e4rya,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 and one must learn of them from the instructions of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. As stated in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (4.17):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 karma\'ebo hy api boddhavya\'e0\line boddhavya\'e0 ca vikarma\'eba\'f9\line akarma\'eba
\'e7 ca boddhavya\'e0\line gahan\'e4 karma\'ebo gati\'f9
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"The intricacies of action are very hard to understand. Therefore one should know properly what action is, what for
bidden action is, and what inaction is." One must learn of these directly from the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who, as Anantadeva, is instructing King Citraketu because of the advanced stage of devotional service he achieved by following the instructi
ons of N\'e4rada and A\'ecgir\'e4.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Herein it is said, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 aha\'e0 vai sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  the Lord is everything (}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 ), including the living entities and the material or physical elements. As the Lord says in }{
\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (7.4-5):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'fcmir \'e4po 'nalo v\'e4yu\'f9\line kha\'e0 mano buddhir eva ca\line aha\'eck\'e4
ra it\'e9ya\'e0 me\line bhinn\'e4 prak\'e5tir a\'f1\'f6adh\'e4
\par apareyam itas tv any\'e4\'e0\line prak\'e5ti\'e0 viddhi me par\'e4m\line j\'e9va-bh\'fct\'e4\'e0 mah\'e4-b\'e4ho\line yayeda\'e0 dh\'e4ryate jagat
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 "Earth, water, fire, air, ether, mind, intelligence and false ego\emdash 
all together these eight comprise My separ
ated material energies. Besides this inferior nature, O mighty-armed Arjuna, there is a superior energy of Mine, which consists of the living entities, who are struggling with material nature and are sustaining the universe." The living entity tries to lo
rd it over the material or physical elements, but both the physical elements and the spiritual spark are energies emanating from the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore the Lord says, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 aha\'e0 vai sarva-bh\'fct
\'e4ni:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  "I am everything." Just as heat and light emanate from fire, these two energies\emdash the physical elements and the living entities\emdash emanate from the Supreme Lord. Therefore the Lord says, }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 aha\'e0 vai sarva-bh\'fct\'e4ni:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  "I expand the physical and spiritual categories."
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Again, the Lord, as the Supersoul, guides t
he living entities who are conditioned by the physical atmosphere. Therefore he is called }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'fct\'e4tm\'e4 bh\'fcta-bh\'e4vana\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 He gives the living entity the intelligence with which to improve his position so that he may return home, back to Godhead, or if he does not
 want to go back to Godhead, the Lord gives him the intelligence with which to improve his material position. This is confirmed by the Lord Himself in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (15.15). }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Sarvasya c\'e4ha\'e0 h\'e5di sannivi\'f1\'f6o matta\'f9 sm\'e5tir j\'ef\'e4nam apohana\'e0 ca:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  "I am seated in e
veryone's heart, and from Me come remembrance, knowledge and forgetfulness." From within, the Lord gives the living being the intelligence with which to work. Therefore the previous verse said that after the Supreme Personality of Godhead endeavors, our e
ndeavors begin. We cannot independently endeavor or act upon anything. Therefore the Lord is }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 bh\'fcta-bh\'e4vana\'f9.
\par }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Another specific feature of the knowledge given in this verse is that }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'e7abda-brahma}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  is also a form of the Supreme Lord. In His eternal, blissful form, Lord K
\'e5\'f1\'eba is accepted by Arjuna as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 para\'e0 brahma.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  A living entity in the conditioned stage accepts something illusory as substantial. This is called }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 m\'e4y\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  or }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 avidy\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \emdash ignorance. Therefore according to the Vedic knowledge, one must become a devotee, and one 
must then distinguish between }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 avidy\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vidy\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  which are elaborately explained in the }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \'c9\'e7opani\'f1ad.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  When one is actually on the platform of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vidy\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 he can personally understand the Personality of Godhead in His forms like those of Lord R\'e4ma, Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba and Sa\'eckar\'f1a\'eb
a. The Vedic knowledge is described as the breathing of the Supreme Lord, and activities begin on the basis of Vedic knowledge. Therefore the Lord says that when He endeavors or breathes, the material universes come into existence, and various acti
vities gradually develop. The Lord says in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pra\'ebava\'f9 sarva-vede\'f1u:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  "I am the syllable }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 o\'e0}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  in all the Vedic }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mantras.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 " Vedic knowledge begins with the vibration of the transcendental sound }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pra\'ebava, o\'e0k\'e4ra.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  The same transcendental sound is Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R\'e4
ma, Hare Hare. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Abhinnatv\'e4n n\'e4ma-n\'e4mino\'f9:}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  there is no difference between the holy name of the Lord and the Lord Himself.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.16.52
\par }\pard\plain \s1167\qc \li0\ri0\sb120\nowidctlpar\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10252087 \b\f35\fs24\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\insrsid10252087 TEXT 52
