\par }\pard\plain \s537\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 One should be very careful not to commit offenses at the lotus feet of Vai\'f1\'eb
avas, of whom Lord \'c7iva is the best. While instructing \'c7r\'e9la R\'fcpa Gosv\'e4m\'e9, \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu described an offense at the lotus feet of a Vai\'f1\'ebava as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 h\'e4t\'e9 m\'e4t\'e4,}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  a mad elephant. When a mad elephant enters a nice garden, it spoils the entire garden. Similarly, if one becomes like a mad elephant and commits offenses at the lotus feet of a Vai\'f1\'ebava, his entire spiri
tual career is halted. One should therefore be very careful not to commit offenses at the lotus feet of a Vai\'f1\'ebava.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Mother P\'e4rvat\'e9
 was justified in punishing Citraketu, for Citraketu impudently criticized the supreme father, Mah\'e4deva, who is the father of the living entities conditioned within this material world. The goddess Durg\'e4 is called mother, and Lord \'c7
iva is called father. A pure Vai\'f1\'ebava should be very careful to engage in his specific duty without criticizing others. This is the safest position. Otherwise, if one tends to criticize others, he may commit the great offense of criticizing a Vai
\'f1\'ebava.
\par Because Citraketu was undoubtedly a Vai\'f1\'ebava, he might have been surprised that P\'e4rvat\'e9 had cursed him. Therefore the goddess P\'e4rvat\'e9 addressed him as }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 putra,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 or son. Everyone is the son of mother Durg\'e4, but she is not an ordinary mother. As soon as there is a small discrepancy in a demon's behavior, mother Durg\'e4
 immediately punishes the demon so that he may come to his senses. This is explained by Lord K\'e5\'f1\'eba in }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (7.14):
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 daiv\'e9 hy e\'f1\'e4 gu\'eba-may\'e9\line mama m\'e4y\'e4 duratyay\'e4\line m\'e4
m eva ye prapadyante\line m\'e4y\'e4m et\'e4\'e0 taranti te
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"This divine energy of Mine, consisting of the three modes of material nature, is difficult to overcome. But those who have surrendered unto Me can easily cross beyond it." To surrender to K\'e5\'f1\'eb
a means to surrender to His devotees also, for no one can be a proper servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba unless he is a proper servant of a devotee. }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Ch\'e4\'f2iy\'e4 vai\'f1\'ebava-sev\'e4 nist\'e4ra p\'e4yeche keb\'e4:}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  without serving a servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba, one cannot be elevated to being a servant of K\'e5\'f1\'eba Himself. Therefore mother P\'e4rvat\'e9
 spoke to Citraketu exactly like a mother who says to her naughty child, "My dear child, I am punishing you so that you won't do anything like this again." This tendency of a mother to punish her child is found even in mother Ya\'e7od\'e4
, who became the mother of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Mother Ya\'e7od\'e4 punished K\'e5\'f1\'eba by binding Him and showing Him a stick. Thus it is the duty of a mother to chastise her beloved 
son, even in the case of the Supreme Lord. It is to be understood that mother Durg\'e4 was justified in punishing Citraketu. This punishment was a boon to Citraketu because after taking birth as the demon V\'e5tr\'e4sura, he was promoted directly to Vaiku
