The question may be raised why the living entities are situated in different conditions and who has arranged this. The answer is that it has been done by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, without anyone's help. The Lord has His own energies (}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 pa}{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid4332220 r\'e4sya \'e7aktir vividhaiva \'e7r\'fcyate}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
), and one of them, namely the external energy, creates the material world and the varieties of happiness and distress for the conditioned souls under the supervision of the Lord. The material world consists of three modes of material nature\emdash }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sattva-gu\'eba, rajo-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tamo-gu\'eba.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  }{\cs1998\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087\charrsid4332220 By}{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  sattva-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  the Lord maintains the material world, by }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 rajo-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  He creates it, and by }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tamo-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  He annihilates it. After the varieties of living entities are created, they are subject to happiness and distress according to their association. When they are in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sattva-gu\'eba,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  the mode of goodness, they feel happiness, when in }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 rajo-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  they are distressed, and when in }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 tamo-gu\'eba}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  they have no sense of what to do or what is right and wrong.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.17.22
