orld of duality are simply mental concoctions, for the so-called happiness and distress are actually one and the same. They are like the happiness and distress in dreams. A sleeping man creates his happiness and distress by dreaming, although actually the
y have no existence.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
The other example given in this verse is that a flower garland is originally very nice, but by mistake, for want of mature knowledge, one may consider it a snake. In this connection there is a statement by Prabodh\'e4nanda Sarasvat\'e9: }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vi\'e7va\'e0 p\'fcr\'eba-sukh\'e4yate.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  Everyone in this material world is distressed by miserable conditions, but \'c7r\'e9la Prabodh\'e4nanda Sarasvat\'e9
 says that this world is full of happiness. How is this possible? He answers, }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 yat-k\'e4ru\'ebya-kat\'e4k\'f1a-vaibhavavat\'e4\'e0 ta\'e0 gauram eva stuma\'f9.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
 A devotee accepts the distress of this material world as happiness only due to the causeless mercy of \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4prabhu. By His personal behavior, \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu showed that He was never distressed but always happy in chanting the Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mah\'e4-mantra.}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  One should follow in the footsteps of \'c7r\'e9 Caitanya Mah\'e4
prabhu and engage constantly in chanting the }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 mah\'e4-mantra}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 \emdash Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare K\'e5\'f1\'eba, K\'e5\'f1\'eba K\'e5\'f1\'eba, Hare Hare/ Hare R\'e4ma, Hare R\'e4ma, R\'e4ma R
\'e4ma, Hare Hare. Then he will never feel the distresses of the world of duality. In any condition of life one will be happy if he chants the holy name of the Lord.
\par In dreams we sometimes enjoy eating sweet rice and sometimes suffer as if one of our beloved family members had died. Because the same mind and b
ody exist in the same material world of duality when we are awake, the so-called happiness and distress of this world are no better than the false, superficial happiness of dreams. The mind is the via medium in both dreams and wakefulness, and everything 
created by the mind in terms of }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 sa\'eckalpa}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  and }{\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 vikalpa,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  acceptance and rejection, is called }{
\cs1998\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 manodharma,}{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  or mental concoction.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.17.31
