\'efeha n\'e4 bujhaya: }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 one should not be astonished to see the activities of exalted, liberated Vai\'f1\'eb
avas. As one should not be misled by the activities of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, one should also not be misled by the activities of His devotees. Both the L
ord and His devotees are liberated. They are on the same platform, the only difference being that the Lord is the master and the devotees are servants. Qualitatively, they are one and the same. In }{\cs2542\i\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 Bhagavad-g\'e9t\'e4}{
\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087  (9.29) the Lord says:
\par }\pard\plain \s1462\qc \li0\ri0\sb180\sa180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \i\f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 samo 'ha\'e0 sarva-bh\'fcte\'f1u\line na me dve\'f1yo 'sti na priya\'f9\line 
ye bhajanti tu m\'e4\'e0 bhakty\'e4\line mayi te te\'f1u c\'e4py aham
\par }\pard\plain \s135\qj \li0\ri0\sb89\sa89\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
"I envy no one, nor am I partial to anyone. I am equal to all. But whoever renders service unto Me in devotion is a friend, is in Me, and I am also a friend to him." From this s
tatement by the Supreme Personality of Godhead, it is clear that the devotees of the Lord are always extremely dear to Him. In effect, Lord \'c7iva told P\'e4rvat\'e9
, "Both Citraketu and I are always very dear to the Supreme Lord. In other words, both he and I are
 on the same level as servants of the Lord. We are always friends, and sometimes we enjoy joking words between us. When Citraketu loudly laughed at my behavior, he did so on friendly terms, and therefore there was no reason to curse him." Thus Lord \'c7
iva tried to convince his wife, P\'e4rvat\'e9, that her cursing of Citraketu was not very sensible.
\par }\pard\plain \s908\qj \fi369\li0\ri0\sa86\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \f35\fs24\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 
Here is a difference between male and female that exists even in the higher statuses of life}{\fs28\insrsid1849595 \emdash }{\fs28\cf1\insrsid10252087 in fact, even between Lord \'c7iva and his wife. Lord \'c7iva could understand Ci
traketu very nicely, but P\'e4rvat\'e9
 could not. Thus even in the higher statuses of life there is a difference between the understanding of a male and that of a female. It may be clearly said that the understanding of a woman is always inferior to the understa
nding of a man. In the Western countries there is now agitation to the effect that man and woman should be considered equal, but from this verse it appears that woman is always less intelligent than man.
\par It is clear that Citraketu wanted to criticize the behavior of his friend Lord \'c7iva because Lord \'c7iva was sitting with his wife on his lap. Then, too, Lord \'c7
iva wanted to criticize Citraketu for externally posing as a great devotee but being interested in enjoying with the Vidy\'e4dhar\'e9 women. These were all friendly jokes; there was nothing serious for which Citraketu should have been cursed by P\'e4rvat
\'e9. Upon hearing the instructions of Lord \'c7iva, P\'e4rvat\'e9 must have been very much ashamed for cursing Citraketu to become a demon. Mother P\'e4rvat\'e9 could not apprecia
te Citraketu's position, and therefore she cursed him, but when she understood the instructions of Lord \'c7iva she was ashamed.
\par }\pard\plain \s1467\qr \li0\ri0\sb180\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \v\f35\fs20\cf11\lang2057\langfe2057\cgrid\langnp2057\langfenp2057 {\insrsid10252087 SB 6.17.36
